lial cell of amnion\")\n19688:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23720296\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002538 \"An epithelial cell of the intrahepatic portion of the bile duct. These cells are flattened or cuboidal in shape, and have a small nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio relative to large/extrahepatic cholangiocytes.\")\n19889:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002560 \"An epithelial cell that resides in the inner root sheath of the hair follicle.\")\n19899:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002561 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the outer root sheath.\")\n19916:# Class: obo:CL_0002563 (intestinal epithelial cell)\n19918:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002563 \"An epithelial cell of the lining of the intestine.\")\n19921:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002563 \"intestinal epithelial cell\")\n19933:# Class: obo:CL_0002565 (iris pigment epithelial cell)\n19938:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002565 \"iris pigment epithelial cell\")\n20050:# Class: obo:CL_0002577 (placental epithelial cell)\n20052:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002577 \"An epithelial cell of the placenta.\")\n20055:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002577 \"placental epithelial cell\")\n20112:# Class: obo:CL_0002584 (renal cortical epithelial cell)\n20114:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002584 \"An epithelial cell of the kidney cortex.\")\n20116:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002584 \"renal cortical epithelial cell\")\n20130:# Class: obo:CL_0002586 (retinal pigment epithelial cell)\n20132:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002586 \"An epithelial cell of the retinal pigmented epithelium.\")\n20138:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002586 \"retinal pigment epithelial cell\")\n20461:# Class: obo:CL_0002621 (gingival epithelial cell)\n20465:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002621 \"gingival epithelial cell\")\n20480:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24646566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843887\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28623666\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34989394\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002623 \"An acinar cell that is part of the salivary gland epithelium, responsible for synthesizing and secreting the primary saliva essential for oral digestion, antimicrobial defense, and mucosal immunity. It features apical-basal polarity with apical secretory granules, and tight junctions that maintain polarity and regulate calcium-dependent saliva exocytosis triggered by parasympathetic and sympathetic signals (Ambudkar, 2015). This cell functions in coordination with contractile myoepithelial cells, which aid saliva flow through the ducts into the oral cavity (Khan et al., 2022). In mice and humans, acinar cell development relies on the transcription factor SOX2 (Emmerson et al., 2017), with self-renewal achieved primarily through acinar cell self-duplication and supported by progenitor populations during injury and regeneration (Aure et al., 2016).\")\n20502:# Class: obo:CL_0002625 (seminiferous tubule epithelial cell)\n20507:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002625 \"seminiferous tubule epithelial cell\")\n20557:# Class: obo:CL_0002631 (epithelial cell of upper respiratory tract)\n20561:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002631 \"epithelial cell of upper respiratory tract\")\n20564:# Class: obo:CL_0002632 (epithelial cell of lower respiratory tract)\n20568:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002632 \"epithelial cell of lower respiratory tract\")\n20581:# Class: obo:CL_0002634 (epithelial cell of anal column)\n20583:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002634 \"An epithelial cell of the anal column.\")\n20586:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002634 \"epithelial cell of anal column\")\n20590:# Class: obo:CL_0002635 (nonkeratinized epithelial cell of anal column)\n20592:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002635 \"A nonkeratinized epithelial cell of the anal canal.\")\n20596:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002635 \"nonkeratinized epithelial cell of anal column\")\n20599:# Class: obo:CL_0002636 (nonkeratinized epithelial cell of inferior part of anal canal)\n20605:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002636 \"nonkeratinized epithelial cell of inferior part of anal canal\")\n20609:# Class: obo:CL_0002637 (keratinized epithelial cell of the anal canal)\n20611:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002637 \"An epithelial cell of the anal canal that is keratinized. This cell type is found towards the lower, rectal end of the anal canal.\")\n20614:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002637 \"keratinized epithelial cell of the anal canal\")\n20626:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002638 \"basal epithelial cell of bronchioalveolar duct junction\")\n20650:# Class: obo:CL_0002641 (epithelial cell of esophageal gland proper)\n20652:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002641 \"An epithelial cell of the esophageal gland proper.\")\n20656:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002641 \"epithelial cell of esophageal gland proper\")\n20660:# Class: obo:CL_0002642 (epithelial cell of esophageal cardiac gland)\n20662:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://web.mac.com/wjkrause/iWeb/Histology/Blog/E3FA5916-1AA9-4885-B579-5051838D98CB.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002642 \"An ep