on(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1100001 \"An epithelial cell that is specialised for the synthesis and secretion of specific biomolecules.\")\n29092:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1100001 \"secretory epithelial cell\"@en)\n29707:# Class: obo:CL_2000064 (ovarian surface epithelial cell)\n29709:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12052228\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15749958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23467088\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31672973\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000064 \"A meso-epithelial cell of the ovarian surface epithelium, varying in shape from flat to cuboidal to pseudostratified columnar. This cell plays a crucial role in ovulation by producing proteolytic enzymes in response to gonadotropins, facilitating follicle rupture through tissue breakdown and TNF-alpha signaling. Additionally, this cell contributes to post-ovulatory wound repair (Morris et al., 2022) and exhibits stem cell-like properties (Flesken-Nikitin et al., 2013; Wang et al., 2019).\")\n29713:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000064 \"ovarian surface epithelial cell\")\n29903:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27091323\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28475124\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31734511\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000084 \"A goblet cell that is part of the conjunctival epithelium, characterized by apical accumulation of mucin granules (containing MUC5AC in humans; Muc5ac/Muc5b in mice). These gel-forming mucins support tear film stability, ocular lubrication, and pathogen defence. The conjunctival goblet cell forms tight junctions with neighbouring epithelial cells via species-specific claudins (claudin-10 in humans, claudin-2 in mice) and regulates immune homeostasis by facilitating soluble antigen transport to dendritic cells through goblet cell-associated antigen passages (GAPs) (Barbosa et al., 2017). The transcription factor SPDEF is essential for its differentiation.\")\n29993:# Class: obo:CL_2000094 (nasal cavity respiratory epithelium epithelial cell of viscerocranial mucosa)\n29995:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000094 \"Any epithelial cell of viscerocranial mucosa that is part of a nasal cavity respiratory epithelium.\")\n29999:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000094 \"nasal cavity respiratory epithelium epithelial cell of viscerocranial mucosa\")\n30034:# Class: obo:CL_3000000 (ciliated epithelial cell of esophagus)\n30036:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29802404\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_3000000 \"A ciliated epithelial cell of the esophagus.\")\n30040:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_3000000 \"ciliated epithelial cell of esophagus\")\n31522:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26778959\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9579598\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023181 \"A neurecto-epithelial cell that is part of the basal layer of the subcommissural organ and specializes in the secretion of proteins into the subarachnoid space. Hypendymal cells have similar characteristics to ependymal cells and express SCO-spondin.\")\n31588:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31233341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32059772\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32059779\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32091393\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33057196\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4028003 \"An alveolar capillary endothelial cell that is located proximally to alveolar capillary type 1 endothelial cells and in close apposition to alveolar type 1 epithelial cells (also known as type I pneumocytes).\")\n31708:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thymic_nurse_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030004 \"A large epithelial cell found in the thymus. This cell type may internalize thymocytes through extensions of plasma membrane. The cell surface and cytoplasmic vacuoles of a thymic nurse cell express MHC Class I and MHC Class II antigens. The interaction of these antigens with a developing thymocyte determines whether the thymocyte undergoes positive or negative selection.\")\n31723:# Class: obo:CL_4030006 (fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell)\n31725:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\n31728:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"oviduct secretory epithelial cell\")\n31729:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"uterine tube secretory epithelial cell\")\n31730:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\n31731:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030006 \"fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell\")\n31736:# Class: obo:CL_4030007 (fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell)\n31738:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\n31744:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"uterine tube ciliated epithelial cell\")\n31745:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell\")\n31752:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10322630\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030008 \"A specialized epithelial cell that contains \\\"feet\\\" that interdigitate with the \\\"feet\\\" of other glomerular epithelial cells in the pronephros.\")\n31755:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFA:0001673\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030008 \"pronephric glomerular visceral epithelial cell\")\n31760:# Class: obo:CL_4030009 (epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 1)\n31764:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030009 \"epithelial cell of segment 1 of proximal tubule\")\n31765:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030009 \"epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 1\")\n31769:# Class: obo:CL_4030010 (epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 2)\n31773:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030010 \"epithelial cell of segment 2 of proximal tubule\")\n31774:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030010 \"epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 2\")\n31778:# Class: obo:CL_4030011 (epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 3)\n31782:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030011 \"epithelial cell of segment 3 of proximal tubule\")\n31783:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31249312\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030011 \"The epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 3 operates under relatively hypoxic conditions and is particularly susceptible to ischemic injury.\")\n31784:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030011 \"epithelial cell of proximal tubule segment 3\")\n31788:# Class: obo:CL_4030012 (kidney loop of Henle short descending thin limb epithelial cell)\n31790:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33769951\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030012 \"Epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the short loop (cortical) nephron limited to the outer medulla (mainly inner strip). It is known in some mammalian species that the short descending limb of the loop of Henle selectively expresses the serine protease Corin, the homeobox TF Uncx, and the urea channel Slc14a2.\")\n31793:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030012 \"epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the short loop of Henle\")\n31794:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030012 \"kidney loop of Henle short descending thin limb epithelial cell\")\n31799:# Class: obo:CL_4030013 (kidney loop of Henle long descending thin limb outer medulla epithelial cell)\n31801:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33769951\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030013 \"Epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the long loop (juxtamedullary) nephron that spans the outer medulla (inner stripe). It is known in some mammalian species that the long descending limb of the loop of Henle in the outer medulla selectively expresses the secreted activin-antagonist protein follistatin (Fst), the GPI-linked adhesion protein Cdh13, and the protein kinase Stk32a.\")\n31803:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030013 \"epithelial cell of the outer medulla of the long descending limb of the loop of Henle\")\n31804:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030013 \"kidney loop of Henle long descending thin limb outer medulla epithelial cell\")\n31808:# Class: obo:CL_4030014 (kidney loop of Henle long descending thin limb inner medulla epithelial cell)\n31810:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33769951\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/8170\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030014 \"Epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the long loop (juxtamedullary) nephron that spans the inner medulla. It is known in some mammalian species that the long descending limb of the loop of Henle in the inner medulla selectively expresses the nuclear receptor Nr2e3, the Ig kappa chain Igkc, and the secreted protein dermokine (Dmkn). SLC14A2, which expresses a urea transporter, is also expressed in the inner medulla.\")\n31812:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030014 \"epithelial cell of the inner medulla of the long descending limb of the loop of Henle\")\n31813:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030014 \"kidney loop of Henle long descending thin limb inner medulla epithelial cell\")\n31826:# Class: obo:CL_4030016 (epithelial cell of early distal convoluted tubule)\n31828:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24855283\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030016 \"An epithelial cell located in the early distal convoluted tubule.\")\n31831:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030016 \"epithelial cell of early distal convoluted tubule\")\n31834:# Class: obo:CL_4030017 (epithelial cell of late distal convoluted tubule)\n31836:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24855283\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030017 \"An epithelial cell located in the late distal convoluted tubule.\")\n31840:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030017 \"epithelial cell of late distal convoluted tubule\")\n31888:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-9578>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30069044\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32726565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33442032\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030023 \"A hillock cell that is located in respiratory epithelium. In some mammalian species, this cell type has been noted to express KRT13 and KRT4 and is postulated to play a role in squamous barrier function and immunomodulation.\")\n31897:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30069044\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030024 \"An epithelial, transitional cell type between basal and secretory; located in stratified, non-ciliated structures (called hillocks) with high cell turnover in epithelium. In some mammalian species, this cell type has been noted to express KRT13 and is postulated to play a role in squamous barrier function and immunomodulation.\")\n31983:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18757316\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21364219\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34044844\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37834236\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030034 \"A multiciliated epithelial cell located in the respiratory tract epithelium, characterized by a columnar shape and motile cilia on its apical surface. This cell develops through a highly orchestrated process, transitioning from a basal progenitor via an intermediate deuterosomal cell stage that generates centrioles essential for ciliogenesis.\")\n32047:# Class: obo:CL_4030040 (endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell)\n32054:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030040 \"endometrial ciliated epithelial cell\")\n32055:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030040 \"endometrium ciliated epithelial cell\")\n32057:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030040 \"endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell\")\n32060:# Class: obo:CL_4030041 (luminal endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell)\n32064:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030041 \"luminal endometrial ciliated epithelial cell\")\n32065:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030041 \"luminal endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell\")\n32069:# Class: obo:CL_4030042 (glandular endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell)\n32073:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030042 \"glandular endometrial ciliated epithelial cell\")\n32074:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030042 \"glandular endometrial multiciliated epithelial cell\")\n32320:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17133361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24183650\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9374839\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030066 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a ureteric bud. A ureteric bud cell has the potential to induce metanephric mesenchymal cells to proliferate and convert to epithelia that form renal tubules via: (1) the secretion of multiple diffusible growth factors that rescue renal progenitors from apoptosis and stimulate them to proliferate and (2) contact-dependent mechanisms that induce mesenchymal-epithelial conversion.\")\n32353:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30566875\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32497356\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4032000 \"An epithelial cell of the urethra that has an expression profile similar to lung club cells. Club-like cells of the urethra epithelium are similar to lung club cells in their expression of SCGB1A1 and in their enrichment of immunomodulatory programs.\")\n32354:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:CL_4032000 \"The term \\\"club-like\\\" is used to disambiguate from club cells which CL defines as a type of bronchial epithelial cell. This seems to reflect common usage of club cell when used without location (club cell seems to mean bronchial club cell, unless it is proceded or preceded by something that says it is not bronchial). In the literature, the name \\\"club-like\\\" isn't used.\")\n32395:# Class: obo:CL_4033003 (myoepithelial cell of bronchus submucosal gland)\n32397:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19996346\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5487122\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033003 \"A(n) myoepithelial cell that is part of a(n) bronchus submucosal gland.\")\n32399:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033003 \"myoepithelial cell of bronchus submucosal gland\")\n32470:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22375063\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35883599\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9520465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/single+cell+type/squamous+epithelial+cells#suprabasalkeratinocytes\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033013 \"A keratinocyte that resides in the epidermal suprabasal layer and expresses differentiation markers, including keratin 1 and keratin 10, in both humans and mice. In human interfollicular epidermis, this cell retains proliferative capacity and possesses retrodifferentiation potential, acquiring basal-like properties during wound healing or basement membrane contact.\")\n32479:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2210508\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30023181\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033014 \"A small, narrow, peg-shaped epithelial cell with little cytoplasm that is part of oviduct epithelium. This cell is rarer than the ciliated and secretory epithelial cells of the fallopian tube epithelium and is often found intercalated between them. Peg cells are generally distributed basally along the epithelium and have been found in high concentrations at the fimbriated, distal end of the fallopian tube in humans. It may have a regenerative/stem-cell function. In humans, markers include EPCAM, CD44, and ITGA6.\")\n32560:# Class: obo:CL_4033021 (myoepithelial cell of trachea gland)\n32562:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29656943\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033021 \"A myoepithelial cell that is part of a submucosal gland of the trachea.\")\n32566:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033021 \"myoepithelial cell of trachea gland\")\n32579:# Class: obo:CL_4033023 (airway submucosal gland collecting duct epithelial cell)\n32581:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25648514\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29656943\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033023 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a collecting duct of an airway submucosal gland.\")\n32585:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033023 \"airway submucosal gland collecting duct epithelial cell\")\n32798:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31558434\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:331922198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36883528\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37291214\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033044 \"An epithelial cell part of respiratory tract epithelium that is a precursor of a multi-ciliated cell. This cell actively amplifies centrioles, a required step for multiciliogenesis.\")\n32843:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25564622\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34044844\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35387001\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37834236\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033048 \"A respiratory epithelial cell derived from a basal cell, with a topographic nuclear position between the basal and luminal cells of the airway epithelium. This non-basal, intermediate progenitor cell has limited proliferative capacity and can differentiate into multiciliated, secretory, or rare airway cells (ionocytes, tuft cells, neuroendocrine cells). It shares some ultrastructural features with basal cells but lacks the defined characteristics of fully differentiated cellular phenotypes.\")\n32921:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17707699\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30864819\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033055 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell located in ciliated duct of an airway submucosal gland, characterized by a columnar shape and motile cilia on its apical surface.\")\n32940:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033057 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that can proliferate and has the potential to differentiate into a lactocyte during pregnancy. In humans, a luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell can be identified by high levels of the markers EpCAM and CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of CD14, Kit, CD61, and Tspan8.\")\n32961:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34156490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033058 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that transduces endocrine cues to orchestrate proliferation, architectural remodeling, and differentiation of other cells in the mammary gland via paracrine signaling. This cell expresses high levels of estrogen receptors. In humans, a luminal hormone-sensing cell can be identified by high levels of EpCAM and low levels of CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of Foxa1, CD133, and Sca1 (Ly6a).\")\n32966:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"hormone-sensing mammary epithelial cell\")\n33078:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27815559\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33970370\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34198768\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033067 \"A follicular cell of ovary that differentiates from a cuboidal granulosa cell during the secondary follicle stage. Mural granulosa cells line the inner surface of the follicle wall, surrounding the fluid-filled antral cavity. These cells produce oestrogen during the follicular phase in response to follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH), and progesterone after ovulation in response to luteinizing hormone (LH).\")\n33090:# Class: obo:CL_4033083 (squamous granulosa cell)\n33092:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28892263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033083 \"A granulosa cell that has a squamous morphology and form a single layer around the oocyte in primordial follicles. This cell develops directly into a cuboidal granulosa cell during the primordial-to-primary follicle transition.\")\n33097:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033083 \"squamous GC\")\n33098:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033083 \"Often in literature squamous granulosa cell and pre-granulosa cell are used as synonyms. However, this term only makes reference to the quiescent granulosa cells that surround the primordial ovarian follicle, while a pre-granulosa cell proliferates to form the primordial follicle (and thus cells become the squamous granulosa cells).\")\n33099:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033083 \"squamous granulosa cell\")\n33105:# Class: obo:CL_4033084 (cuboidal granulosa cell)\n33107:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28892263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033084 \"A granulosa cell that has a cuboidal morphology and develops from squamous granulosa cell during the transition between primordial follicle to primary follicle. Cuboidal granulosa cells proliferate to form a second layer within secondary follicles.\")\n33111:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31849844\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal epithelial granulosa cell\")\n33113:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal GC\")\n33114:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal granulosa cell\")\n33205:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20614614\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29105366\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36983561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37768272\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033093 \"A stem cell that is part of the corneo-scleral limbus. This cell type resides at the basal layer of the epithelium and has a small size and high nuclear to cytoplasmatic ratio (Secker and Daniels, 2009). A limbal stem cell is responsible for corneal epithelial renewal and repair (Li et al., 2023), and to help maintain a clear corneal surface by preventing conjunctival epithelial cells from migrating onto the cornea (Wang et al., 2023).\")\n33318:# Class: obo:CL_4040003 (fetal pre-type II pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell)\n33323:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9624168\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4040003 \"fetal alveolar pre-type II epithelial cell\")\n33325:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12114192\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4040003 \"fetal pre-type II alveolar epithelial cell\")\n33327:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4040003 \"According to PMID:1316350 this cell type does not yet produce surfactant. According to PMID:9109447 and PMID:12114192 this cell type produces low levels of surfactant that can be increased by administration of very low-density lipoproteins. This cell type is of medical relevance, as a central feature of the fetal respiratory distress syndrome seems to be the presence in the lung of abundant pre-type II alveolar epithelial cells (PMID:1316350).\")\n33328:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4040003 \"fetal pre-type II pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell\")\n33609:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12429182\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354325\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042021 \"In vitro cultures of embryonic mouse neural tubes show that neuronal-restricted precursors (NRPs) are derived from multipotent neuroepithelial cells to give rise to neurons. This progression suggests a linear relationship between multipotent progenitors and neuronal-restricted differentiation. (Mayer-Proschel et al., 1997). In the spinal cord of rats, neural-restricted precursor cells give rise cholinergic, GABAergic, glutametergic neurons (Cao and Howard et al., 2002).\")\n34201:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31756561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32531023\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35913117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38260422\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1038/s41467-021-27901-5\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the crypt of Lieberkuhn, originating from intestinal stem cells and giving rise to enteroendocrine cells (EECs). In mouse and human, this cell can be characterized by the expression of Neurog3, and has the ability to proliferate and differentiate into multiple EEC subtypes. Its proliferative potential contributes to crypt growth, distinguishing it from fully differentiated EECs.\")\n34338:# Class: obo:CL_4052018 (fallopian tube epithelial cell)\n34340:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052018 \"Any epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube.\")\n34343:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052018 \"oviduct epithelial cell\")\n34344:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052018 \"uterine tube epithelial cell\")\n34345:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052018 \"fallopian tube epithelial cell\")\n34348:# Class: obo:CL_4052019 (fallopian tube non-ciliated epithelial cell)\n34350:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052019 \"Any epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube and lacks cilia.\")\n34354:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052019 \"fallopian tube non-ciliated epithelial cell\")\n34394:# Class: obo:CL_4052023 (luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell)\n34396:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32929266\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36581776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38559249\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052023 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the endometrial luminal epithelium, forming a continuous layer lining the uterine cavity. This cell undergoes cyclical changes during the menstrual cycle, proliferating under estrogen in the proliferative phase, and differentiating under progesterone in the secretory phase to prepare for potential implantation. During the window of implantation, this cell changes from a tall columnar shape to a shorter columnar or cuboidal form, loses polarity, and becomes receptive to blastocyst implantation.\")\n34399:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052023 \"The luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell expresses WNT7A, and LGR5 during the proliferative phase, transitioning to express VTCN1 and SULT1E1 in the early secretory phase, and LEFTY1, IL6, and PTGS1 in the mid- to late-secretory phases.\")\n34400:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052023 \"luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell\")\n34483:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35355013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36796082\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052031 \"A secretory epithelial cell of the respiratory and terminal bronchioles.\")\n34488:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35355013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36796082\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052031 \"The respiratory airway secretory cell is cuboidal and has a unique transcriptomic profile compared to other epithelial cells in the same region. In humans, it functions as a multipotent progenitor, capable of regenerating alveolar type 2 (AT2) cells.\")\n34517:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30022164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30904566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35668088\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36351364\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36961668\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052034 \"A tuft cell that is part of the medullary epithelium of the thymus, characterized by lateral microvilli and specific markers, including L1CAM in both mice (Zhang et al., 2022) and humans (Sun et al., 2023), as well as MHC II in mice (Miller et al., 2018). This cell is pivotal in immune functions such as antigen presentation, central tolerance, and type 2 immunity. A tuft cell in the thymus exhibits characteristics of both a medullary thymic epithelial cell (mTEC) and a peripheral tuft cell. Its development is governed by transcription factors such as POU2F3.\")\n34521:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30904566\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052034 \"A thymic tuft cell is a subset of terminally differentiated medullary thymic epithelial cell comprising 5-10% of total mTECs. Lineage-tracing studies indicate that this cell arises from mature MHCII mTECs, with development occurring through both Aire-dependent and Aire-independent pathways. However, its exact origins remain unclear.\")\n34563:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30379593\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34932383\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38306414\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052038 \"A tuft cell that is part of the nasal cavity respiratory epithelium. Acting as a chemosensor, it detects bitter taste ligands and bacterial signals via taste receptors, maintaining epithelial-microbial homeostasis by stimulating antimicrobial peptide secretion from adjacent epithelial cells. This cell is a major source of IL-25, promoting type 2 immune responses and potentially contributing to chronic rhinosinusitis (O'Leary et al., 2019).\")\n34644:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30855909\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35799078\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37724716\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052048 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell that is part of the intercalated duct of salivary gland. This cell expresses proteins commonly associated with acinar cells and displays calcium signaling characteristics similar to secretory cells, indicating an active role in the secretory process rather than ion reabsorption.\")\n34658:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30855909\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34147989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052049 \"An columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell that is part of the striated duct of salivary gland, characterized by basal striations formed by infoldings of the plasma membrane. This cell play a crucial role in modifying the electrolyte composition and concentration of saliva through active ion transport, particularly the absorption of sodium and secretion of potassium.\")\n34671:# Class: obo:CL_4052050 (luminal epithelial cell of endometrium)\n34673:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36273006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052050 \"An epithelial cell that is part of an endometrium luminal epithelium.\")\n34676:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31317179\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052050 \"endometrial luminal epithelial cell\")\n34677:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052050 \"luminal epithelial cell of endometrium\")\n34807:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29383862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36726292\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052067 \"An acinar cell of the salivary gland, with a hybrid seromucous phenotype, co-expressing serous and mucous markers and producing a mixed secretion of enzymes-containing serous fluid and mucins essential for lubrication, digestion, and antimicrobial defense. Predominant in the submandibular glands of humans and mice, its differentiation and secretory gene expression are regulated by FGFR2b–MAPK signaling, driven by paracrine FGF7 from adjacent myoepithelial cells, which provides a key niche signal for seromucous identity.\")\n34816:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28192873\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31194408\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1007/978-3-030-35784-9_2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.5772/intechopen.75538\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052069 \"A duct epithelial cell that is part of the excretory duct of the salivary gland, which transports saliva from the intralobular ductal system to the oral cavity. While primarily serving as a conduit, this cell may play a role in the saliva modification, contributing to its hypotonicity. In humans, this cell has a pseudostratified columnar shape.\")\n34826:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40475517\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052070 \"A bipotent progenitor cell within the human fallopian tube epithelium, characterized by the concurrent expression of epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers at both the cell surface and transcript levels. This cell has the capacity to differentiate into ciliated and secretory epithelial cells, as well as potentially endothelial/stromal lineages. Positioned at the apex of lineage bifurcation, the cell exhibits stem-like and endothelial features, representing an intermediate developmental state between undifferentiated progenitors and lineage-committed epithelial cells.\")\n34830:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35320732\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4052070 \"non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells)\")\n34831:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35320732\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4052070 \"non-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells)\")\n35495:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17020902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837987\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32187560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32726565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37672481\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770004 \"An epithelial cell that resides in the layer(s) immediately above the basal layer in stratified or pseudostratified epithelia. This cell mainly originates from basal cells and is found across various tissues, including skin, esophagus, oral mucosa, airway, and cornea.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
