ncreased weight of an organism.\n--\n825-\n826-[Term]\n827:id: PATO:0000129\n828-name: obsolete absolute weight\n829-is_obsolete: true\n830-\n831-[Term]\n832:id: PATO:0000130\n833-name: obsolete relative weight\n834-is_obsolete: true\n835-\n836-[Term]\n837:id: PATO:0000131\n838-name: obsolete relative size\n839-is_obsolete: true\n840-\n841-[Term]\n842:id: PATO:0000133\n843-name: orientation\n844-alt_id: PATO:0000137\n845-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's placement which is defined by the angle between the bearer and an axis, or the angle between the bearer and another object.\" [PATOC:JE]\n--\n854-\n855-[Term]\n856:id: PATO:0000134\n857-name: obsolete absolute_angle\n858-is_obsolete: true\n859-\n860-[Term]\n861:id: PATO:0000135\n862-name: obsolete relative_angle\n863-is_obsolete: true\n864-\n865-[Term]\n866:id: PATO:0000136\n867-name: closure\n868-def: \"A morphological quality pertaining to the degree to which an object contains an opening, aperture, orifice or vent.\" [PATOC:CJM, PATOC:GVG]\n869-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n871-\n872-[Term]\n873:id: PATO:0000138\n874-name: obsolete absolute orientation\n875-is_obsolete: true\n876-\n877-[Term]\n878:id: PATO:0000139\n879-name: obsolete relative orientation\n880-is_obsolete: true\n881-\n882-[Term]\n883:id: PATO:0000140\n884-name: position\n885-alt_id: PATO:0001032\n886-alt_id: PATO:0001631\n--\n893-\n894-[Term]\n895:id: PATO:0000141\n896-name: structure\n897-alt_id: PATO:0001452\n898-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's relative position, shape, arrangements and connectivity of an organism's various parts; the pattern underlying its form.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n903-\n904-[Term]\n905:id: PATO:0000142\n906-name: obsolete substance\n907-is_obsolete: true\n908-\n909-[Term]\n910:id: PATO:0000143\n911-name: obsolete addictive substance\n912-is_obsolete: true\n913-\n914-[Term]\n915:id: PATO:0000144\n916-name: obsolete solid substance\n917-comment: This t