y virtue of the bearer's having a horizontal surface without a slope, tilt, or curvature.\" [web:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/]\n2482-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2487-\n2488-[Term]\n2489:id: PATO:0000409\n2490-name: oblate\n2491-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting an equatorial diameter greater than its polar diameter.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n2492-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2497-\n2498-[Term]\n2499:id: PATO:0000410\n2500-name: pinnate\n2501-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having leaflets or leaflets-like structures on each side of a common axis.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n2502-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2508-\n2509-[Term]\n2510:id: PATO:0000411\n2511-name: circular\n2512-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being such that every part of the surface or the circumference is equidistant from the center.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n2513-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2519-\n2520-[Term]\n2521:id: PATO:0000413\n2522-name: square\n2523-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an equal-sided rectangular form.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n2524-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2527-\n2528-[Term]\n2529:id: PATO:0000414\n2530-name: unbranched\n2531-def: \"A branchiness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking branches.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n2532-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2537-\n2538-[Term]\n2539:id: PATO:0000415\n2540-name: uncoiled\n2541-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being not curled or wound (especially in concentric rings or spirals).\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n2542-subset: cell_quality\n--\n2547-\n2548-[Term]\n2549:id: PATO:0000416\n2550-name: obsolete count value\n2551-is_obsolete: true\n2552-\n2553-[Term]\n2554:id: PATO:0000417\n2555-name: obsolete absolute number value\n2556-is_obsolete: true\n2557-\n2558-[Term]\n2559:id: PATO:0000418\n2560-name: obsolete relative number