et: value_slim\n--\n3780-\n3781-[Term]\n3782:id: PATO:0000609\n3783-name: closure incomplete\n3784-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's affording not completed blocked passage or view.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3785-subset: value_slim\n--\n3787-\n3788-[Term]\n3789:id: PATO:0000610\n3790-name: open\n3791-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's affording unobstructed passage or view.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n3792-subset: value_slim\n--\n3795-\n3796-[Term]\n3797:id: PATO:0000611\n3798-name: obsolete absolute orientation value\n3799-is_obsolete: true\n3800-\n3801-[Term]\n3802:id: PATO:0000612\n3803-name: obsolete relative orientation value\n3804-is_obsolete: true\n3805-\n3806-[Term]\n3807:id: PATO:0000613\n3808-name: disoriented\n3809-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking orientation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3810-subset: value_slim\n--\n3813-\n3814-[Term]\n3815:id: PATO:0000614\n3816-name: oriented\n3817-def: \"A pattern where all the repeated elements are oriented in the same direction.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n3818-subset: value_slim\n--\n3821-\n3822-[Term]\n3823:id: PATO:0000615\n3824-name: wholly anteriorized\n3825-def: \"An anteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally anterior structures.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3826-subset: value_slim\n--\n3831-\n3832-[Term]\n3833:id: PATO:0000616\n3834-name: asymmetrical\n3835-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking symmetry.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3836-subset: cell_quality\n--\n3842-\n3843-[Term]\n3844:id: PATO:0000617\n3845-name: bent\n3846-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one or more angle(s) in its length.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n3847-subset: value_slim\n--\n3851-\n3852-[Term]\n3853:id: PATO:0000618\n3854-name: bilateral\n3855-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two sides; two-sided.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n3856-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n3859-\n3860-[Term]\n3861:id: PATO:0000619\n3862-name: crowded\n3863-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being overfilled.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n3864-subset: value_slim\n--\n3867-\n3868-[Term]\n3869:id: PATO:0000620\n3870-name: wholly dorsalized\n3871-def: \"A dorsalized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally dorsal structures.\" [PATOC:melissa]\n3872-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n3876-\n3877-[Term]\n3878:id: PATO:0000622\n3879-name: erect\n3880-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being upright in position or posture.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n3881-subset: value_slim\n--\n3884-\n3885-[Term]\n3886:id: PATO:0000623\n3887-name: exserted\n3888-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's protruding or projecting from the body.\" [sdvc:sdvc]\n3889-subset: value_slim\n--\n3893-\n3894-[Term]\n3895:id: PATO:0000624\n3896-name: inserted into\n3897-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's becoming joined together with an additional entity.\" [PATOC:nw]\n3898-subset: relational_slim\n--\n3903-\n3904-[Term]\n3905:id: PATO:0000625\n3906-name: inverted\n3907-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being reversed in position, order, or condition.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3908-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n3913-\n3914-[Term]\n3915:id: PATO:0000626\n3916-name: lateralized\n3917-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being moved or displaced to one side so as to make lateral.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n3918-subset: value_slim\n--\n3920-\n3921-[Term]\n3922:id: PATO:0000627\n3923-name: localized\n3924-def: \"A spatial pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being confined or restricted to a particular location.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n3925-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n3931-\n3932-[Term]\n3933:id: PATO:0000628\n3934-name: mislocalised\n3935-alt_id: PATO:0000621\n3936-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's being changed in abnormal position.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n3942-\n3943-[Term]\n3944:id: PATO:0000629\n3945-name: misrouted\n3946-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having mistakenly taken course, way, or passage; ill-routed.\" [NDI:NDI]\n3947-subset: value_slim\n--\n3949-\n3950-[Term]\n3951:id: PATO:0000630\n3952-name: wholly posteriorized\n3953-def: \"A posteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally posterior structures.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3954-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n3960-\n3961-[Term]\n3962:id: PATO:0000631\n3963-name: prostrate\n3964-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being stretched out and lying at full length along the ground.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n3965-subset: value_slim\n--\n3967-\n3968-[Term]\n3969:id: PATO:0000632\n3970-name: symmetrical\n3971-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being capable of division by a longitudinal plane into similar halves.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3972-comment: similar pattern in both halves\n--\n3979-\n3980-[Term]\n3981:id: PATO:0000633\n3982-name: uncrowded\n3983-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being not overfilled.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n3984-subset: value_slim\n--\n3987-\n3988-[Term]\n3989:id: PATO:0000634\n3990-name: unilateral\n3991-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's involvement of only one part or side.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n3992-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n3995-\n3996-[Term]\n3997:id: PATO:0000635\n3998-name: unlocalised\n3999-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not being confined or restricted to a particular location.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n4000-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4003-\n4004-[Term]\n4005:id: PATO:0000636\n4006-name: wholly ventralized\n4007-def: \"A ventralized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally ventral structures.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n4008-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4012-\n4013-[Term]\n4014:id: PATO:0000637\n4015-name: obsolete structure value\n4016-is_obsolete: true\n4017-\n4018-[Term]\n4019:id: PATO:0000638\n4020-name: apoptotic\n4021-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of blebbing of the nucleus and DNA fragmentation due to the cell undergoing a specific form of programmed cell death termed apoptosis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n4022-subset: value_slim\n--\n4025-\n4026-[Term]\n4027:id: PATO:0000639\n4028-name: degenerate\n4029-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer whose structure deteriorates or is lost over time due to an active pathological process.\" [PATOC:mb, PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n4030-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4038-\n4039-[Term]\n4040:id: PATO:0000640\n4041-name: dysplastic\n4042-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting an alteration in size, shape or organization of its constituent cells.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n4043-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4047-\n4048-[Term]\n4049:id: PATO:0000641\n4050-name: obsolete deposition defective\n4051-is_obsolete: true\n4052-\n4053-[Term]\n4054:id: PATO:0000642\n4055-name: fused with\n4056-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being merged with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n4057-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4067-\n4068-[Term]\n4069:id: PATO:0000643\n4070-name: herniated\n4071-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bodily structure that has protruded through an abnormal opening in the wall that contains it.\" [spinalstenosis:spinalstenosis]\n4072-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4075-\n4076-[Term]\n4077:id: PATO:0000644\n4078-name: hyperplastic\n4079-alt_id: PATO:0000943\n4080-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an organ or tissue by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting an increased number of cells, typically associated with an increase in size.\" [Wikipedia:Hyperplasia]\n--\n4087-\n4088-[Term]\n4089:id: PATO:0000645\n4090-name: hypoplastic\n4091-alt_id: PATO:0000942\n4092-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an organ or tissue by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a decreased number of cells, typically associated with a decrease in size.\" [PATOC:GVG, Wikipedia:Hypoplasia]\n--\n4100-\n4101-[Term]\n4102:id: PATO:0000646\n4103-name: malformed\n4104-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being distorted during formation.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n4105-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4109-\n4110-[Term]\n4111:id: PATO:0000647\n4112-name: necrotic\n4113-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's undergoing unprogrammed cell death.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necrotic]\n4114-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4117-\n4118-[Term]\n4119:id: PATO:0000648\n4120-name: obstructed\n4121-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being blocked or filled with obstacles or an obstacle.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n4122-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n4125-\n4126-[Term]\n4127:id: PATO:0000651\n4128-name: unfused from\n4129-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being no longer merged with another entity.\" [PATOC:nw]\n4130-subset: relational_slim\n--\n4135-\n4136-[Term]\n4137:id: PATO:0000652\n4138-name: obsolete substance value\n4139-is_obsolete: true\n4140-\n4141-[Term]\n4142:id: PATO:0000653\n4143-name: obsolete addictive substance value\n4144-is_obsolete: true\n4145-\n4146-[Term]\n4147:id: PATO:0000654\n4148-name: obsolete alcochol value\n4149-is_obsolete: true\n4150-\n4151-[Term]\n4152:id: PATO:0000655\n4153-name: obsolete amphetamine value\n4154-is_obsolete: true