osed to its length or width.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n5582-comment: Thickness often refers to the smallest 1-D extent compared to the other two orthogonal dimensions, however, this is not always true. See https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/337 for full discussion.\n--\n5587-\n5588-[Term]\n5589:id: PATO:0000916\n5590-name: obsolete absolute thickness\n5591-is_obsolete: true\n5592-\n5593-[Term]\n5594:id: PATO:0000917\n5595-name: obsolete relative thickness\n5596-is_obsolete: true\n5597-\n5598-[Term]\n5599:id: PATO:0000918\n5600-name: volume\n5601-def: \"A 3-D extent quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's amount of 3-dimensional space it occupies.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n5602-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n5606-\n5607-[Term]\n5608:id: PATO:0000919\n5609-name: obsolete absolute volume\n5610-is_obsolete: true\n5611-\n5612-[Term]\n5613:id: PATO:0000920\n5614-name: obsolete relative volume\n5615-is_obsolete: true\n5616-\n5617-[Term]\n5618:id: PATO:0000921\n5619-name: width\n5620-def: \"A 1-D extent quality which is equal to the distance from one side of an object to another side which is opposite.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n5621-comment: Width often refers to the dimension that is greater than the extent in only one of the other two orthogonal dimensions, however, this is not always true. See https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/337 for full discussion.\n--\n5627-\n5628-[Term]\n5629:id: PATO:0000922\n5630-name: obsolete absolute width\n5631-is_obsolete: true\n5632-\n5633-[Term]\n5634:id: PATO:0000923\n5635-name: obsolete relative width\n5636-is_obsolete: true\n5637-\n5638-[Term]\n5639:id: PATO:0000924\n5640-name: obsolete relative enzyme function\n5641-is_obsolete: true\n5642-\n5643-[Term]\n5644:id: PATO:0000925\n5645-name: obsolete absolute enzyme function\n5646-is_obsolete: true\n5647-\n5648-[Term]\n5649:id: PATO:0000926\n5650-name: obsolete intercross fertility\n5651-is_obsolete: true\n5652-\n5653-[Term]\n5654:id: PATO:0000927\n5655-name: photosensitivity\n5656-de