:0001278\n7864-name: desaturated orange\n7865-def: \"A color consisting of orange hue and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7866-subset: value_slim\n--\n7869-\n7870-[Term]\n7871:id: PATO:0001280\n7872-name: dark pale pink\n7873-alt_id: PATO:0001279\n7874-def: \"Pink color having medium brightness and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n7879-\n7880-[Term]\n7881:id: PATO:0001281\n7882-name: saturated purple\n7883-def: \"A color consisting of purple color and high saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7884-subset: value_slim\n--\n7887-\n7888-[Term]\n7889:id: PATO:0001282\n7890-name: desaturated purple\n7891-def: \"A color consisting of purple color and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7892-subset: value_slim\n--\n7895-\n7896-[Term]\n7897:id: PATO:0001283\n7898-name: saturated red\n7899-def: \"A color consisting of red hue and high saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7900-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n7904-\n7905-[Term]\n7906:id: PATO:0001284\n7907-name: desaturated red\n7908-def: \"A color consisting of red hue and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7909-subset: value_slim\n--\n7912-\n7913-[Term]\n7914:id: PATO:0001285\n7915-name: saturated yellow\n7916-def: \"A color consisting of yellow hue and high saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7917-subset: value_slim\n--\n7920-\n7921-[Term]\n7922:id: PATO:0001286\n7923-name: desaturated yellow\n7924-def: \"A color consisting of yellow hue and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7925-subset: value_slim\n--\n7928-\n7929-[Term]\n7930:id: PATO:0001287\n7931-name: red brown\n7932-def: \"A color consisting of red and brown hue.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7933-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n7936-\n7937-[Term]\n7938:id: PATO:0001288\n7939-name: dark red brown\n7940-def: \"A color consisting of red and brown hue and low brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7941-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n7944-\n7945-[Term]\n7946:id: PATO:0001289\n7947-name: light red brown\n7948-def: \"A color consisting of red and brown hue and high brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7949-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n7952-\n7953-[Term]\n7954:id: PATO:0001290\n7955-name: fluorescent\n7956-def: \"A fluorescence quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of emitting light during exposure to radiation from an external source.\" [web:www.thefreedictionary.com/]\n7957-subset: value_slim\n--\n7959-\n7960-[Term]\n7961:id: PATO:0001291\n7962-name: obsolete electromagnetic (EM) radiation quality\n7963-def: \"OBSOLETE A radiation quality that inheres in a bearer by virtue of how that bearer interacts with electromagnetic radiation.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromagnetic_radiation]\n7964-comment: See https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/490\n--\n7967-\n7968-[Term]\n7969:id: PATO:0001292\n7970-name: full-spectrum EM radiation quality\n7971-def: \"An EM radiation quality that is independent of the EM wavelength range.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7972-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n7974-\n7975-[Term]\n7976:id: PATO:0001293\n7977-name: absorption quality\n7978-def: \"A scalar EM radiation quality which obtains by the capacity of the bearer to retain radiation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7979-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n7981-\n7982-[Term]\n7983:id: PATO:0001294\n7984-name: radiation reflective quality\n7985-def: \"A scalar EM radiation quality which obtains by the capacity of the bearer to scatter or reflect radiation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n7986-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n7988-\n7989-[Term]\n7990:id: PATO:0001295\n7991-name: albedo\n7992-def: \"A reflective quality restricted to a particular wavelength.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n7993-comment: Typically used for light, but also applied to full EM spectrum.\n--\n7996-\n7997-[Term]\n7998:id: PATO:0001296\n7999-name: luminous flux\n8000-def: \"A scalar optical quality which obtains by the magnitude of the light emitted by the bearer.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8001-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8003-\n8004-[Term]\n8005:id: PATO:0001297\n8006-name: reflectivity\n8007-def: \"A radiation reflective quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the ratio of the energy of a wave reflected from its surface to the energy possessed by the wave striking the bearer's surface.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8008-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8010-\n8011-[Term]\n8012:id: PATO:0001298\n8013-name: phosphorescence\n8014-def: \"A fluorescence in which the emittence continues after the absorption has ceased.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8015-subset: relational_slim\n--\n8017-\n8018-[Term]\n8019:id: PATO:0001299\n8020-name: radiation emitting quality\n8021-def: \"A scalar EM radiation quality which obtains by the capacity of the bearer to emit radiation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8022-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8024-\n8025-[Term]\n8026:id: PATO:0001300\n8027-name: optical quality\n8028-def: \"An EM radiation quality in which the EM radiation is within the fiat range of the spectrum visible deemed to be light.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8029-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8031-\n8032-[Term]\n8033:id: PATO:0001301\n8034-name: chromatic property\n8035-def: \"An optical quality that is the mixture, purity or pattern of wavelengths of light perceived by the observer.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n8036-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8038-\n8039-[Term]\n8040:id: PATO:0001302\n8041-name: vermilion\n8042-def: \"A color consisting of red and orange hue with a slight amount of gray.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8043-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n8046-\n8047-[Term]\n8048:id: PATO:0001303\n8049-name: variability\n8050-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to varying or changing.\" [Dictionary:http\\://dictionary.reference.com/]\n8051-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8054-\n8055-[Term]\n8056:id: PATO:0001304\n8057-name: variability of temperature\n8058-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits temperature variation or change.\" [PATO:GVG]\n8059-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8062-\n8063-[Term]\n8064:id: PATO:0001305\n8065-name: increased temperature\n8066-alt_id: PATO:0000678\n8067-def: \"A temperature which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n8074-\n8075-[Term]\n8076:id: PATO:0001306\n8077-name: decreased temperature\n8078-alt_id: PATO:0000677\n8079-def: \"A temperature which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n8086-\n8087-[Term]\n8088:id: PATO:0001307\n8089-name: decreased variability of temperature\n8090-def: \"A variability of temperature which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8091-subset: value_slim\n--\n8096-\n8097-[Term]\n8098:id: PATO:0001308\n8099-name: increased variability of temperature\n8100-def: \"A variability of temperature which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8101-subset: value_slim\n--\n8106-\n8107-[Term]\n8108:id: PATO:0001309\n8109-name: duration\n8110-alt_id: PATO:0000081\n8111-def: \"A process quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's magnitude of the temporal extent between the starting and ending point.\" [PATOC:mellybelly]\n--\n8117-\n8118-[Term]\n8119:id: PATO:0001310\n8120-name: duration of temperature\n8121-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's duration of exhibition of thermal energy.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8122-comment: TODO: obsolete? I don't know what this means.\n--\n8125-\n8126-[Term]\n8127:id: PATO:0001311\n8128-name: decreased duration of temperature\n8129-def: \"A duration of temperature which is lesser relative to the normal or average enduring or continuing in time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8130-subset: value_slim\n--\n8134-\n8135-[Term]\n8136:id: PATO:0001312\n8137-name: increased duration of temperature\n8138-def: \"A duration of temperature which is greater relative to the normal or average in respect to the quality of temperature of enduring or continuing in time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8139-subset: value_slim\n--\n8144-\n8145-[Term]\n8146:id: PATO:0001313\n8147-name: invariant temperature\n8148-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking or not exhibiting variation of temperature.\" [PATO:GVG]\n8149-subset: relational_slim\n--\n8152-\n8153-[Term]\n8154:id: PATO:0001314\n8155-name: variant temperature\n8156-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or exhibiting variation of temperature.\" [PATO:GVG]\n8157-subset: value_slim\n--\n8160-\n8161-[Term]\n8162:id: PATO:0001315\n8163-name: mild increased temperature\n8164-def: \"A temperature which is increased by a low degree.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8165-subset: value_slim\n--\n8167-\n8168-[Term]\n8169:id: PATO:0001316\n8170-name: moderate increased temperature\n8171-def: \"A temperature which is increased by a medium degree.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8172-subset: value_slim\n--\n8174-\n8175-[Term]\n8176:id: PATO:0001317\n8177-name: severe increased temperature\n8178-def: \"A temperature which is increased by a high degree.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8179-subset: value_slim\n--\n8181-\n8182-[Term]\n8183:id: PATO:0001318\n8184-name: indiscriminate\n8185-def: \"A discrimination quality in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being incapable perceiving differences between two or more stimuli.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8186-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n8192-\n8193-[Term]\n8194:id: PATO:0001319\n8195-name: discriminate\n8196-def: \"A discrimination quality in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being capable of perceiving differences between two or more stimuli.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8197-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n8202-\n8203-[Term]\n8204:id: PATO:0001320\n8205-name: pubescent hair\n8206-def: \"A pilosity quality of being covered with short hairs or soft down.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8207-subset: value_slim\n--\n8209-\n8210-[Term]\n8211:id: PATO:0001321\n8212-name: right angle to\n8213-def: \"An angle which is 90 degrees to another entity.\" [thesaurus.math:thesaurus.math]\n8214-subset: relational_slim\n--\n8217-\n8218-[Term]\n8219:id: PATO:0001322\n8220-name: straight angle to\n8221-def: \"An angle which is 180 degrees to another entity.\" [thesaurus.maths:thesaurus.maths]\n8222-comment: TODO: decide on correct parentage.\n--\n8226-\n8227-[Term]\n8228:id: PATO:0001323\n8229-name: area\n8230-def: \"A 2-D extent quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's two dimensional extent.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area]\n8231-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8235-\n8236-[Term]\n8237:id: PATO:0001324\n8238-name: bilateral symmetry\n8239-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being symmetric about a plane running from its frontal end to its caudal end (head to tail), and has nearly identical right and left halves.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilateral_symmetry]\n8240-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8245-\n8246-[Term]\n8247:id: PATO:0001325\n8248-name: radial symmetry\n8249-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having equal proportion around a central point or axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8250-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8254-\n8255-[Term]\n8256:id: PATO:0001326\n8257-name: obsolete left-right symmetry\n8258-subset: value_slim\n8259-is_obsolete: true\n8260-\n8261-[Term]\n8262:id: PATO:0001327\n8263-name: zygomorphic\n8264-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being capable of division into symmetrical halves by only one longitudinal plane passing through the axis.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n8265-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8268-\n8269-[Term]\n8270:id: PATO:0001328\n8271-name: actinomorphic\n8272-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being capable of division into symmetrical halves by any longitudinal plane passing through the axis.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n8273-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8276-\n8277-[Term]\n8278:id: PATO:0001329\n8279-name: flavourful\n8280-def: \"A flavor quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having flavour.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8281-subset: relational_slim\n--\n8285-\n8286-[Term]\n8287:id: PATO:0001330\n8288-name: flavourless\n8289-def: \"A flavor quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking flavour.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8290-subset: relational_slim\n--\n8293-\n8294-[Term]\n8295:id: PATO:0001331\n8296-name: odorous\n8297-def: \"An odor quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having odour.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8298-subset: value_slim\n--\n8300-\n8301-[Term]\n8302:id: PATO:0001332\n8303-name: amorphous\n8304-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lack of distinct morphology.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8305-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8309-\n8310-[Term]\n8311:id: PATO:0001333\n8312-name: temporally extended\n8313-def: \"A quality of a process which ends later than the natural end time.\" [PATOC:melissa]\n8314-subset: value_slim\n--\n8317-\n8318-[Term]\n8319:id: PATO:0001334\n8320-name: diameter\n8321-def: \"A length quality which is equal to the length of any straight line segment that passes through the center of a circle and whose endpoints are on the circular boundary.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diameter]\n8322-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8326-\n8327-[Term]\n8328:id: PATO:0001335\n8329-name: bacterial mating type\n8330-def: \"A mating type that indicates whether the F plasmid has integrated into the chromosome.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8331-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8333-\n8334-[Term]\n8335:id: PATO:0001336\n8336-name: obsolete unknown sex\n8337-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual whose sex is unknown.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8338-comment: Unknown is not a type of sex.\n--\n8341-\n8342-[Term]\n8343:id: PATO:0001337\n8344-name: yeast mating type\n8345-def: \"A yeast mating type.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8346-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8348-\n8349-[Term]\n8350:id: PATO:0001338\n8351-name: mixed sex\n8352-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in a population of multiple sexes.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8353-comment: For example a mixture of females and male or males and hermaphrodites.\n--\n8356-\n8357-[Term]\n8358:id: PATO:0001339\n8359-name: biomaterial purity\n8360-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's homogeneity of a biomaterial.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8361-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8364-\n8365-[Term]\n8366:id: PATO:0001340\n8367-name: hermaphrodite\n8368-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an organism or a population with both male and female sexual organs in one individual.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8369-subset: value_slim\n--\n8373-\n8374-[Term]\n8375:id: PATO:0001341\n8376-name: a mating type (yeast)\n8377-def: \"A S. cerevisiae mating type cells that secrete a pheromone that in alpha haploids stimulates processes that lead to mating.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8378-subset: value_slim\n--\n8381-\n8382-[Term]\n8383:id: PATO:0001342\n8384-name: Saccharomyces cerevisiae mating type\n8385-def: \"A S. cerevisiae mating type.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8386-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8388-\n8389-[Term]\n8390:id: PATO:0001343\n8391-name: Schizosaccharomyces pombe mating type\n8392-def: \"A S. pombe mating type determined by the gene configuration on the mat1 locus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8393-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8395-\n8396-[Term]\n8397:id: PATO:0001344\n8398-name: alpha mating type (yeast)\n8399-def: \"A S. cerevisiae mating type cells that secrete a pheromone that stimulates a haploids.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8400-subset: value_slim\n--\n8403-\n8404-[Term]\n8405:id: PATO:0001345\n8406-name: h minus\n8407-def: \"A S. pombe mating type determined by the mat1-Mc and mat1-Mi on the mat1 locus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8408-subset: value_slim\n--\n8412-\n8413-[Term]\n8414:id: PATO:0001346\n8415-name: h plus\n8416-def: \"A S. pombe mating type determined by the mat1-Pc and mat1-Pi on the mat1 locus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8417-subset: value_slim\n--\n8421-\n8422-[Term]\n8423:id: PATO:0001347\n8424-name: F mating type\n8425-def: \"A bacterial mating type indicating the presence of F plasmid in a bacterial cell.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8426-subset: value_slim\n--\n8428-\n8429-[Term]\n8430:id: PATO:0001348\n8431-name: F minus mating type\n8432-def: \"A bacterial mating type indicating the absence of F plasmid in a bacterial cell.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8433-subset: value_slim\n--\n8436-\n8437-[Term]\n8438:id: PATO:0001349\n8439-name: high frequency recombinant\n8440-def: \"A mating type that indicates that the F plasmid has integrated into the chromosome.\" [MGED:MGED]\n8441-subset: value_slim\n--\n8444-\n8445-[Term]\n8446:id: PATO:0001350\n8447-name: angular acceleration\n8448-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the rate of change of the bearer's angular velocity.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angular_acceleration]\n8449-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8452-\n8453-[Term]\n8454:id: PATO:0001351\n8455-name: area density\n8456-def: \"A density quality which inheres in a bearer by virtue of some influence exerted by the bearer's mass on a given area.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area_density]\n8457-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8460-\n8461-[Term]\n8462:id: PATO:0001352\n8463-name: linear density\n8464-def: \"A density quality which is equal to the mass exerting an influence on a one-dimensional object.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_density]\n8465-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8468-\n8469-[Term]\n8470:id: PATO:0001353\n8471-name: volumetric density\n8472-def: \"A density quality which inheres in a bearer by virtue of some influence exerted by the bearer's mass on a given volume.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_density]\n8473-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8476-\n8477-[Term]\n8478:id: PATO:0001354\n8479-name: translucent\n8480-def: \"A optical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting low opacity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8481-subset: value_slim\n--\n8483-\n8484-[Term]\n8485:id: PATO:0001355\n8486-name: convex\n8487-def: \"A shape quality that obtains by virtue of the bearer having inward facing edges; having a surface or boundary that curves or bulges outward, as the exterior of a sphere.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8488-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8492-\n8493-[Term]\n8494:id: PATO:0001356\n8495-name: pleomorphic\n8496-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a cell by virtue of the bearer's ability to take on two or more different shapes during its life cycle.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8497-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8502-\n8503-[Term]\n8504:id: PATO:0001357\n8505-name: pulvinate\n8506-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a cushion or has a marked convex cushion-like form.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8507-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n8510-\n8511-[Term]\n8512:id: PATO:0001358\n8513-name: umbonate\n8514-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a knob or knoblike protuberance.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8515-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8518-\n8519-[Term]\n8520:id: PATO:0001359\n8521-name: rugose\n8522-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having many wrinkles or creases on the surface.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8523-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8527-\n8528-[Term]\n8529:id: PATO:0001360\n8530-name: filamentous\n8531-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having thin filamentous extensions at its edge.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8532-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8535-\n8536-[Term]\n8537:id: PATO:0001361\n8538-name: warty\n8539-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being covered with warts or projections that resemble warts resulting in a hard rough surface.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8540-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n8543-\n8544-[Term]\n8545:id: PATO:0001362\n8546-name: fragile\n8547-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being easily damaged or destroyed.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n8548-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n8553-\n8554-[Term]\n8555:id: PATO:0001364\n8556-name: rhizoidal\n8557-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having root like extensions radiating from its center.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8558-subset: value_slim\n--\n8560-\n8561-[Term]\n8562:id: PATO:0001365\n8563-name: spiny\n8564-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having spines, thorns or similar thin projections on its surface.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8565-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8568-\n8569-[Term]\n8570:id: PATO:0001366\n8571-name: punctiform\n8572-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being small and resembling a point.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8573-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8577-\n8578-[Term]\n8579:id: PATO:0001367\n8580-name: lobate\n8581-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having deeply undulating edges forming lobes.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8582-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8586-\n8587-[Term]\n8588:id: PATO:0001368\n8589-name: erose\n8590-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an irregularly toothed edge.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8591-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8595-\n8596-[Term]\n8597:id: PATO:0001369\n8598-name: raised\n8599-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a colony by virtue of the bearer's appearing above the medium surface with terraced edges.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8600-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n8603-\n8604-[Term]\n8605:id: PATO:0001370\n8606-name: viscid\n8607-def: \"A coating quality which is sticky or clammy.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8608-subset: value_slim\n--\n8610-\n8611-[Term]\n8612:id: PATO:0001371\n8613-name: mucoid\n8614-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's consistency of mucus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8615-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n8620-\n8621-[Term]\n8622:id: PATO:0001372\n8623-name: refractivity\n8624-def: \"A physical quality that inheres in propagating wave (light or sound) virtue of the bearer's change in direction when passing from one medium to another.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n8625-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8628-\n8629-[Term]\n8630:id: PATO:0001373\n8631-name: glistening\n8632-def: \"A reflectivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's reflecting lots of light.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8633-subset: value_slim\n--\n8637-\n8638-[Term]\n8639:id: PATO:0001374\n8640-name: ploidy\n8641-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's number of homologous sets of chromosomes in the nucleus or primary chromosome-containing compartment of the cell, each set essentially coding for all the biological traits of the organism.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ploidy]\n8642-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8644-\n8645-[Term]\n8646:id: PATO:0001375\n8647-name: haploid\n8648-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing a single set of homologous chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haploid]\n8649-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8652-\n8653-[Term]\n8654:id: PATO:0001376\n8655-name: monoploid\n8656-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing a single set of unique homologous chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monoploid]\n8657-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8660-\n8661-[Term]\n8662:id: PATO:0001377\n8663-name: polyploid\n8664-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing more than two homologous sets of chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyploid]\n8665-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8668-\n8669-[Term]\n8670:id: PATO:0001378\n8671-name: autopolyploid\n8672-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing chromosomes derived from a single species.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autopolyploid]\n8673-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8676-\n8677-[Term]\n8678:id: PATO:0001379\n8679-name: allopolyploidy\n8680-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing chromosomes derived from different species.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allopolyploidy]\n8681-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8684-\n8685-[Term]\n8686:id: PATO:0001380\n8687-name: paleopolyploid\n8688-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an ancient polyploid ancestor.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paleopolyploid]\n8689-subset: value_slim\n--\n8691-\n8692-[Term]\n8693:id: PATO:0001381\n8694-name: triploid\n8695-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing three homologous sets of chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triploid]\n8696-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8699-\n8700-[Term]\n8701:id: PATO:0001382\n8702-name: tetraploid\n8703-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing four homologous sets of chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetraploid]\n8704-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8707-\n8708-[Term]\n8709:id: PATO:0001383\n8710-name: pentaploid\n8711-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing five homologous sets of chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pentaploid]\n8712-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8715-\n8716-[Term]\n8717:id: PATO:0001384\n8718-name: hexaploid\n8719-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing six homologous sets of chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hexaploid]\n8720-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8723-\n8724-[Term]\n8725:id: PATO:0001385\n8726-name: aneuploid\n8727-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing a non-integral multiple of the monoploid number, due to extra or missing chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aneuploid]\n8728-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8731-\n8732-[Term]\n8733:id: PATO:0001386\n8734-name: monosomy\n8735-def: \"An aneuploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing only one chromosome from a pair in a cell's nucleus.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monosomy]\n8736-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8739-\n8740-[Term]\n8741:id: PATO:0001387\n8742-name: disomy\n8743-def: \"An aneuploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing only two chromosome from a pair in a cell's nucleus.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disomy]\n8744-comment: For diploid organisms, such as humans, it is the normal condition, whilst for organisms that are normally triploid or above, disomy is an aneuploidy.\n--\n8748-\n8749-[Term]\n8750:id: PATO:0001388\n8751-name: uniparental disomy\n8752-def: \"A disomy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing two copies of the chromosome from one of the parents (with no contribution from the other parent).\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniparental_disomy]\n8753-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8756-\n8757-[Term]\n8758:id: PATO:0001389\n8759-name: trisomy\n8760-def: \"An aneuploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing three, instead of two, chromosomes of a particular numbered type in an organism.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trisomy]\n8761-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8764-\n8765-[Term]\n8766:id: PATO:0001390\n8767-name: partial trisomy\n8768-def: \"A trisomy quality inhering in a bearer when part of the bearer's extra chromosome is attached to one of the other chromosomes, or if one of the bearer's chromosomes has two copies of part of its chromosome.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partial_trisomy]\n8769-subset: value_slim\n--\n8771-\n8772-[Term]\n8773:id: PATO:0001391\n8774-name: mosaic trisomy\n8775-def: \"A trisomy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having extra chromosomal material in only some of it's cells.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8776-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8779-\n8780-[Term]\n8781:id: PATO:0001392\n8782-name: endopolyploid\n8783-def: \"A polyploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's chromosome number being increased by endomitosis and for which the degree of ploidy is proportional to the number of times that endomitosis has taken place.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endopolyploid]\n8784-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8787-\n8788-[Term]\n8789:id: PATO:0001393\n8790-name: euploid\n8791-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing an integral multiple of the monoploid number, possibly excluding the sex-determining chromosomes.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euploid]\n8792-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8795-\n8796-[Term]\n8797:id: PATO:0001394\n8798-name: diploid\n8799-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two copies (homologs) of each chromosome, usually one from the mother and one from the father.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diploid]\n8800-comment: The exact number may be one or two different from the 2n number and still be classified as diploidy (although with aneuploidy). Nearly all mammals are diploid organisms, although all individuals have some small fraction of cells that are polyploidy.\n--\n8804-\n8805-[Term]\n8806:id: PATO:0001395\n8807-name: haplodiploid\n8808-def: \"A diploidy quality inhering in a bearer in by virtue of belonging in a species whose one of the sexes has haploid cells and the other has diploid cells.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haplodiploid]\n8809-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8812-\n8813-[Term]\n8814:id: PATO:0001396\n8815-name: cellular quality\n8816-def: \"A monadic quality of continuant that exists at the cellular level of organisation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8817-is_a: PATO:0070044 ! anatomical structure quality\n8818-\n8819-[Term]\n8820:id: PATO:0001397\n8821-name: cellular potency\n8822-def: \"A cellular quality that arises by virtue of whether the bearer's disposition to differentiate into one or more mature cell types.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8823-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8826-\n8827-[Term]\n8828:id: PATO:0001398\n8829-name: self-renewal\n8830-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having the ability to go through numerous cycles of cell division while maintaining the undifferentiated state.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8831-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8834-\n8835-[Term]\n8836:id: PATO:0001399\n8837-name: totipotent\n8838-def: \"A cellular potency that is the capacity to produce differentiated cell types of all three primary germ layers and extraembryonic cell types.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Totipotent]\n8839-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8843-\n8844-[Term]\n8845:id: PATO:0001400\n8846-name: unipotent\n8847-def: \"A cellular potency that is the capacity to produce only one differentiated cell type.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unipotent]\n8848-comment: Unipotent cells have the quality of self-renewal which distinguishes them from non-stem cells.\n--\n8853-\n8854-[Term]\n8855:id: PATO:0001401\n8856-name: oligopotent\n8857-def: \"A cellular potency that is the capacity to form multiple differentiated cell types of a specific lineage and lack self renewing capacity.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n8858-comment: Less potent than multipotent, often thought of as precursor or progenitor cell status.\n--\n8863-\n8864-[Term]\n8865:id: PATO:0001402\n8866-name: multipotent\n8867-def: \"A cellular potency that is the capacity to form multiple differentiated cell types.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multipotent]\n8868-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8872-\n8873-[Term]\n8874:id: PATO:0001403\n8875-name: pluripotent\n8876-def: \"A cellular potency that is the capacity to produce differentiated cell types of all three primary germ layers but not extraembryonic cell types.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluripotent]\n8877-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8881-\n8882-[Term]\n8883:id: PATO:0001404\n8884-name: nucleate quality\n8885-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's number of nuclei.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8886-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8888-\n8889-[Term]\n8890:id: PATO:0001405\n8891-name: anucleate\n8892-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having no nucleus.\" [Biology-online:Biology-online]\n8893-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8897-\n8898-[Term]\n8899:id: PATO:0001406\n8900-name: binucleate\n8901-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two nuclei.\" [Biology-online:Biology-online]\n8902-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8906-\n8907-[Term]\n8908:id: PATO:0001407\n8909-name: mononucleate\n8910-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one nucleus.\" [Biology-online:Biology-online]\n8911-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8915-\n8916-[Term]\n8917:id: PATO:0001408\n8918-name: ciliated\n8919-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one or more cilia as a part.\" [PMID:36924208, wikipedia:Cilium]\n8920-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8923-\n8924-[Term]\n8925:id: PATO:0001409\n8926-name: spindle-shaped\n8927-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a long tapered rod.\" [Biology-online:Biology-online]\n8928-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8932-\n8933-[Term]\n8934:id: PATO:0001410\n8935-name: striated\n8936-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by narrow lines or grooves, usually parallel.\" [Biology-online:Biology-online]\n8937-subset: cell_quality\n--\n8941-\n8942-[Term]\n8943:id: PATO:0001411\n8944-name: structured\n8945-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having distinct structure.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8946-subset: value_slim\n--\n8949-\n8950-[Term]\n8951:id: PATO:0001412\n8952-name: unstructured\n8953-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking distinct structure.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8954-subset: value_slim\n--\n8957-\n8958-[Term]\n8959:id: PATO:0001413\n8960-name: angular velocity\n8961-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the rate of the bearer's angular movement about an axis; the angle rotated in a given time.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angular_velocity]\n8962-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8965-\n8966-[Term]\n8967:id: PATO:0001414\n8968-name: catalytic activity\n8969-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a catalyst by virtue of the amount of the catalyst's action.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8970-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8973-\n8974-[Term]\n8975:id: PATO:0001415\n8976-name: morbidity\n8977-def: \"A quality inhering in a population by virtue of the proportion of its members that are ill at a given time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8978-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n8981-\n8982-[Term]\n8983:id: PATO:0001416\n8984-name: regular duration\n8985-def: \"A duration which has regular start and/or end times.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n8986-subset: value_slim\n--\n8989-\n8990-[Term]\n8991:id: PATO:0001417\n8992-name: irregular duration\n8993-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's duration which has irregular start and/or end times.\" [PATOC:melissa]\n8994-subset: value_slim\n--\n8997-\n8998-[Term]\n8999:id: PATO:0001418\n9000-name: lethargic\n9001-def: \"A behavioral quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being deficient in alertness or activity.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9002-subset: value_slim\n--\n9004-\n9005-[Term]\n9006:id: PATO:0001419\n9007-name: sharp\n9008-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's terminating in a point or edge.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9009-subset: cell_quality\n--\n9012-\n9013-[Term]\n9014:id: PATO:0001420\n9015-name: buoyancy\n9016-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to rise or float in a fluid medium such as water or air.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9017-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9021-\n9022-[Term]\n9023:id: PATO:0001421\n9024-name: alive\n9025-def: \"A viability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's condition before death.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9026-subset: value_slim\n--\n9028-\n9029-[Term]\n9030:id: PATO:0001422\n9031-name: dead\n9032-def: \"A viability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the cessation of the bearer's life.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9033-subset: value_slim\n--\n9035-\n9036-[Term]\n9037:id: PATO:0001423\n9038-name: refractile\n9039-def: \"A reflectivity quality inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to refract light.\" [biology-online:biology-online]\n9040-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9043-\n9044-[Term]\n9045:id: PATO:0001424\n9046-name: violet\n9047-def: \"A color hue with very low wavelength of that portion of the visible spectrum lying between reddish blue or bluish purple, evoked in the human observer by radiant energy with wavelengths of approximately 420 to 380 nanometers.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet]\n9048-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9051-\n9052-[Term]\n9053:id: PATO:0001425\n9054-name: rosy\n9055-def: \"A color hue consisting of red hue and yellow hue and high brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9056-subset: value_slim\n--\n9058-\n9059-[Term]\n9060:id: PATO:0001426\n9061-name: maroon\n9062-def: \"A color consisting of purple and brown hue.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maroon]\n9063-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9066-\n9067-[Term]\n9068:id: PATO:0001427\n9069-name: compound acidity\n9070-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in compound by virtue of the bearer's tendency to act as a hydron donor.\" [chemicool:chemicool]\n9071-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9074-\n9075-[Term]\n9076:id: PATO:0001428\n9077-name: medium acidity\n9078-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in a medium by virtue of the bearer's tendency to hydronate a specific reference base.\" [chemicool:chemicool]\n9079-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9082-\n9083-[Term]\n9084:id: PATO:0001429\n9085-name: acidic\n9086-def: \"An medium acidity quality inhering in a solution by virtue of the bearer's a high concentration of H+ ions.\" [chemicool:chemicool]\n9087-subset: value_slim\n--\n9089-\n9090-[Term]\n9091:id: PATO:0001430\n9092-name: alkaline\n9093-def: \"An medium acidity quality inhering in a solution by virtue of the bearer's a low concentration of H+ ions.\" [chemicool:chemicool]\n9094-subset: value_slim\n--\n9096-\n9097-[Term]\n9098:id: PATO:0001431\n9099-name: adhesivity\n9100-def: \"An emergent molecular quality that arises by virtue of the bearer's disposition to exhibit molecular attraction to another entity in contact.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9101-comment: The definition is general enough to cover adhesion arising from different kinds of chemical bonding/forces, although for PATO this term will most commonly used for cellular adhesion. See also GO:0031589 \"cell-substrate adhesion\".\n--\n9108-\n9109-[Term]\n9110:id: PATO:0001432\n9111-name: decayed\n9112-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's decomposition into component parts.\" [Medical-dictionary:Medical-dictionary]\n9113-subset: value_slim\n--\n9115-\n9116-[Term]\n9117:id: PATO:0001433\n9118-name: growth quality of occurrent\n9119-alt_id: PATO:0001489\n9120-def: \"A quality of a single process which describes the growth of an organism, structure, or group of organisms.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n--\n9125-\n9126-[Term]\n9127:id: PATO:0001434\n9128-name: reproductive quality\n9129-def: \"An organismal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to produce new life or offspring.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9130-is_a: PATO:0001995 ! organismal quality\n9131-\n9132-[Term]\n9133:id: PATO:0001435\n9134-name: attachment quality\n9135-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having connection or association with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9136-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9139-\n9140-[Term]\n9141:id: PATO:0001436\n9142-name: sessile (sensu botany)\n9143-def: \"An attachment quality inhering in a flower by virtue of the bearer's lacking a stalk, as in flowers or leaves that grow directly from the stem.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sessility_(botany)]\n9144-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9147-\n9148-[Term]\n9149:id: PATO:0001437\n9150-name: sessile (sensu zoology)\n9151-def: \"A attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's inability to move about.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sessile_(zoology)]\n9152-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9156-\n9157-[Term]\n9158:id: PATO:0001438\n9159-name: pedicellate\n9160-def: \"A attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or being supported by a pedicel or pedicle.\" [MedTerms:MedTerms]\n9161-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9164-\n9165-[Term]\n9166:id: PATO:0001439\n9167-name: tonicity\n9168-alt_id: PATO:0001498\n9169-def: \"A contractile quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's elastic tension that facilitate response to stimuli.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n--\n9176-\n9177-[Term]\n9178:id: PATO:0001440\n9179-name: homophilic\n9180-def: \"A cellular adhesivity quality inhering in a molecule in one cell by virtue of the bearer's attachment to an identical molecule in an adjacent cell.\" [GO:GO]\n9181-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9185-\n9186-[Term]\n9187:id: PATO:0001441\n9188-name: heterophilic\n9189-def: \"A cellular adhesivity quality inhering in a molecule in one cell by virtue of the bearer's attachment to an nonidentical molecule in an adjacent cell.\" [GO:GO]\n9190-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9193-\n9194-[Term]\n9195:id: PATO:0001442\n9196-name: wholeness\n9197-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer includes all its components.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9198-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9200-\n9201-[Term]\n9202:id: PATO:0001444\n9203-name: broken\n9204-alt_id: PATO:0001443\n9205-alt_id: PATO:0001820\n--\n9216-\n9217-[Term]\n9218:id: PATO:0001445\n9219-name: disassembled\n9220-def: \"A wholeness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being taken apart into its constituent parts.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9221-subset: value_slim\n--\n9223-\n9224-[Term]\n9225:id: PATO:0001446\n9226-name: whole\n9227-def: \"A wholeness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's including all its components.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9228-subset: value_slim\n--\n9230-\n9231-[Term]\n9232:id: PATO:0001447\n9233-name: calcified\n9234-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's being encrusted or impregnated with calcium carbonate (CHEBI:3311).\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9235-subset: cell_quality\n--\n9241-\n9242-[Term]\n9243:id: PATO:0001448\n9244-name: ossified\n9245-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's being hardened by the deposition of calcium into bone.\" [MAMMALOGY:MAMMALOGY]\n9246-subset: value_slim\n--\n9248-\n9249-[Term]\n9250:id: PATO:0001449\n9251-name: cartilaginous\n9252-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's cartilage quantities.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartilaginous]\n9253-comment: Cartilage is a type of dense connective tissue. It is composed of specialized cells called chondrocytes (CL:0000138) that produce a large amount of extracellular matrix composed of collagen fibers, abundant ground substance rich in proteoglycan, and elastin fibers.\n--\n9257-\n9258-[Term]\n9259:id: PATO:0001450\n9260-name: edematous\n9261-def: \"A structural quality which is held by a bearer when the latter exhibits an excessive accumulation of extracellular fluid.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9262-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9270-\n9271-[Term]\n9272:id: PATO:0001451\n9273-name: obsolete edematous (sensu botany)\n9274-def: \"An extended swelling in plant organs caused primarily by an excessive accumulation of water.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9275-synonym: \"edemic\" RELATED []\n--\n9279-\n9280-[Term]\n9281:id: PATO:0001453\n9282-name: detached from\n9283-def: \"An attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking connection or association with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9284-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9289-\n9290-[Term]\n9291:id: PATO:0001454\n9292-name: sensitivity to oxygen\n9293-def: \"A sensitivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's dependence on oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9294-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9298-\n9299-[Term]\n9300:id: PATO:0001455\n9301-name: aerobic\n9302-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's dependence on oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9303-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9308-\n9309-[Term]\n9310:id: PATO:0001456\n9311-name: anaerobic\n9312-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's independence on oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9313-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9317-\n9318-[Term]\n9319:id: PATO:0001457\n9320-name: sensitivity of a process\n9321-def: \"A quality of a process inhering in bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to respond to stimulation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9322-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9327-\n9328-[Term]\n9329:id: PATO:0001458\n9330-name: sensitivity of a process to oxygen\n9331-def: \"A sensitivity of a process quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's unfolding in a location with or without oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9332-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9336-\n9337-[Term]\n9338:id: PATO:0001459\n9339-name: aerobic (for occurrence)\n9340-def: \"A sensitivity of a process inhering in a biological process by virtue of the process unfolding in a location with oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9341-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9345-\n9346-[Term]\n9347:id: PATO:0001460\n9348-name: anaerobic (for occurrence)\n9349-def: \"A sensitivity of a process inhering in a biological process by virtue of the process unfolding in a location without oxygen.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9350-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9354-\n9355-[Term]\n9356:id: PATO:0001461\n9357-name: surface tension\n9358-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a liquid by virtue of the bearer's ability to attraction of molecules at its surface as a result of unbalanced molecular cohesive forces.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surface_tension]\n9359-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9363-\n9364-[Term]\n9365:id: PATO:0001462\n9366-name: membrane potential\n9367-def: \"A quality inhering in a cell's plasma membrane by virtue of the electrical potential difference across it.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Membrane_potential]\n9368-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9371-\n9372-[Term]\n9373:id: PATO:0001463\n9374-name: action potential\n9375-def: \"A quality inhering in a cell's plasma membrane by virtue of a brief fluctuation in the bearer's potential caused by the rapid opening and closing of voltage-gated ion channels.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Action_potential]\n9376-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9379-\n9380-[Term]\n9381:id: PATO:0001464\n9382-name: electric potential\n9383-def: \"A quality that is equal to the potential energy per unit charge associated with a static (time-invariant) electric field, also called the electrostatic potential.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_potential]\n9384-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9387-\n9388-[Term]\n9389:id: PATO:0001465\n9390-name: monstrous\n9391-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's all-encompassing, grotesque morphological defects.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9392-subset: value_slim\n--\n9394-\n9395-[Term]\n9396:id: PATO:0001466\n9397-name: curved rostral\n9398-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the front of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9399-subset: value_slim\n--\n9403-\n9404-[Term]\n9405:id: PATO:0001467\n9406-name: curved caudal\n9407-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the part of the body from which the tail arises.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9408-subset: value_slim\n--\n9412-\n9413-[Term]\n9414:id: PATO:0001468\n9415-name: curved dorsal\n9416-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the back or upper surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9417-subset: value_slim\n--\n9421-\n9422-[Term]\n9423:id: PATO:0001469\n9424-name: curved ventral\n9425-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the abdomen of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9426-subset: value_slim\n--\n9430-\n9431-[Term]\n9432:id: PATO:0001470\n9433-name: ratio\n9434-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's magnitude in proportion to the magnitude of another entity.\" [] {terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140\"}\n9435-comment: Examples: height to weight; brain size to body size; root to shoot ratio; urinary sodium to potassium ratio. waist-hip ratio. {terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140\"}\n--\n9444-\n9445-[Term]\n9446:id: PATO:0001472\n9447-name: decreased depth\n9448-alt_id: PATO:0001692\n9449-def: \"A depth which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n9456-\n9457-[Term]\n9458:id: PATO:0001473\n9459-name: duplicated\n9460-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being present in two copies.\" [Dictionary.com:Dictionary.com]\n9461-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9465-\n9466-[Term]\n9467:id: PATO:0001474\n9468-name: anteverted\n9469-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's axis being positioned forward.\" [bdid:bdid]\n9470-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9473-\n9474-[Term]\n9475:id: PATO:0001475\n9476-name: increased position\n9477-def: \"A position which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9478-subset: value_slim\n--\n9483-\n9484-[Term]\n9485:id: PATO:0001476\n9486-name: decreased position\n9487-def: \"A positional which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9488-subset: value_slim\n--\n9493-\n9494-[Term]\n9495:id: PATO:0001477\n9496-name: retracted\n9497-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being drawn in or pulled back from any given point.\" [Dictionary.com:Dictionary.com]\n9498-subset: value_slim\n--\n9502-\n9503-[Term]\n9504:id: PATO:0001478\n9505-name: collapsed\n9506-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being broken down; caved in.\" [Dictionary.com:Dictionary.com]\n9507-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9510-\n9511-[Term]\n9512:id: PATO:0001480\n9513-name: spongy\n9514-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a sponge in elasticity, absorbency, or porousness.\" [Answers.com:Answers.com]\n9515-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9519-\n9520-[Term]\n9521:id: PATO:0001481\n9522-name: sloped\n9523-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an oblique or slanted direction.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9524-subset: value_slim\n--\n9526-\n9527-[Term]\n9528:id: PATO:0001482\n9529-name: prominent\n9530-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's standing out or projecting beyond a surface or line.\" [Dictionary.com:Dictionary.com]\n9531-subset: value_slim\n--\n9534-\n9535-[Term]\n9536:id: PATO:0001483\n9537-name: aplastic\n9538-def: \"Absence of an organ, tissue or cell due to failure to develop from a primordium or precursor cell.\" [PATOC:GVG, PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n9539-comment: With aplasia, the primordium or precursor develops, but does not proceed in its development to a mature structure\n--\n9546-\n9547-[Term]\n9548:id: PATO:0001484\n9549-name: recent\n9550-def: \"A quality of a process which occurs near to or not long before the present.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9551-subset: value_slim\n--\n9553-\n9554-[Term]\n9555:id: PATO:0001485\n9556-name: condensed\n9557-alt_id: PATO:0001840\n9558-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being thicker or more closely packed together; pressed tightly together.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n9567-\n9568-[Term]\n9569:id: PATO:0001486\n9570-name: chronological age\n9571-def: \"An age quality that exists by virtue of the time (years and months) that the bearer has existed.\" [WordNet:Wordnet]\n9572-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9574-\n9575-[Term]\n9576:id: PATO:0001487\n9577-name: senescent\n9578-def: \"A time quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's growing old; aging.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n9579-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9582-\n9583-[Term]\n9584:id: PATO:0001488\n9585-name: cellular motility\n9586-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a cell by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits the ability to move spontaneously.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9587-comment: Term should be obsoleted and the GO term cellular motility should be used instead.\n--\n9592-\n9593-[Term]\n9594:id: PATO:0001490\n9595-name: heterochronic growth\n9596-def: \"A growth quality of a process inhering in an organism, structure, or group of organisms by virtue of the bearer's reduced or increased growth.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n9597-subset: value_slim\n--\n9599-\n9600-[Term]\n9601:id: PATO:0001491\n9602-name: neotenous growth\n9603-def: \"A paedomorphic growth quality which is due to a reduced rate.\" [PATOC:mh]\n9604-subset: value_slim\n--\n9607-\n9608-[Term]\n9609:id: PATO:0001492\n9610-name: growth rate\n9611-def: \"The rate or speed of the change in size of an individual entity or change in number of a population.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9900-7880, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n9612-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9615-\n9616-[Term]\n9617:id: PATO:0001493\n9618-name: hypertrophic growth\n9619-comment: This term will be obsoleted; Use GO:growth and PATO:rate.\n9620-subset: value_slim\n--\n9623-\n9624-[Term]\n9625:id: PATO:0001494\n9626-name: hypotrophic growth\n9627-comment: This term will be obsoleted; Use GO:growth and PATO:rate.\n9628-subset: value_slim\n--\n9631-\n9632-[Term]\n9633:id: PATO:0001495\n9634-name: notched\n9635-def: \"A concave quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape being a V-shaped cut.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9636-subset: cell_quality\n--\n9641-\n9642-[Term]\n9643:id: PATO:0001496\n9644-name: brood quality\n9645-def: \"A reproductive quality inhering in the young of an animal by virtue of the bearer's being cared for at one time.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9646-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9648-\n9649-[Term]\n9650:id: PATO:0001497\n9651-name: brood viability\n9652-def: \"A reproductive quality inhering in the young of an animal by virtue of the bearer's disposition to survive and develop normally.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9653-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9656-\n9657-[Term]\n9658:id: PATO:0001499\n9659-name: spherical\n9660-alt_id: PATO:0000408\n9661-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a ball (a sphere whose equatorial diameter is equal to the polar diameter).\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n--\n9669-\n9670-[Term]\n9671:id: PATO:0001500\n9672-name: tapered\n9673-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being gradually narrower or thinner toward one end.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9674-subset: cell_quality\n--\n9678-\n9679-[Term]\n9680:id: PATO:0001501\n9681-name: immature\n9682-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking complete growth, differentiation, or development.\" [Merriam-Webster:Merriam-Webster]\n9683-subset: value_slim\n--\n9687-\n9688-[Term]\n9689:id: PATO:0001502\n9690-name: complexity\n9691-def: \"A monadic quality of continuant inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being intricate and compounded.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9692-comment: TODO: obsolete this.\n--\n9695-\n9696-[Term]\n9697:id: PATO:0001503\n9698-name: simple\n9699-def: \"A complexity quality in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having few parts or being complicated or compound.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9700-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9704-\n9705-[Term]\n9706:id: PATO:0001504\n9707-name: complex\n9708-def: \"A complexity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being intricate and compounded.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9709-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9712-\n9713-[Term]\n9714:id: PATO:0001505\n9715-name: separated from\n9716-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not being in contact with another entity, or of no longer being connected or joined with another entity.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n9717-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9723-\n9724-[Term]\n9725:id: PATO:0001506\n9726-name: diastatic\n9727-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's separation of normally joined parts, such as the separation of adjacent bones without fracture or of certain abdominal muscles during pregnancy.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n9728-subset: relational_slim\n--\n9731-\n9732-[Term]\n9733:id: PATO:0001507\n9734-name: disrupted\n9735-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being interrupted of its normal course.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9736-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9739-\n9740-[Term]\n9741:id: PATO:0001509\n9742-name: functionality\n9743-def: \"A quality of a single physical entity that arises by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits the ability to perform a regular function(s).\" [PATOC:MAH]\n9744-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9748-\n9749-[Term]\n9750:id: PATO:0001510\n9751-name: functional\n9752-def: \"A functionality quality held by the bearer when the latter is able to perform a regular function(s).\" [PATOC:MAH]\n9753-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9757-\n9758-[Term]\n9759:id: PATO:0001511\n9760-name: non-functional\n9761-alt_id: PATO:0001640\n9762-def: \"A disfunctional quality held by the bearer when the latter is unable to perform a regular function(s).\" [PATC:MAH]\n--\n9771-\n9772-[Term]\n9773:id: PATO:0001512\n9774-name: punctate\n9775-def: \"A pattern inhering in a surface by virtue of the bearer's being marked by the presence of dots, punctures, points or pits.\" [medical-dictionary:medical-dictionary]\n9776-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9782-\n9783-[Term]\n9784:id: PATO:0001514\n9785-name: delaminated\n9786-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking some outer layer.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n9787-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n9790-\n9791-[Term]\n9792:id: PATO:0001515\n9793-name: variable color\n9794-def: \"A color quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being uneven in color.\" [PATOC:NC]\n9795-subset: value_slim\n--\n9798-\n9799-[Term]\n9800:id: PATO:0001516\n9801-name: focus\n9802-def: \"An optical quality where light rays originating from a point on the object converge.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Focus_(optics)]\n9803-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9805-\n9806-[Term]\n9807:id: PATO:0001517\n9808-name: focused\n9809-def: \"An optical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having focus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9810-subset: value_slim\n--\n9812-\n9813-[Term]\n9814:id: PATO:0001518\n9815-name: blurry\n9816-def: \"An optical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking focus.\" [PATOC:NC]\n9817-subset: value_slim\n--\n9819-\n9820-[Term]\n9821:id: PATO:0001519\n9822-name: sound quality\n9823-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of vibration, as perceived by the sense of hearing.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_quality]\n9824-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9826-\n9827-[Term]\n9828:id: PATO:0001520\n9829-name: sound frequency\n9830-def: \"The frequency of transmitted vibrations.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n9831-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9834-\n9835-[Term]\n9836:id: PATO:0001521\n9837-name: sound amplitude\n9838-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a sound wave by virtue of the maximum magnitude (value without regard to sign) of its disturbance.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n9839-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9842-\n9843-[Term]\n9844:id: PATO:0001522\n9845-name: sound speed\n9846-def: \"A physical quality inhering in sound by virtue of the bearer's travelling speed in a given medium under specified conditions.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_speed]\n9847-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9850-\n9851-[Term]\n9852:id: PATO:0001523\n9853-name: sound wavelength\n9854-def: \"A physical quality which is equal to the quotient of the speed of a sound wave divided by its wavelength.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_wavelength]\n9855-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9858-\n9859-[Term]\n9860:id: PATO:0001524\n9861-name: intrasonic\n9862-def: \"A sound frequency in the range of 0-20 Hz.\" [studyphysics:studyphysics]\n9863-subset: value_slim\n--\n9865-\n9866-[Term]\n9867:id: PATO:0001525\n9868-name: sonic\n9869-def: \"A sound frequency in the range of 20 to 20.000 Hz.\" [url:http\\://www.studyphysics.ca/]\n9870-subset: value_slim\n--\n9872-\n9873-[Term]\n9874:id: PATO:0001526\n9875-name: ultrasonic\n9876-def: \"A sound frequency in the range of 20 000 + Hz.\" [studyphysics:studyphysics]\n9877-subset: value_slim\n--\n9879-\n9880-[Term]\n9881:id: PATO:0001527\n9882-name: quiet\n9883-def: \"A sound amplitude which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9884-subset: value_slim\n--\n9886-\n9887-[Term]\n9888:id: PATO:0001528\n9889-name: loud\n9890-def: \"A sound amplitude which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9891-subset: value_slim\n--\n9893-\n9894-[Term]\n9895:id: PATO:0001529\n9896-name: cellular spatiotemporal quality\n9897-def: \"A spatiotemporal quality inhering in a cell.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9898-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9900-\n9901-[Term]\n9902:id: PATO:0001530\n9903-name: behavioral quality of a process\n9904-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's behavior.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9905-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9908-\n9909-[Term]\n9910:id: PATO:0001531\n9911-name: cellular adhesivity\n9912-def: \"A cellular quality that exists by virtue of the disposition of the cell to adhere to other cells and molecules, through the emergent action of the molecular parts of the cell surface.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n9913-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9917-\n9918-[Term]\n9919:id: PATO:0001532\n9920-name: mono-colored\n9921-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one hue.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9922-subset: value_slim\n--\n9928-\n9929-[Term]\n9930:id: PATO:0001533\n9931-name: multi-colored\n9932-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's having two or more hues or degrees of saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9933-subset: value_slim\n--\n9936-\n9937-[Term]\n9938:id: PATO:0001534\n9939-name: motley\n9940-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's having 3 or more hues or degrees of saturations.\" [merriam-webster.:merriam-webster.]\n9941-subset: value_slim\n--\n9943-\n9944-[Term]\n9945:id: PATO:0001535\n9946-name: dappled\n9947-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's being marked with small spots, patches, or specks of hue or degree of saturation differing from that of the background.\" [merriam-webster.:merriam-webster.]\n9948-subset: value_slim\n--\n9951-\n9952-[Term]\n9953:id: PATO:0001536\n9954-name: solubility\n9955-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the bearer's disposition to dissolve in a liquid.\" [edp:edp]\n9956-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9961-\n9962-[Term]\n9963:id: PATO:0001537\n9964-name: soluble in\n9965-def: \"A solubility quality inhering in a substance by virtue of the bearer's disposition to dissolve in a liquid.\" [edp:edp]\n9966-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9973-\n9974-[Term]\n9975:id: PATO:0001538\n9976-name: insoluble in\n9977-def: \"A solubility quality inhering in a substance by virtue of the bearer's inability of a substance to dissolve in a liquid.\" [edp:edp]\n9978-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n9984-\n9985-[Term]\n9986:id: PATO:0001539\n9987-name: amylose composition\n9988-def: \"A compositional quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's quantities or relative ratios of amylose of the inhering entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n9989-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n9993-\n9994-[Term]\n9995:id: PATO:0001540\n9996-name: glutinous\n9997-def: \"An amylose composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's having negligible or no amylose content.\" [TO:TO]\n9998-subset: value_slim\n--\n10000-\n10001-[Term]\n10002:id: PATO:0001541\n10003-name: non-glutinous\n10004-def: \"An amylose composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's having high amount of amylose content.\" [TO:TO]\n10005-subset: value_slim\n--\n10007-\n10008-[Term]\n10009:id: PATO:0001542\n10010-name: delayed phase\n10011-def: \"A phase which starts later than natural start point.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10012-subset: value_slim\n--\n10014-\n10015-[Term]\n10016:id: PATO:0001543\n10017-name: flexibility\n10018-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being turned, bowed, or twisted without breaking.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n10019-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10022-\n10023-[Term]\n10024:id: PATO:0001544\n10025-name: flexible\n10026-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability of being turned, bowed, or twisted without breaking.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n10027-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10032-\n10033-[Term]\n10034:id: PATO:0001545\n10035-name: inflexible\n10036-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's inability of being turned, bowed, or twisted without breaking.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n10037-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10043-\n10044-[Term]\n10045:id: PATO:0001546\n10046-name: quality of a solid\n10047-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting the physical characteristics of an entity characterized by particles arranged such that their shape and volume are relatively stable.\" [Chemistry:http\\://chemistry.about.com/od/chemistryglossary/a/soliddefinition.htm]\n10048-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10051-\n10052-[Term]\n10053:id: PATO:0001547\n10054-name: quality of a gas\n10055-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting the physical characteristics of an entity consisting of particles that have neither a defined volume nor defined shape.\" [Chemistry:http\\://chemistry.about.com/od/chemistryglossary/a/gasdefinition.htm, PATOC:GVG]\n10056-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10059-\n10060-[Term]\n10061:id: PATO:0001548\n10062-name: quality of a liquid\n10063-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an entity exhibiting the physical characteristics of an amorphous (non-crystalline) form of matter between a gas and a solid that has a definite volume, but no definite shape.\" [url:http\\://www.chemistry-dictionary.com/definition/liquid.php]\n10064-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10067-\n10068-[Term]\n10069:id: PATO:0001549\n10070-name: increased sensitivity toward\n10071-def: \"A sensitivity toward an external stimulus which is higher than normal/average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10072-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10080-\n10081-[Term]\n10082:id: PATO:0001550\n10083-name: decreased sensitivity toward\n10084-def: \"A sensitivity toward an external stimulus which is lower than normal/average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10085-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10093-\n10094-[Term]\n10095:id: PATO:0001551\n10096-name: increased sensitivity of a process\n10097-def: \"A sensitivity of a process which is higher than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10098-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10105-\n10106-[Term]\n10107:id: PATO:0001552\n10108-name: decreased sensitivity of a process\n10109-def: \"A sensitivity of a process which is lower than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10110-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10117-\n10118-[Term]\n10119:id: PATO:0001553\n10120-name: increased sensitivity of a process to oxygen\n10121-def: \"A sensitivity of occurrent to oxygen which is higher than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10122-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10128-\n10129-[Term]\n10130:id: PATO:0001554\n10131-name: decreased sensitivity of a process to oxygen\n10132-def: \"A sensitivity of a process to oxygen which is lower than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10133-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10139-\n10140-[Term]\n10141:id: PATO:0001555\n10142-name: has number of\n10143-def: \"The number of parts of a particular type that the bearer entity has. This is a relational quality, and thus holds between two entities: the bearer of the quality, and the type of parts.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n10144-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10154-\n10155-[Term]\n10156:id: PATO:0001558\n10157-name: lacking processual parts\n10158-def: \"A quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking a processual part as specified by the additional entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10159-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10163-\n10164-[Term]\n10165:id: PATO:0001559\n10166-name: having extra function\n10167-def: \"A functionality quality which is held by the bearer when the latter is able to perform additional or different function(s).\" [PATO:MAH]\n10168-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10173-\n10174-[Term]\n10175:id: PATO:0001561\n10176-name: having extra processual parts\n10177-def: \"A quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having additional processual parts.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10178-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10182-\n10183-[Term]\n10184:id: PATO:0001562\n10185-name: decreased mass\n10186-alt_id: PATO:0000579\n10187-def: \"A mass which is lower than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n--\n10194-\n10195-[Term]\n10196:id: PATO:0001563\n10197-name: increased mass\n10198-alt_id: PATO:0000578\n10199-def: \"A mass which is higher than normal or average.\" [PATO:GVG]\n--\n10206-\n10207-[Term]\n10208:id: PATO:0001564\n10209-name: extra or missing processual parts\n10210-def: \"A quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's processual parts.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10211-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10213-\n10214-[Term]\n10215:id: PATO:0001566\n10216-name: distributed\n10217-alt_id: PATO:0001513\n10218-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being spread out or scattered about or divided up.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n--\n10226-\n10227-[Term]\n10228:id: PATO:0001567\n10229-name: undistributed\n10230-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not being spread out or scattered about or divided up.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10231-subset: value_slim\n--\n10234-\n10235-[Term]\n10236:id: PATO:0001570\n10237-name: having decreased processual parts\n10238-def: \"A quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having fewer processual parts.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10239-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10242-\n10243-[Term]\n10244:id: PATO:0001571\n10245-name: dilated\n10246-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being made wider or larger in all dimensions.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10247-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10250-\n10251-[Term]\n10252:id: PATO:0001573\n10253-name: isometrical\n10254-def: \"A symmetry quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having equal dimensions or measurements.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10255-subset: cell_quality\n--\n10258-\n10259-[Term]\n10260:id: PATO:0001574\n10261-name: flow rate\n10262-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's motion characteristic.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10263-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10266-\n10267-[Term]\n10268:id: PATO:0001575\n10269-name: decreased pressure\n10270-def: \"A pressure which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10271-subset: value_slim\n--\n10276-\n10277-[Term]\n10278:id: PATO:0001576\n10279-name: increased pressure\n10280-def: \"A pressure which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10281-subset: value_slim\n--\n10286-\n10287-[Term]\n10288:id: PATO:0001577\n10289-name: increased permeability\n10290-def: \"A permeability which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10291-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10297-\n10298-[Term]\n10299:id: PATO:0001578\n10300-name: decreased permeability\n10301-def: \"A permeability which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10302-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10308-\n10309-[Term]\n10310:id: PATO:0001579\n10311-name: contractility\n10312-def: \"A physical quality that is the ability to contract or shrink.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10313-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10317-\n10318-[Term]\n10319:id: PATO:0001580\n10320-name: increased contractility\n10321-def: \"A contractility which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10322-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10328-\n10329-[Term]\n10330:id: PATO:0001581\n10331-name: decreased contractility\n10332-def: \"A contractility which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10333-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10339-\n10340-[Term]\n10341:id: PATO:0001582\n10342-name: obsolete relaxational quality\n10343-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in an inactive muscle or muscle fibers by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting gradual lengthening.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10344-comment: GO has now relevant relation terms which should be used instead.\n--\n10346-\n10347-[Term]\n10348:id: PATO:0001583\n10349-name: decreased variability\n10350-def: \"A variability which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10351-subset: value_slim\n--\n10356-\n10357-[Term]\n10358:id: PATO:0001584\n10359-name: increased variability\n10360-def: \"A variability which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10361-subset: value_slim\n--\n10366-\n10367-[Term]\n10368:id: PATO:0001585\n10369-name: conductivity\n10370-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to transmit of an entity through a medium.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10371-comment: Examples could be heat or electricity or sound.\n--\n10376-\n10377-[Term]\n10378:id: PATO:0001586\n10379-name: variability of rate\n10380-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits rate variation or change.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10381-subset: value_slim\n--\n10384-\n10385-[Term]\n10386:id: PATO:0001587\n10387-name: increased variability of rate\n10388-def: \"A variability of rate which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10389-subset: value_slim\n--\n10394-\n10395-[Term]\n10396:id: PATO:0001588\n10397-name: decreased variability of rate\n10398-def: \"A variability of rate which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10399-subset: value_slim\n--\n10404-\n10405-[Term]\n10406:id: PATO:0001589\n10407-name: obsolete enhanced\n10408-def: \"Increased, intensified.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10409-comment: Obsoleted because it used to be a child of behavioral quality, which really meant increased magnitude of a given behavior. Now this can be done by using increased magnitude with another quality.\n--\n10412-\n10413-[Term]\n10414:id: PATO:0001590\n10415-name: overlap with\n10416-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's coinciding spatially, partially or wholly with another entity.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10417-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10421-\n10422-[Term]\n10423:id: PATO:0001591\n10424-name: curvature\n10425-def: \"A surface shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a degree of bending.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10426-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10428-\n10429-[Term]\n10430:id: PATO:0001592\n10431-name: increased curvature\n10432-def: \"A curvature which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10433-subset: value_slim\n--\n10437-\n10438-[Term]\n10439:id: PATO:0001593\n10440-name: decreased curvature\n10441-def: \"A curvature which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10442-subset: value_slim\n--\n10446-\n10447-[Term]\n10448:id: PATO:0001594\n10449-name: arched\n10450-def: \"A concave quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's forming or resembling an arch.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10451-subset: cell_quality\n--\n10453-\n10454-[Term]\n10455:id: PATO:0001595\n10456-name: depth\n10457-def: \"A 1-D extent quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's downward or backward or inward dimension.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10458-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10461-\n10462-[Term]\n10463:id: PATO:0001596\n10464-name: increased depth\n10465-alt_id: PATO:0001666\n10466-def: \"A depth quality which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n--\n10472-\n10473-[Term]\n10474:id: PATO:0001597\n10475-name: everted\n10476-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being turned outward in placement.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n10477-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10480-\n10481-[Term]\n10482:id: PATO:0001598\n10483-name: protruding\n10484-alt_id: PATO:0001644\n10485-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's extending out above or beyond a surface or boundary.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n--\n10490-\n10491-[Term]\n10492:id: PATO:0001599\n10493-name: rotated\n10494-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being relocated around an axis.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n10495-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10499-\n10500-[Term]\n10501:id: PATO:0001600\n10502-name: posteriorly rotated\n10503-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the rear of organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10504-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10507-\n10508-[Term]\n10509:id: PATO:0001601\n10510-name: anteriorly rotated\n10511-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the front of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10512-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10515-\n10516-[Term]\n10517:id: PATO:0001602\n10518-name: distended\n10519-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being abnormally expanded or increased in size.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10520-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10524-\n10525-[Term]\n10526:id: PATO:0001603\n10527-name: increased life span\n10528-def: \"A life span which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10529-synonym: \"high life span\" EXACT []\n--\n10533-\n10534-[Term]\n10535:id: PATO:0001604\n10536-name: decreased life span\n10537-def: \"A life span which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10538-synonym: \"low life span\" EXACT []\n--\n10542-\n10543-[Term]\n10544:id: PATO:0001605\n10545-name: disheveled\n10546-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in disarray; extremely disorderly.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10547-subset: cell_quality\n--\n10550-\n10551-[Term]\n10552:id: PATO:0001606\n10553-name: greasy\n10554-def: \"A coating which is oily and slippery.\" [.answers.com:.answers.com]\n10555-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10558-\n10559-[Term]\n10560:id: PATO:0001607\n10561-name: matted\n10562-def: \"A tangled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being not possible to unravel.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n10563-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10566-\n10567-[Term]\n10568:id: PATO:0001608\n10569-name: patchy\n10570-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by, consisting of, or diversified with patches.\" [Merriam-Webster:Merriam-Webster]\n10571-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10574-\n10575-[Term]\n10576:id: PATO:0001609\n10577-name: sparse\n10578-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being scattered; spread irregularly, and at a distance from each other.\" [biology.lsu:biology.lsu]\n10579-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10582-\n10583-[Term]\n10584:id: PATO:0001611\n10585-name: variability of color\n10586-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits color variation or change.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10587-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10590-\n10591-[Term]\n10592:id: PATO:0001612\n10593-name: increased variability of color\n10594-def: \"A variability of color which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10595-subset: value_slim\n--\n10600-\n10601-[Term]\n10602:id: PATO:0001613\n10603-name: decreased variability of color\n10604-def: \"A variability of color which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10605-subset: value_slim\n--\n10610-\n10611-[Term]\n10612:id: PATO:0001614\n10613-name: invariant color\n10614-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking or not exhibiting variation of color.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10615-subset: value_slim\n--\n10618-\n10619-[Term]\n10620:id: PATO:0001615\n10621-name: variant color\n10622-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or exhibiting variation of colour.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10623-subset: value_slim\n--\n10626-\n10627-[Term]\n10628:id: PATO:0001617\n10629-name: deformed\n10630-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being distorted in form.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n10631-subset: value_slim\n--\n10635-\n10636-[Term]\n10637:id: PATO:0001618\n10638-name: increased tonicity\n10639-def: \"A tonicity which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10640-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10646-\n10647-[Term]\n10648:id: PATO:0001619\n10649-name: decreased tonicity\n10650-def: \"A tonicity which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10651-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10657-\n10658-[Term]\n10659:id: PATO:0001620\n10660-name: turgor\n10661-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a cell or blood vessel or capillary by virtue of the bearer's being in a rigid state of fullness resulting from pressure of the contents against the wall or membrane.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10662-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10665-\n10666-[Term]\n10667:id: PATO:0001621\n10668-name: decreased turgor\n10669-def: \"A turgor which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10670-subset: cell_quality\n--\n10676-\n10677-[Term]\n10678:id: PATO:0001622\n10679-name: increased turgor\n10680-def: \"A turgor which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10681-subset: cell_quality\n--\n10687-\n10688-[Term]\n10689:id: PATO:0001623\n10690-name: atrophied\n10691-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of a part or parts of the bearer's being decreased in size due to reduction in tissue mass through wasting.\" [Wiikipedia:Wasting, Wikipedia:Atrophy]\n10692-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10696-\n10697-[Term]\n10698:id: PATO:0001624\n10699-name: decreased functionality\n10700-alt_id: PATO:0001556\n10701-alt_id: PATO:0001568\n--\n10717-\n10718-[Term]\n10719:id: PATO:0001625\n10720-name: increased functionality\n10721-def: \"A functional quality held by the bearer when the latter exhibits increased ability to perform a regular function(s).\" [PATO:MAH]\n10722-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10728-\n10729-[Term]\n10730:id: PATO:0001626\n10731-name: sufficiency\n10732-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer has enough functionality.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10733-comment: This term and children should probably be obsoleted.\n--\n10737-\n10738-[Term]\n10739:id: PATO:0001627\n10740-name: sufficient\n10741-def: \"A wholeness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's has enough functionality.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10742-subset: value_slim\n--\n10746-\n10747-[Term]\n10748:id: PATO:0001628\n10749-name: insufficient\n10750-def: \"A wholeness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacks enough functionality.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10751-subset: value_slim\n--\n10755-\n10756-[Term]\n10757:id: PATO:0001629\n10758-name: aggregated\n10759-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being gathered or tending to gather into a mass or whole.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10760-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10765-\n10766-[Term]\n10767:id: PATO:0001630\n10768-name: dispersed\n10769-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being distributed or spread over a considerable extent.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10770-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10773-\n10774-[Term]\n10775:id: PATO:0001632\n10776-name: anterior to\n10777-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the front of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:nw]\n10778-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10783-\n10784-[Term]\n10785:id: PATO:0001633\n10786-name: posterior to\n10787-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the rear of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:nw]\n10788-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10794-\n10795-[Term]\n10796:id: PATO:0001634\n10797-name: necessity (continuant)\n10798-def: \"A quality of a single physical entity inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer is essential or indispensable.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10799-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10801-\n10802-[Term]\n10803:id: PATO:0001635\n10804-name: necessary (continuant)\n10805-def: \"A necessity quality (continuant) inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being essential or indispensable.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10806-subset: value_slim\n--\n10810-\n10811-[Term]\n10812:id: PATO:0001636\n10813-name: unnecessary (continuant)\n10814-def: \"A necessity quality (continuant) inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being non-essential or dispensable.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10815-subset: value_slim\n--\n10818-\n10819-[Term]\n10820:id: PATO:0001637\n10821-name: necessity of occurrent\n10822-def: \"A quality of single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer is essential or indispensable.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10823-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10825-\n10826-[Term]\n10827:id: PATO:0001638\n10828-name: necessary (occurrent)\n10829-def: \"A necessity quality inhering in a process by virtue of the bearer's being essential or indispensable.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10830-subset: value_slim\n--\n10833-\n10834-[Term]\n10835:id: PATO:0001639\n10836-name: unnecessary (occurrent)\n10837-def: \"A necessity quality inhering in a process by virtue of the bearer's being non-essential or dispensable.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10838-subset: value_slim\n--\n10841-\n10842-[Term]\n10843:id: PATO:0001643\n10844-name: stubby\n10845-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a short, stocky build.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n10846-subset: value_slim\n--\n10848-\n10849-[Term]\n10850:id: PATO:0001645\n10851-name: protruding into\n10852-def: \"A quality inhering into a bearer by virtue of the bearer's extending out above or beyond its surface or boundary into the surface or boundary of another entity.\" [PATOC:nc]\n10853-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10856-\n10857-[Term]\n10858:id: PATO:0001646\n10859-name: protruding out of\n10860-def: \"A quality inhering into a bearer by virtue of the bearer's extending out above or beyond its surface or boundary and outwards in relation to the physical space occupied by another entity.\" [PATOC:nc]\n10861-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10867-\n10868-[Term]\n10869:id: PATO:0001648\n10870-name: circumference\n10871-def: \"An 1-D extent quality which is equal to the length of the closed curve of a circle.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n10872-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10875-\n10876-[Term]\n10877:id: PATO:0001649\n10878-name: curved lateral\n10879-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10880-subset: value_slim\n--\n10882-\n10883-[Term]\n10884:id: PATO:0001650\n10885-name: increased resistance to\n10886-def: \"A resistance to a stimulus which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10887-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10895-\n10896-[Term]\n10897:id: PATO:0001651\n10898-name: decreased resistance to\n10899-def: \"A resistance to a stimulus which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10900-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n10908-\n10909-[Term]\n10910:id: PATO:0001652\n10911-name: alignment\n10912-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's spatial positioning with respect to an additional entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10913-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10917-\n10918-[Term]\n10919:id: PATO:0001653\n10920-name: aligned with\n10921-def: \"An alignment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in a proper spatial positioning with respect to an additional entity.\" [PATO:GVG]\n10922-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10928-\n10929-[Term]\n10930:id: PATO:0001654\n10931-name: misaligned with\n10932-def: \"An alignment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in a improper spatial positioning with respect to an additional entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10933-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10939-\n10940-[Term]\n10941:id: PATO:0001655\n10942-name: osmolarity\n10943-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's amount of osmoles of solute per liter of solution.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmolarity]\n10944-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n10948-\n10949-[Term]\n10950:id: PATO:0001656\n10951-name: decreased osmolarity\n10952-def: \"A osmolarity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10953-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10960-\n10961-[Term]\n10962:id: PATO:0001657\n10963-name: increased osmolarity\n10964-def: \"A osmolarity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10965-subset: relational_slim\n--\n10972-\n10973-[Term]\n10974:id: PATO:0001658\n10975-name: dorsally rotated\n10976-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the back or upper surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10977-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10980-\n10981-[Term]\n10982:id: PATO:0001659\n10983-name: ventrally rotated\n10984-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the abdomen of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10985-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n10989-\n10990-[Term]\n10991:id: PATO:0001660\n10992-name: obsolete decreased action potential\n10993-def: \"An action potential which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n10994-subset: value_slim\n--\n10997-\n10998-[Term]\n10999:id: PATO:0001661\n11000-name: obsolete increased action potential\n11001-def: \"An action potential which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11002-subset: value_slim\n--\n11005-\n11006-[Term]\n11007:id: PATO:0001662\n11008-name: fragility\n11009-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being damaged or destroyed.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n11010-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11014-\n11015-[Term]\n11016:id: PATO:0001663\n11017-name: increased solubility\n11018-def: \"A solubility which is relatively high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n11019-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11026-\n11027-[Term]\n11028:id: PATO:0001664\n11029-name: decreased solubility\n11030-def: \"A solubility which is relatively low.\" [PATO:GVG]\n11031-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11038-\n11039-[Term]\n11040:id: PATO:0001665\n11041-name: superficial\n11042-alt_id: PATO:0001471\n11043-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located near a surface.\" [Dictionary.com:Dictionary.com]\n--\n11049-\n11050-[Term]\n11051:id: PATO:0001667\n11052-name: attached to\n11053-def: \"An attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's connection or association with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11054-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n11060-\n11061-[Term]\n11062:id: PATO:0001668\n11063-name: associated with\n11064-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in close proximity and physically interacting with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11065-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n11070-\n11071-[Term]\n11072:id: PATO:0001669\n11073-name: increased susceptibility toward\n11074-def: \"A susceptibility toward an external stimulus which is higher than normal/average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11075-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11083-\n11084-[Term]\n11085:id: PATO:0001670\n11086-name: decreased susceptibility toward\n11087-def: \"A susceptibility toward an external stimulus which is lower than normal/average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11088-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11096-\n11097-[Term]\n11098:id: PATO:0001671\n11099-name: increased distribution\n11100-def: \"A distribution which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11101-subset: value_slim\n--\n11106-\n11107-[Term]\n11108:id: PATO:0001672\n11109-name: decreased distribution\n11110-def: \"A distribution which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11111-subset: value_slim\n--\n11116-\n11117-[Term]\n11118:id: PATO:0001673\n11119-name: cystic\n11120-def: \"Structure quality that is the presence of at least one sac-like closed membranous structure containing one or more liquid or solid organism substances.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n11121-comment: Cystic is an abnormal condition.\n--\n11125-\n11126-[Term]\n11127:id: PATO:0001674\n11128-name: catalytic (activity) concentration\n11129-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's catalytic activity divided by the volume of the system.\" [IUPAC:IUPAC]\n11130-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11134-\n11135-[Term]\n11136:id: PATO:0001675\n11137-name: decreased efficiency\n11138-def: \"An efficiency which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11139-subset: value_slim\n--\n11144-\n11145-[Term]\n11146:id: PATO:0001676\n11147-name: increased efficiency\n11148-def: \"An efficiency which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11149-subset: value_slim\n--\n11154-\n11155-[Term]\n11156:id: PATO:0001677\n11157-name: inefficient\n11158-def: \"An efficiency quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking efficiency.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11159-subset: value_slim\n--\n11163-\n11164-[Term]\n11165:id: PATO:0001678\n11166-name: efficient\n11167-def: \"An efficiency quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having efficiency.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11168-subset: value_slim\n--\n11171-\n11172-[Term]\n11173:id: PATO:0001679\n11174-name: specific volume\n11175-def: \"A volume quality inhering in a mass of substance by virtue of the amount of 3-dimensional space it occupies.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Specific_volume]\n11176-comment: The reciprocal of density.\n--\n11180-\n11181-[Term]\n11182:id: PATO:0001680\n11183-name: molar volume\n11184-def: \"A volume quality inhering in a homogeneous substance containing 6.02 x 1023 atoms or molecules by virtue of the amount of 3-dimensional space it occupies.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molar_volume]\n11185-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11188-\n11189-[Term]\n11190:id: PATO:0001681\n11191-name: molar mass\n11192-def: \"A physical quality that inheres in a homogeneous substance containing 6.02 x 1023 atoms or molecules.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molar_mass]\n11193-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11196-\n11197-[Term]\n11198:id: PATO:0001682\n11199-name: magnetism\n11200-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to exert an attractive or repulsive force on other entities.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnetism]\n11201-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11205-\n11206-[Term]\n11207:id: PATO:0001683\n11208-name: increased magnetism\n11209-def: \"A magnetism which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11210-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11216-\n11217-[Term]\n11218:id: PATO:0001684\n11219-name: decreased magnetism\n11220-def: \"A magnetism which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11221-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11227-\n11228-[Term]\n11229:id: PATO:0001685\n11230-name: magnetic\n11231-def: \"A magnetic quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to exert magnitism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11232-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11237-\n11238-[Term]\n11239:id: PATO:0001686\n11240-name: non-magnetic\n11241-def: \"A magnetic quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's inability to exert magnitism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11242-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11246-\n11247-[Term]\n11248:id: PATO:0001687\n11249-name: elevation\n11250-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's vertical distance of a point above or below a reference surface.\" [Trailillustrated:Trailillustrated]\n11251-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11253-\n11254-[Term]\n11255:id: PATO:0001688\n11256-name: increased elevation\n11257-def: \"An elevation which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11258-subset: value_slim\n--\n11264-\n11265-[Term]\n11266:id: PATO:0001689\n11267-name: decreased elevation\n11268-def: \"An elevation which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11269-subset: value_slim\n--\n11274-\n11275-[Term]\n11276:id: PATO:0001690\n11277-name: contractile\n11278-def: \"A contractility quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability of contracting or being contracted.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11279-comment: This refers to the disposition of the bearer.\n--\n11285-\n11286-[Term]\n11287:id: PATO:0001691\n11288-name: non-contractile\n11289-def: \"A contractility quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's inability of contracting or being contracted.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11290-comment: This refers to the disposition of the bearer.\n--\n11295-\n11296-[Term]\n11297:id: PATO:0001693\n11298-name: increased viscosity\n11299-def: \"A viscosity which relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11300-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11306-\n11307-[Term]\n11308:id: PATO:0001694\n11309-name: decreased viscosity\n11310-def: \"A viscosity which relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11311-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11317-\n11318-[Term]\n11319:id: PATO:0001695\n11320-name: increased fecundity\n11321-def: \"A fecundity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11322-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11328-\n11329-[Term]\n11330:id: PATO:0001696\n11331-name: decreased fecundity\n11332-def: \"A fecundity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11333-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11339-\n11340-[Term]\n11341:id: PATO:0001697\n11342-name: decreased photosensitivity\n11343-def: \"A photosensitivity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11344-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11351-\n11352-[Term]\n11353:id: PATO:0001698\n11354-name: increased photosensitivity\n11355-def: \"A photosensitivity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11356-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11363-\n11364-[Term]\n11365:id: PATO:0001699\n11366-name: regular sleep pattern\n11367-def: \"A sleep pattern which has regular start and/or end times.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11368-subset: value_slim\n--\n11371-\n11372-[Term]\n11373:id: PATO:0001700\n11374-name: irregular sleep pattern\n11375-def: \"A sleep pattern which has irregular start and/or end times.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11376-subset: value_slim\n--\n11379-\n11380-[Term]\n11381:id: PATO:0001701\n11382-name: mature\n11383-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting complete growth, differentiation, or development.\" [Merriam-Webster:Merriam-Webster]\n11384-subset: value_slim\n--\n11387-\n11388-[Term]\n11389:id: PATO:0001702\n11390-name: saturated violet\n11391-def: \"A color consisting of violet hue and high saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11392-subset: value_slim\n--\n11395-\n11396-[Term]\n11397:id: PATO:0001703\n11398-name: desaturated violet\n11399-def: \"A color consisting of violet hue and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11400-subset: value_slim\n--\n11403-\n11404-[Term]\n11405:id: PATO:0001704\n11406-name: light violet\n11407-def: \"A color consisting of violet hue and high brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11408-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n11411-\n11412-[Term]\n11413:id: PATO:0001705\n11414-name: dark violet\n11415-def: \"A color consisting of violet hue and low brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11416-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n11419-\n11420-[Term]\n11421:id: PATO:0001706\n11422-name: behavioural inactive\n11423-def: \"A behavioral quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to lack activity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11424-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11429-\n11430-[Term]\n11431:id: PATO:0001707\n11432-name: behavioural active\n11433-def: \"A behavioral quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting marked activity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11434-subset: value_slim\n--\n11437-\n11438-[Term]\n11439:id: PATO:0001708\n11440-name: 1-D extent\n11441-def: \"A size quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's extension in one dimension.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11442-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11445-\n11446-[Term]\n11447:id: PATO:0001709\n11448-name: 2-D extent\n11449-def: \"A size quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's extension in two dimensions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11450-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11453-\n11454-[Term]\n11455:id: PATO:0001710\n11456-name: 3-D extent\n11457-def: \"A size quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's extension in three dimensions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11458-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11461-\n11462-[Term]\n11463:id: PATO:0001711\n11464-name: perimeter\n11465-def: \"An 1-D extent quality inhering in two-dimensional bearer by virtue of being equal to the distance around it.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perimeter]\n11466-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11469-\n11470-[Term]\n11471:id: PATO:0001712\n11472-name: increased perimeter\n11473-def: \"A perimeter which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11474-subset: value_slim\n--\n11478-\n11479-[Term]\n11480:id: PATO:0001713\n11481-name: decreased perimeter\n11482-def: \"A perimeter which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11483-subset: value_slim\n--\n11487-\n11488-[Term]\n11489:id: PATO:0001714\n11490-name: increased diameter\n11491-def: \"A diameter which is relatively large.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11492-subset: value_slim\n--\n11496-\n11497-[Term]\n11498:id: PATO:0001715\n11499-name: decreased diameter\n11500-def: \"A diameter which is relatively small.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11501-subset: value_slim\n--\n11505-\n11506-[Term]\n11507:id: PATO:0001716\n11508-name: non-fragile\n11509-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to withstand great strain without tearing or breaking.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n11510-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11517-\n11518-[Term]\n11519:id: PATO:0001717\n11520-name: radiation emitting intensity quality\n11521-def: \"A radiation emitting quality which obtains by the intensity of the bearer emitted radiation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11522-is_a: PATO:0001299 ! radiation emitting quality\n11523-\n11524-[Term]\n11525:id: PATO:0001718\n11526-name: luminance\n11527-def: \"A quality that exists by virtue of the luminous intensity per unit area projected in a given direction.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luminance]\n11528-is_a: PATO:0001296 ! luminous flux\n11529-\n11530-[Term]\n11531:id: PATO:0001719\n11532-name: receptivity\n11533-def: \"A behavioral quality which holds by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits the ability to receive another agentitive entity.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n11534-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11538-\n11539-[Term]\n11540:id: PATO:0001720\n11541-name: female receptivity\n11542-def: \"A behavioral quality which holds by virtue of extent of the receptiveness of a female to male advances.\" [GO:GO]\n11543-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11547-\n11548-[Term]\n11549:id: PATO:0001721\n11550-name: male receptivity\n11551-def: \"A behavioral quality which holds by virtue of extent of the receptiveness of a male to female advances.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11552-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11556-\n11557-[Term]\n11558:id: PATO:0001723\n11559-name: increased female receptivity\n11560-def: \"A female receptivity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11561-subset: relational_slim\n--\n11567-\n11568-[Term]\n11569:id: PATO:0001724\n11570-name: decreased female receptivity\n11571-def: \"A female receptivity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11572-subset: relational_slim\n--\n11578-\n11579-[Term]\n11580:id: PATO:0001725\n11581-name: increased male receptivity\n11582-def: \"A male receptivity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11583-subset: relational_slim\n--\n11589-\n11590-[Term]\n11591:id: PATO:0001726\n11592-name: decreased male receptivity\n11593-def: \"A male receptivity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11594-subset: relational_slim\n--\n11600-\n11601-[Term]\n11602:id: PATO:0001727\n11603-name: disposition\n11604-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's prevailing tendency, mood, or inclination.\" [Merriam-Webster:Merriam-Webster]\n11605-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11610-\n11611-[Term]\n11612:id: PATO:0001728\n11613-name: multi-cellular organismal disposition\n11614-def: \"A disposition inhering in a multi-cellular organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11615-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11618-\n11619-[Term]\n11620:id: PATO:0001729\n11621-name: shedability\n11622-def: \"An organismal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to lose an entity by natural process.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11623-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11627-\n11628-[Term]\n11629:id: PATO:0001730\n11630-name: deciduous (generic)\n11631-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to shed body parts.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11632-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11636-\n11637-[Term]\n11638:id: PATO:0001731\n11639-name: deciduous (plant)\n11640-def: \"A quality inhering in a plant by virtue of the bearer's disposition to shed foliage.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n11641-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11645-\n11646-[Term]\n11647:id: PATO:0001732\n11648-name: non-deciduous (any body part)\n11649-def: \"A quality inhering in a plant by virtue of the bearer's disposition to not shed any body part.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11650-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11654-\n11655-[Term]\n11656:id: PATO:0001733\n11657-name: evergreen (plant)\n11658-def: \"A quality inhering in a plant by virtue of the bearer's disposition to retain foliage.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11659-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11663-\n11664-[Term]\n11665:id: PATO:0001734\n11666-name: semi-deciduous(plant)\n11667-def: \"A quality inhering in a plant by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being between evergeen and deciduous.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n11668-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11672-\n11673-[Term]\n11674:id: PATO:0001735\n11675-name: liquid configuration\n11676-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's parts having the arrangement which exhibits characteristics of liquids.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11677-synonym: \"liquid\" EXACT []\n--\n11679-\n11680-[Term]\n11681:id: PATO:0001736\n11682-name: solid configuration\n11683-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's parts having the arrangement which exhibits characteristics of solids.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11684-subset: value_slim\n--\n11687-\n11688-[Term]\n11689:id: PATO:0001737\n11690-name: gaseus configuration\n11691-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's parts having the arrangement which exhibits characteristics of gases.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11692-synonym: \"gas\" EXACT []\n--\n11694-\n11695-[Term]\n11696:id: PATO:0001738\n11697-name: dissociated from\n11698-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking physically interaction with another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11699-subset: relational_slim\n--\n11703-\n11704-[Term]\n11705:id: PATO:0001739\n11706-name: radiation quality\n11707-def: \"A quality of radiation that reflects the fluence spectrum of charged and neutral particles within the material or medium where dose is being deposited.\" [DOI:10.20348/STOREDB/1173/1250, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5111-7263]\n11708-comment: Radiation quality is often expressed in terms of the linear energy transfer of the ionising particles that deliver the absorbed dose, but this is an over simplification. {xref=\"DOI:10.2307/3570787\"}\n--\n11711-\n11712-[Term]\n11713:id: PATO:0001740\n11714-name: activity (of a radionuclide)\n11715-def: \"A radiation quality inhering in a radioactive substance by virtue of its transformation (disintegration) rate.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11716-comment: See https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/490\n--\n11721-\n11722-[Term]\n11723:id: PATO:0001741\n11724-name: radioactive\n11725-def: \"A radiation quality inhering in bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting or being caused by radioactivity.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n11726-subset: value_slim\n--\n11728-\n11729-[Term]\n11730:id: PATO:0001742\n11731-name: increased radioactivity\n11732-def: \"A radioactivity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11733-subset: value_slim\n--\n11738-\n11739-[Term]\n11740:id: PATO:0001743\n11741-name: decreased radioactivity\n11742-def: \"A radioactivity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11743-subset: value_slim\n--\n11748-\n11749-[Term]\n11750:id: PATO:0001744\n11751-name: irradiated\n11752-def: \"A quality of a substance inhering in a bearer by virtue of it being currently or previously exposed to electromagnetic radiation,\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5111-7263, ISSN:9781496335418]\n11753-comment: This may refer to incident external irradiation or internal radiation from an ingested or otherwise internal source.\n--\n11758-\n11759-[Term]\n11760:id: PATO:0001745\n11761-name: obsolete radiation absorbed dose\n11762-def: \"OBSOLETE A radiation exposure quality inhering in a substance by virtue of the radiation energy \\\"deposited\\\" in a kilogram of a substance.\" [arpansa:arpansa]\n11763-comment: https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/485\n--\n11768-\n11769-[Term]\n11770:id: PATO:0001746\n11771-name: obsolete radiation equivalent dose\n11772-def: \"OBSOLETE A radiation exposure quality inhering in a tissue by virtue of the relation between the absorbed dose to the effective biological damage of the radiation to that tissue.\" [arpansa:arpansa]\n11773-comment: See: https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/485\n--\n11778-\n11779-[Term]\n11780:id: PATO:0001747\n11781-name: obsolete radiation effective dose\n11782-def: \"OBSOLETE A radiation exposure quality inhering in an organ by virtue of the multiplication of an equivalent dose to that organ multiplied by the tissue weighting factor for that organ.\" [arpansa:arpansa]\n11783-comment: See: https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/485\n--\n11788-\n11789-[Term]\n11790:id: PATO:0001748\n11791-name: invaginated\n11792-def: \"A shape quality in which a portion of the outermost boundary of an entity folds in space such that a portion that was originally convex is now concave.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11793-subset: cell_quality\n--\n11797-\n11798-[Term]\n11799:id: PATO:0001749\n11800-name: paedomorphic growth\n11801-def: \"A heterochronic growth quality inhering in an organism, structure, or group of organisms by virtue of the bearer's reduced growth.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11802-subset: value_slim\n--\n11807-\n11808-[Term]\n11809:id: PATO:0001750\n11810-name: postdisplaced growth\n11811-def: \"A paedomorphic growth quality which is due to a delayed onset.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11812-subset: value_slim\n--\n11814-\n11815-[Term]\n11816:id: PATO:0001751\n11817-name: progenetic growth\n11818-def: \"A paedomorphic growth quality which is due to an earlier offset.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11819-subset: value_slim\n--\n11821-\n11822-[Term]\n11823:id: PATO:0001752\n11824-name: peramorphic growth\n11825-def: \"A heterochronic growth quality inhering in an organism, structure, or group of organisms by virtue of the bearer's increased growth.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11826-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11830-\n11831-[Term]\n11832:id: PATO:0001753\n11833-name: accelerated growth\n11834-def: \"A peramorphic growth quality which is due to an increased rate.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11835-subset: value_slim\n--\n11837-\n11838-[Term]\n11839:id: PATO:0001754\n11840-name: predisplaced growth\n11841-def: \"A peramorphic growth quality which is due to an earlier onset.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11842-subset: value_slim\n--\n11845-\n11846-[Term]\n11847:id: PATO:0001755\n11848-name: hypermorphic growth\n11849-def: \"A peramorphic growth quality which is due to a delayed offset.\" [PATOC:mh]\n11850-subset: value_slim\n--\n11852-\n11853-[Term]\n11854:id: PATO:0001756\n11855-name: heat conductivity\n11856-def: \"A conductivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to spontaneous transfer of thermal energy from a region of higher temperature to a region of lower temperature.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_conduction]\n11857-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11862-\n11863-[Term]\n11864:id: PATO:0001757\n11865-name: electrical conductivity\n11866-def: \"A conductivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to convey electricity.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrical_conduction]\n11867-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11871-\n11872-[Term]\n11873:id: PATO:0001758\n11874-name: nerve conductivity\n11875-def: \"A conductivity quality inhering in motor and sensory nerves by virtue of the bearer's ability to convey electricity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11876-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11880-\n11881-[Term]\n11882:id: PATO:0001759\n11883-name: granular\n11884-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing granules.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n11885-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n11888-\n11889-[Term]\n11890:id: PATO:0001760\n11891-name: female semi-fertile\n11892-subset: disposition_slim\n11893-subset: value_slim\n--\n11896-\n11897-[Term]\n11898:id: PATO:0001761\n11899-name: male semi-fertile\n11900-subset: disposition_slim\n11901-subset: value_slim\n--\n11904-\n11905-[Term]\n11906:id: PATO:0001762\n11907-name: male semi-sterile\n11908-subset: disposition_slim\n11909-subset: value_slim\n--\n11912-\n11913-[Term]\n11914:id: PATO:0001763\n11915-name: female semi-sterile\n11916-subset: disposition_slim\n11917-subset: value_slim\n--\n11920-\n11921-[Term]\n11922:id: PATO:0001764\n11923-name: increased age\n11924-def: \"An age which is high relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11925-subset: value_slim\n--\n11930-\n11931-[Term]\n11932:id: PATO:0001765\n11933-name: decreased age\n11934-def: \"An age which is low relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11935-subset: value_slim\n--\n11940-\n11941-[Term]\n11942:id: PATO:0001766\n11943-name: obsolete cellular polarity\n11944-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a cell by virtue of its anisotropic intracellular organization.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n11945-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11949-\n11950-[Term]\n11951:id: PATO:0001767\n11952-name: semi-fertile\n11953-subset: disposition_slim\n11954-subset: value_slim\n--\n11956-\n11957-[Term]\n11958:id: PATO:0001768\n11959-name: semi-lethal (sensu genetics)\n11960-def: \"A viability quality inhering in a bearer or a population by virtue of some of it's members' inability to survive to reproduce.\" [PATOC:CVC]\n11961-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11964-\n11965-[Term]\n11966:id: PATO:0001769\n11967-name: positional polarity\n11968-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location of features or characteristics along an axis.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n11969-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n11972-\n11973-[Term]\n11974:id: PATO:0001770\n11975-name: semi-viable\n11976-def: \"A viability quality inhering in a population by virtue of some of it's members' ability to survive.\" [PATOC:CVC]\n11977-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n11980-\n11981-[Term]\n11982:id: PATO:0001772\n11983-name: surrounding\n11984-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being extended on all sides of another entity simultaneously.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n11985-comment: Nedd to add reciprocal of relationship to 'surrounded by' PATO:0005016.\n--\n11992-\n11993-[Term]\n11994:id: PATO:0001773\n11995-name: monophasic\n11996-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having only one phase or stage.\" [hefreedictionary.com:hefreedictionary.com]\n11997-subset: value_slim\n--\n11999-\n12000-[Term]\n12001:id: PATO:0001774\n12002-name: polyphasic\n12003-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or existing in many phases.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12004-subset: value_slim\n--\n12006-\n12007-[Term]\n12008:id: PATO:0001775\n12009-name: dorsal-ventral polarity\n12010-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location of features or characteristics along the dorsal-ventral axis.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n12011-subset: value_slim\n--\n12013-\n12014-[Term]\n12015:id: PATO:0001776\n12016-name: increased flexibility\n12017-def: \"A flexibility which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12018-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12024-\n12025-[Term]\n12026:id: PATO:0001777\n12027-name: decreased flexibility\n12028-def: \"A flexibility which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12029-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12035-\n12036-[Term]\n12037:id: PATO:0001778\n12038-name: increased strength\n12039-def: \"A strength which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12040-subset: value_slim\n--\n12045-\n12046-[Term]\n12047:id: PATO:0001779\n12048-name: decreased strength\n12049-def: \"A strength which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12050-subset: value_slim\n--\n12055-\n12056-[Term]\n12057:id: PATO:0001780\n12058-name: dystrophic\n12059-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being abnormally developed, usually due to malnutrition.\" [Wiikipedia:Wiikipedia]\n12060-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12065-\n12066-[Term]\n12067:id: PATO:0001781\n12068-name: irregular thickness\n12069-def: \"A thickness quality which lacks pattern.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12070-is_a: PATO:0000915 ! thickness\n12071-\n12072-[Term]\n12073:id: PATO:0001782\n12074-name: increased intensity\n12075-def: \"An intensity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12076-subset: value_slim\n--\n12081-\n12082-[Term]\n12083:id: PATO:0001783\n12084-name: decreased intensity\n12085-def: \"An intensity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12086-subset: value_slim\n--\n12091-\n12092-[Term]\n12093:id: PATO:0001784\n12094-name: bifurcated\n12095-alt_id: PATO:0001572\n12096-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided into two branches.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n--\n12104-\n12105-[Term]\n12106:id: PATO:0001785\n12107-name: splayed\n12108-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outward.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12109-comment: TODO: obsolete, definition too ambiguous.\n--\n12113-\n12114-[Term]\n12115:id: PATO:0001786\n12116-name: split\n12117-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided or broken up into parts or divisions.\" [die.net:die.net]\n12118-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12127-\n12128-[Term]\n12129:id: PATO:0001787\n12130-name: rotational curvature\n12131-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved around an axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12132-subset: value_slim\n--\n12134-\n12135-[Term]\n12136:id: PATO:0001788\n12137-name: increased mass density\n12138-def: \"A density which is higher relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12139-subset: value_slim\n--\n12144-\n12145-[Term]\n12146:id: PATO:0001789\n12147-name: domed\n12148-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape resembling a dome.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12149-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12153-\n12154-[Term]\n12155:id: PATO:0001790\n12156-name: decreased mass density\n12157-def: \"A density which is lower relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12158-subset: value_slim\n--\n12163-\n12164-[Term]\n12165:id: PATO:0001791\n12166-name: multi-localised\n12167-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being confined or restricted to multiple locations.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12168-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12172-\n12173-[Term]\n12174:id: PATO:0001792\n12175-name: left side of\n12176-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located on left side of from the a another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12177-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12181-\n12182-[Term]\n12183:id: PATO:0001793\n12184-name: right side of\n12185-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located on right side of a another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12186-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12190-\n12191-[Term]\n12192:id: PATO:0001794\n12193-name: coiling\n12194-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being wound in a continuous series of loops.\" [Online_Dictionary:Online_Dictionary]\n12195-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12197-\n12198-[Term]\n12199:id: PATO:0001795\n12200-name: increased coiling\n12201-def: \"A coiling which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12202-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12208-\n12209-[Term]\n12210:id: PATO:0001796\n12211-name: decreased coiling\n12212-def: \"A coiling which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12213-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12219-\n12220-[Term]\n12221:id: PATO:0001798\n12222-name: kinked\n12223-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having multiple angles in its length.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n12224-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12229-\n12230-[Term]\n12231:id: PATO:0001799\n12232-name: ruffled\n12233-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting disturbance of its smoothness or regularity.\" [.thefreedictionary.com:.thefreedictionary.com]\n12234-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12237-\n12238-[Term]\n12239:id: PATO:0001800\n12240-name: water composition\n12241-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the quantities or relative ratios of water of the inhering entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12242-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12245-\n12246-[Term]\n12247:id: PATO:0001801\n12248-name: decreased water composition\n12249-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the reduction in amount of water the bearer contains.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dehydrated]\n12250-subset: value_slim\n--\n12255-\n12256-[Term]\n12257:id: PATO:0001802\n12258-name: loose\n12259-def: \"A pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not being compact or dense in arrangement.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12260-subset: value_slim\n--\n12262-\n12263-[Term]\n12264:id: PATO:0001803\n12265-name: phototoxic\n12266-def: \"A photosensitivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being susceptible to damage by light.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12267-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12270-\n12271-[Term]\n12272:id: PATO:0001804\n12273-name: scaly\n12274-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being covered or partially covered with scales.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12275-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12279-\n12280-[Term]\n12281:id: PATO:0001805\n12282-name: flaky\n12283-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's formed or tending to form flakes or thin, crisp fragments.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12284-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12287-\n12288-[Term]\n12289:id: PATO:0001806\n12290-name: sensitivity to irradiation\n12291-def: \"A sensitivity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exposure to radiation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12292-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12296-\n12297-[Term]\n12298:id: PATO:0001807\n12299-name: decreased sensitivity to irradiation\n12300-def: \"A sensitivity to irradiation which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12301-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12307-\n12308-[Term]\n12309:id: PATO:0001808\n12310-name: increased sensitivity to irradiation\n12311-def: \"A sensitivity to irradiation which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12312-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12318-\n12319-[Term]\n12320:id: PATO:0001809\n12321-name: tight\n12322-def: \"A pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being compact or dense in arrangement.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12323-subset: value_slim\n--\n12325-\n12326-[Term]\n12327:id: PATO:0001810\n12328-name: wrinkled\n12329-def: \"A grooved texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by one or more creases in a normally smooth surface.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/wrinkled]\n12330-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12333-\n12334-[Term]\n12335:id: PATO:0001811\n12336-name: obsolete increased relaxation\n12337-def: \"A relaxation which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12338-comment: GO has now relevant relation terms which should be used instead.\n--\n12342-\n12343-[Term]\n12344:id: PATO:0001812\n12345-name: obsolete decreased relaxation\n12346-def: \"A relaxation which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12347-comment: GO has now relevant relation terms which should be used instead.\n--\n12351-\n12352-[Term]\n12353:id: PATO:0001813\n12354-name: atonicity\n12355-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lack elastic tension that facilitate response to stimuli.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12356-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12359-\n12360-[Term]\n12361:id: PATO:0001814\n12362-name: dystonicity\n12363-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's impaired elastic tension that facilitate response to stimuli.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12364-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12367-\n12368-[Term]\n12369:id: PATO:0001815\n12370-name: fatigability\n12371-def: \"A strength quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to lose strength.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n12372-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12376-\n12377-[Term]\n12378:id: PATO:0001816\n12379-name: increased fatigability\n12380-def: \"A fatigability which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12381-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12387-\n12388-[Term]\n12389:id: PATO:0001817\n12390-name: decreased fatigability\n12391-def: \"A fatigability which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12392-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12398-\n12399-[Term]\n12400:id: PATO:0001818\n12401-name: progressive\n12402-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's increasing over time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12403-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n12408-\n12409-[Term]\n12410:id: PATO:0001819\n12411-name: atretic\n12412-def: \"A morphological quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's absence or closure of a normal body orifice or tubular passage.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12413-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12417-\n12418-[Term]\n12419:id: PATO:0001821\n12420-name: imperforate\n12421-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having no opening.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n12422-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12427-\n12428-[Term]\n12429:id: PATO:0001822\n12430-name: wetness\n12431-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer's being covered by a liquid.\" [wordreference.com:wordreference.com]\n12432-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12436-\n12437-[Term]\n12438:id: PATO:0001823\n12439-name: wet\n12440-def: \"A wetness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being covered by a liquid.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12441-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12446-\n12447-[Term]\n12448:id: PATO:0001824\n12449-name: dry\n12450-def: \"A wetness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not being covered by a liquid.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12451-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12455-\n12456-[Term]\n12457:id: PATO:0001825\n12458-name: increased wetness\n12459-def: \"A wetness quality that is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12460-subset: value_slim\n--\n12464-\n12465-[Term]\n12466:id: PATO:0001826\n12467-name: decreased wetness\n12468-def: \"A wetness quality that is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12469-subset: value_slim\n--\n12474-\n12475-[Term]\n12476:id: PATO:0001827\n12477-name: pseudohermaphrodite\n12478-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population by virtue of having internal reproductive organs of one sex and external sexual characteristics of the other sex.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n12479-subset: value_slim\n--\n12481-\n12482-[Term]\n12483:id: PATO:0001828\n12484-name: male pseudohermaphrodite\n12485-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population by virtue of having internal reproductive organs of male and external sexual characteristics of female.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12486-subset: value_slim\n--\n12488-\n12489-[Term]\n12490:id: PATO:0001829\n12491-name: female pseudohermaphrodite\n12492-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population by virtue of having internal reproductive organs of female and external sexual characteristics of male.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12493-subset: value_slim\n--\n12495-\n12496-[Term]\n12497:id: PATO:0001830\n12498-name: decreased female fertility\n12499-def: \"A female fertility which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12500-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12506-\n12507-[Term]\n12508:id: PATO:0001831\n12509-name: increased female fertility\n12510-def: \"A female fertility which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12511-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12517-\n12518-[Term]\n12519:id: PATO:0001832\n12520-name: increased male fertility\n12521-def: \"A male fertility which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12522-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12528-\n12529-[Term]\n12530:id: PATO:0001833\n12531-name: decreased male fertility\n12532-def: \"A male fertility which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12533-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12539-\n12540-[Term]\n12541:id: PATO:0001834\n12542-name: decreased fertility\n12543-def: \"A fertility which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12544-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12550-\n12551-[Term]\n12552:id: PATO:0001835\n12553-name: increased fertility\n12554-def: \"A fertility which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12555-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12561-\n12562-[Term]\n12563:id: PATO:0001836\n12564-name: congested\n12565-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer with some kind of aperture or opening that is blocked or clogged.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12566-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12569-\n12570-[Term]\n12571:id: PATO:0001838\n12572-name: decreased fluid flow\n12573-def: \"A flow that is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12574-subset: value_slim\n--\n12579-\n12580-[Term]\n12581:id: PATO:0001839\n12582-name: increased fluid flow\n12583-def: \"A fluid flow that is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12584-subset: value_slim\n--\n12589-\n12590-[Term]\n12591:id: PATO:0001841\n12592-name: remittent intensity\n12593-def: \"An intensity which is characterized by temporary abatement in severity.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12594-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n12598-\n12599-[Term]\n12600:id: PATO:0001842\n12601-name: acidity\n12602-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing acid (hydrogen ions).\" [biology-online:biology-online]\n12603-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12607-\n12608-[Term]\n12609:id: PATO:0001843\n12610-name: decreased acidity\n12611-def: \"An acidity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12612-subset: value_slim\n--\n12618-\n12619-[Term]\n12620:id: PATO:0001844\n12621-name: increased acidity\n12622-def: \"An acidity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12623-subset: value_slim\n--\n12629-\n12630-[Term]\n12631:id: PATO:0001845\n12632-name: irregular rhythm\n12633-def: \"A rhythm quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking rhythm lacking pattern.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12634-subset: value_slim\n--\n12636-\n12637-[Term]\n12638:id: PATO:0001846\n12639-name: tangled\n12640-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being entwined and difficult to unravel.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12641-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12644-\n12645-[Term]\n12646:id: PATO:0001847\n12647-name: constricted\n12648-alt_id: PATO:0001837\n12649-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being drawn together, compressed or squeezed physically.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n--\n12655-\n12656-[Term]\n12657:id: PATO:0001848\n12658-name: asymmetrically curved\n12659-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved asymmetrically.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12660-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12663-\n12664-[Term]\n12665:id: PATO:0001849\n12666-name: abrased\n12667-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of a portion of the bearer's surface being scraped away.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12668-subset: value_slim\n--\n12670-\n12671-[Term]\n12672:id: PATO:0001850\n12673-name: scarred\n12674-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being fibrous tissue that replaces normal tissue destroyed by injury or disease.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12675-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12678-\n12679-[Term]\n12680:id: PATO:0001851\n12681-name: swollen\n12682-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting transient abnormal enlargement, not due to cell proliferation.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n12683-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12689-\n12690-[Term]\n12691:id: PATO:0001852\n12692-name: dislocated\n12693-alt_id: PATO:0001479\n12694-alt_id: PATO:0002158\n--\n12704-\n12705-[Term]\n12706:id: PATO:0001853\n12707-name: hydrocephalic\n12708-def: \"A structural quality which is held by a bearer when the latter exhibits an excessive accumulation of cerebral spinal fluid.\" [PATOC:mh]\n12709-subset: value_slim\n--\n12711-\n12712-[Term]\n12713:id: PATO:0001854\n12714-name: vertical\n12715-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being situated at right angles to the horizon.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n12716-subset: value_slim\n--\n12718-\n12719-[Term]\n12720:id: PATO:0001855\n12721-name: horizontal\n12722-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in the plane of the horizon.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n12723-subset: value_slim\n--\n12725-\n12726-[Term]\n12727:id: PATO:0001856\n12728-name: introverted\n12729-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being turned inward upon itself.\" [die.net:die.net]\n12730-comment: For example, a tubular organ or part.\n--\n12733-\n12734-[Term]\n12735:id: PATO:0001857\n12736-name: concave\n12737-def: \"A shape quality in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's curving inward.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n12738-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12742-\n12743-[Term]\n12744:id: PATO:0001858\n12745-name: partially paralysed\n12746-def: \"A functionality quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being not completely paralysed.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12747-subset: value_slim\n--\n12749-\n12750-[Term]\n12751:id: PATO:0001859\n12752-name: increased coordination\n12753-def: \"A coordination which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12754-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12760-\n12761-[Term]\n12762:id: PATO:0001860\n12763-name: decreased coordination\n12764-def: \"A coordination which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12765-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12771-\n12772-[Term]\n12773:id: PATO:0001861\n12774-name: fasciculated\n12775-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's forming a bundle of aligned anatomical fibers, as of muscle or nerve.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n12776-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n12782-\n12783-[Term]\n12784:id: PATO:0001862\n12785-name: lack of fertility in offspring\n12786-def: \"A fertility quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to make its offspring sterile.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12787-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n12791-\n12792-[Term]\n12793:id: PATO:0001863\n12794-name: chronic\n12795-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having slow progressive course of indefinite duration.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n12796-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n12801-\n12802-[Term]\n12803:id: PATO:0001865\n12804-name: spheroid\n12805-alt_id: PATO:0001864\n12806-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a quadric surface in three dimensions obtained by rotating an ellipse about one of its principal axes. Includes spheres and oblate/prolate spheroids.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spheroid]\n--\n12812-\n12813-[Term]\n12814:id: PATO:0001866\n12815-name: prolate\n12816-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a polar diameter longer than its equatorial diameter.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prolate]\n12817-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12822-\n12823-[Term]\n12824:id: PATO:0001867\n12825-name: rectangular\n12826-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of it being a quadrilateral polygon in which all four angles are right angles.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectangular]\n12827-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12831-\n12832-[Term]\n12833:id: PATO:0001868\n12834-name: autofluorescence\n12835-def: \"A fluorescence quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting fluorescence which is self-induced.\" [PATOC:mb]\n12836-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12838-\n12839-[Term]\n12840:id: PATO:0001869\n12841-name: pathological\n12842-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being abnormal and having a destructive effect on living tissue.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n12843-subset: abnormal_slim\n--\n12846-\n12847-[Term]\n12848:id: PATO:0001870\n12849-name: crescent-shaped\n12850-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a circular disk by virtue of the bearer's having a segment of another circle removed from its edge, so that what remains is a shape enclosed by two circular arcs of different diameters which intersect at two points (usually in such a manner that the enclosed shape does not include the center of the original circle).\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent]\n12851-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12858-\n12859-[Term]\n12860:id: PATO:0001871\n12861-name: reniform\n12862-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having the shape of a kidney.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n12863-subset: value_slim\n--\n12867-\n12868-[Term]\n12869:id: PATO:0001872\n12870-name: cuboid\n12871-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resemblance to a cube (a 3-D shape with a square cross section).\" [PATOC:MAH]\n12872-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12878-\n12879-[Term]\n12880:id: PATO:0001873\n12881-name: cylindrical\n12882-alt_id: PATO:0001203\n12883-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a consistently-sized round cross section.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n--\n12891-\n12892-[Term]\n12893:id: PATO:0001874\n12894-name: discoid\n12895-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being cylindrical, in which the height is less than the diameter.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n12896-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12901-\n12902-[Term]\n12903:id: PATO:0001875\n12904-name: triangular\n12905-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having three angles.\" [wordreference:wordreference]\n12906-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12913-\n12914-[Term]\n12915:id: PATO:0001876\n12916-name: dumbbell-shaped\n12917-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two parts, roughly spherical and of equal size, connected by a bar.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12918-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12921-\n12922-[Term]\n12923:id: PATO:0001877\n12924-name: lanceolate\n12925-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a lance-head, considerably longer than wide, tapering towards the tip from below the middle; attached at the broad end.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n12926-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12930-\n12931-[Term]\n12932:id: PATO:0001878\n12933-name: sigmoid\n12934-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of two curves, in opposite directions. S-shaped.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n12935-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12940-\n12941-[Term]\n12942:id: PATO:0001879\n12943-name: U-shaped\n12944-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of the letter U.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n12945-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12950-\n12951-[Term]\n12952:id: PATO:0001880\n12953-name: caudate\n12954-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a tail or tail-like projection.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n12955-subset: value_slim\n--\n12959-\n12960-[Term]\n12961:id: PATO:0001881\n12962-name: arrow-shaped\n12963-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's forming two equal obtuse triangles with a short side in common.\" [ISBN:0881923214, RKC:RKC]\n12964-comment: Gradually enlarged at the base, like the head of an arrow.\n--\n12969-\n12970-[Term]\n12971:id: PATO:0001882\n12972-name: limaciform\n12973-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a slug.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n12974-subset: cell_quality\n--\n12977-\n12978-[Term]\n12979:id: PATO:0001883\n12980-name: clavate\n12981-alt_id: PATO:0001797\n12982-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gradually becoming thicker towards the end.\" [MP:0000576]\n--\n12988-\n12989-[Term]\n12990:id: PATO:0001884\n12991-name: hydrophobicity\n12992-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's disposition to being water-repellent; tending to repel and not absorb water.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n12993-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n12998-\n12999-[Term]\n13000:id: PATO:0001885\n13001-name: hydrophobic\n13002-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking affinity for water; tending to repel and not absorb water; tending not to dissolve in or mix with or be wetted by water.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n13003-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n13007-\n13008-[Term]\n13009:id: PATO:0001886\n13010-name: hydrophilicity\n13011-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's disposition to having an affinity for water; it is readily absorbing or dissolving in water.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n13012-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13016-\n13017-[Term]\n13018:id: PATO:0001887\n13019-name: hydrophilic\n13020-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to having a strong affinity for water; tending to dissolve in, mix with, or be wetted by water.\" [WordNet:WordNet]\n13021-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n13025-\n13026-[Term]\n13027:id: PATO:0001888\n13028-name: miscibility\n13029-def: \"A quality of a liquid inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to mix with (dissolve in) another liquid.\" [Chemicool:Chemicool]\n13030-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13033-\n13034-[Term]\n13035:id: PATO:0001889\n13036-name: scalloped\n13037-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having the border, edge, or outline cut into a series of segments of circles resembling a scallop-shell.\" [Oxford:EnglishDictionary]\n13038-subset: cell_quality\n--\n13043-\n13044-[Term]\n13045:id: PATO:0001890\n13046-name: tripartite\n13047-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided into three branches.\" [InfoVisual:InfoVisual]\n13048-subset: cell_quality\n--\n13053-\n13054-[Term]\n13055:id: PATO:0001891\n13056-name: ovate\n13057-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a continuous convex surface with an axis of symmetry and one axis longer than the other; egg-shaped.\" [PATOC:mc]\n13058-subset: cell_quality\n--\n13067-\n13068-[Term]\n13069:id: PATO:0001892\n13070-name: decreased odor\n13071-def: \"An odor quality of having decreased odor.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13072-subset: value_slim\n--\n13076-\n13077-[Term]\n13078:id: PATO:0001893\n13079-name: increased odor\n13080-def: \"An odor quality of having increased odor.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13081-subset: value_slim\n--\n13085-\n13086-[Term]\n13087:id: PATO:0001894\n13088-name: phenotypic sex\n13089-def: \"An organismal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's physical expression of sexual characteristics.\" []\n13090-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13092-\n13093-[Term]\n13094:id: PATO:0001895\n13095-name: mating type\n13096-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population that undergo sexual reproduction.\" [wikipedia:wikipedia]\n13097-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13099-\n13100-[Term]\n13101:id: PATO:0001896\n13102-name: unlumenized\n13103-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking of a three dimensional space surrounded by one or more anatomical structures and containing one or more anatomical substances.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13104-subset: value_slim\n--\n13107-\n13108-[Term]\n13109:id: PATO:0001897\n13110-name: lumenized\n13111-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a three dimensional space surrounded by one or more anatomical structures and containing one or more anatomical substances.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13112-comment: See GO term: GO:0031974 membrane-enclosed lumen [DEF:\"The enclosed volume within a sealed membrane or between two sealed membranes\"].\n--\n13116-\n13117-[Term]\n13118:id: PATO:0001898\n13119-name: increased circumference\n13120-def: \"A circumference which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13121-subset: value_slim\n--\n13125-\n13126-[Term]\n13127:id: PATO:0001899\n13128-name: decreased circumference\n13129-def: \"A circumference which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13130-subset: value_slim\n--\n13134-\n13135-[Term]\n13136:id: PATO:0001900\n13137-name: front\n13138-def: \"A directional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's direction that is similar to the direction of an object to the south when it faces north.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13139-subset: value_slim\n--\n13142-\n13143-[Term]\n13144:id: PATO:0001901\n13145-name: back\n13146-def: \"A directional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's direction that is similar to the direction of an object to the north when it faces south.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13147-subset: value_slim\n--\n13150-\n13151-[Term]\n13152:id: PATO:0001902\n13153-name: unidirectional\n13154-def: \"A directional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one direction only.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13155-subset: value_slim\n--\n13157-\n13158-[Term]\n13159:id: PATO:0001903\n13160-name: bi-directional\n13161-def: \"A directional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two directions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13162-subset: value_slim\n--\n13164-\n13165-[Term]\n13166:id: PATO:0001904\n13167-name: circling direction\n13168-def: \"A directional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's direction approximating the shape of a circle.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13169-subset: value_slim\n--\n13171-\n13172-[Term]\n13173:id: PATO:0001905\n13174-name: has normal numbers of parts of type\n13175-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part = n, where n is the normal amount for a comparable organism. Note that the bearer of the quality is the whole, not the part.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13176-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13180-\n13181-[Term]\n13182:id: PATO:0001906\n13183-name: movement quality\n13184-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's participation in movement.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13185-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13187-\n13188-[Term]\n13189:id: PATO:0001907\n13190-name: botryoidal\n13191-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being like the surface of a compact mass of grapes.\" [PATOC:cvs]\n13192-subset: value_slim\n--\n13194-\n13195-[Term]\n13196:id: PATO:0001908\n13197-name: multinucleate\n13198-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having more than one nucleus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13199-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13202-\n13203-[Term]\n13204:id: PATO:0001909\n13205-name: trinucleate\n13206-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having three nuclei.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n13207-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13210-\n13211-[Term]\n13212:id: PATO:0001910\n13213-name: folded\n13214-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's one part being layered over another connected part.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n13215-subset: value_slim\n--\n13217-\n13218-[Term]\n13219:id: PATO:0001911\n13220-name: circling\n13221-def: \"A behavioral quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting movement in a circular course.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13222-subset: value_slim\n--\n13224-\n13225-[Term]\n13226:id: PATO:0001912\n13227-name: physiological state\n13228-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the state of bearer's mechanical, physical, and biochemical processes.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13229-is_a: PATO:0001236 ! process quality\n13230-\n13231-[Term]\n13232:id: PATO:0001913\n13233-name: ictal\n13234-def: \"A physiological state which is characterized by periods of high-frequency high amplitude electrical activity in neuronal tissue.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13235-is_a: PATO:0001912 ! physiological state\n13236-\n13237-[Term]\n13238:id: PATO:0001914\n13239-name: non-ictal\n13240-def: \"A physiological state which is characterized by normal electrical activity in neuronal tissue.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13241-is_a: PATO:0001912 ! physiological state\n13242-\n13243-[Term]\n13244:id: PATO:0001915\n13245-name: anterodorsal to\n13246-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the front and upper surface of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:wd]\n13247-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13250-\n13251-[Term]\n13252:id: PATO:0001916\n13253-name: posterodorsal to\n13254-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the rear and upper surface of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:wd]\n13255-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13258-\n13259-[Term]\n13260:id: PATO:0001917\n13261-name: anteroventral to\n13262-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the front and abdomen of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:wd]\n13263-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13266-\n13267-[Term]\n13268:id: PATO:0001918\n13269-name: posteroventral to\n13270-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the rear and abdomen of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:wd]\n13271-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13274-\n13275-[Term]\n13276:id: PATO:0001919\n13277-name: mislocalised dorsally\n13278-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the back or upper surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13279-subset: value_slim\n--\n13281-\n13282-[Term]\n13283:id: PATO:0001920\n13284-name: mislocalised ventrally\n13285-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the abdomen of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13286-subset: value_slim\n--\n13288-\n13289-[Term]\n13290:id: PATO:0001921\n13291-name: mislocalised anteriorly\n13292-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the front of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13293-subset: value_slim\n--\n13295-\n13296-[Term]\n13297:id: PATO:0001922\n13298-name: mislocalised posteriorly\n13299-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the rear of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13300-subset: value_slim\n--\n13302-\n13303-[Term]\n13304:id: PATO:0001923\n13305-name: mislocalised laterally\n13306-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the side of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13307-subset: value_slim\n--\n13309-\n13310-[Term]\n13311:id: PATO:0001924\n13312-name: mislocalised medially\n13313-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the middle of an organism.\" [PATOC:mb]\n13314-subset: value_slim\n--\n13316-\n13317-[Term]\n13318:id: PATO:0001925\n13319-name: surface feature shape\n13320-def: \"A surface shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape of features present on its surface or outer shell.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13321-comment: This quality either inheres directly in the surface, or in the entity that has the surface. For example, to say that a particular fly wing is curved is shorthand for saying the wing has a surface which is curved.\n--\n13324-\n13325-[Term]\n13326:id: PATO:0001926\n13327-name: increased fluorescence\n13328-def: \"A fluorescence which is higher than normal.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13329-subset: value_slim\n--\n13334-\n13335-[Term]\n13336:id: PATO:0001927\n13337-name: decreased fluorescence\n13338-def: \"A fluorescence which is lower than normal.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13339-subset: value_slim\n--\n13344-\n13345-[Term]\n13346:id: PATO:0001928\n13347-name: blistered\n13348-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of a local accumulation of fluid underneath the surface of the bearer.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13349-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13353-\n13354-[Term]\n13355:id: PATO:0001929\n13356-name: variability of shape\n13357-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits shape variation or change.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13358-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13361-\n13362-[Term]\n13363:id: PATO:0001930\n13364-name: variant shape\n13365-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's having or exhibiting variation its shape.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13366-subset: value_slim\n--\n13369-\n13370-[Term]\n13371:id: PATO:0001931\n13372-name: invariant shape\n13373-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking or not exhibiting variation of shape.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13374-subset: value_slim\n--\n13377-\n13378-[Term]\n13379:id: PATO:0001932\n13380-name: alternate placement\n13381-def: \"A pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being placed alternately one above the other.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13382-subset: value_slim\n--\n13384-\n13385-[Term]\n13386:id: PATO:0001933\n13387-name: opposite\n13388-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned on opposite sides on the same plane.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13389-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13392-\n13393-[Term]\n13394:id: PATO:0001934\n13395-name: orbicular\n13396-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being perfectly circular.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13397-subset: value_slim\n--\n13399-\n13400-[Term]\n13401:id: PATO:0001935\n13402-name: obtuse\n13403-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being roundish, a little inclining to be oblong.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13404-subset: value_slim\n--\n13407-\n13408-[Term]\n13409:id: PATO:0001936\n13410-name: obovate\n13411-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being egg-shaped and flat, with the narrow end attached to the base.\" [wordreference:wordreference]\n13412-subset: value_slim\n--\n13415-\n13416-[Term]\n13417:id: PATO:0001937\n13418-name: spatulate\n13419-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being oblong, with the lower end very much attenuated.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13420-subset: value_slim\n--\n13423-\n13424-[Term]\n13425:id: PATO:0001938\n13426-name: rhomboid\n13427-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being oval and a little angular in the middle.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13428-subset: value_slim\n--\n13430-\n13431-[Term]\n13432:id: PATO:0001940\n13433-name: gigantic\n13434-def: \"A size quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being many folds greater relative to the normal average.\" [PATOC:UMH]\n13435-subset: value_slim\n--\n13438-\n13439-[Term]\n13440:id: PATO:0001941\n13441-name: yellow green\n13442-def: \"A color consisting of yellow and green hues.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13443-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13446-\n13447-[Term]\n13448:id: PATO:0001942\n13449-name: brown green\n13450-def: \"A color consisting of brown and green hues.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13451-synonym: \"olive green\" EXACT []\n--\n13453-\n13454-[Term]\n13455:id: PATO:0001943\n13456-name: lilac\n13457-def: \"A purple color which has low saturation and low brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13458-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13461-\n13462-[Term]\n13463:id: PATO:0001944\n13464-name: yellow orange\n13465-def: \"A color consisting of yellow and orange hue.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13466-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13469-\n13470-[Term]\n13471:id: PATO:0001945\n13472-name: ochre\n13473-def: \"A moderate yellow-orange to orange color.\" [wordreference:wordreference]\n13474-subset: value_slim\n--\n13476-\n13477-[Term]\n13478:id: PATO:0001946\n13479-name: banded\n13480-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's exhibiting transverse stripes of one hue or degree of saturation crossing another.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13481-subset: value_slim\n--\n13484-\n13485-[Term]\n13486:id: PATO:0001947\n13487-name: netted\n13488-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's being covered with reticulated lines of a different hue or degree of saturation.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13489-subset: value_slim\n--\n13493-\n13494-[Term]\n13495:id: PATO:0001948\n13496-name: furrowed\n13497-def: \"A grooved texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by two or more parallel channels.\" [PATOC:JE]\n13498-subset: value_slim\n--\n13501-\n13502-[Term]\n13503:id: PATO:0001949\n13504-name: pointleted\n13505-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's terminating abruptly in a little point.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13506-subset: value_slim\n--\n13508-\n13509-[Term]\n13510:id: PATO:0001950\n13511-name: blunt\n13512-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's terminating gradually in a rounded end.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13513-subset: value_slim\n--\n13515-\n13516-[Term]\n13517:id: PATO:0001951\n13518-name: whorled\n13519-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in opposition round a common axis.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13520-subset: value_slim\n--\n13522-\n13523-[Term]\n13524:id: PATO:0001952\n13525-name: distichous\n13526-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being arranged in two opposite rows (and hence in the same plane).\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13527-subset: value_slim\n--\n13529-\n13530-[Term]\n13531:id: PATO:0001953\n13532-name: decussate\n13533-def: \"A pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of paired parts that alternately cross each other.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13534-subset: value_slim\n--\n13539-\n13540-[Term]\n13541:id: PATO:0001954\n13542-name: subulate\n13543-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being linear, very narrow, tapering to a very fine point from a narrow base.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13544-subset: value_slim\n--\n13548-\n13549-[Term]\n13550:id: PATO:0001955\n13551-name: cuneate\n13552-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being narrowly triangular, wider at the apex and tapering toward the base.\" [wordreference:wordreference]\n13553-subset: value_slim\n--\n13556-\n13557-[Term]\n13558:id: PATO:0001956\n13559-name: variability of size\n13560-def: \"A variability quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits size variation or change.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13561-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13564-\n13565-[Term]\n13566:id: PATO:0001957\n13567-name: decreased variability of size\n13568-def: \"A variability of size which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13569-subset: value_slim\n--\n13574-\n13575-[Term]\n13576:id: PATO:0001958\n13577-name: increased variability of size\n13578-def: \"A variability of size which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13579-subset: value_slim\n--\n13584-\n13585-[Term]\n13586:id: PATO:0001959\n13587-name: defasciculated\n13588-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's in which bundles of aligned anatomical fibers have become separated.\" [PATOC:mw]\n13589-subset: value_slim\n--\n13592-\n13593-[Term]\n13594:id: PATO:0001960\n13595-name: interdigitated\n13596-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's parts or projections being interlocked; for example, the fingers of two hands that are clasped.\" [PATOC:wdahdul]\n13597-subset: value_slim\n--\n13599-\n13600-[Term]\n13601:id: PATO:0001961\n13602-name: in contact with\n13603-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's touching another entity.\" [PATOC:wdahdul]\n13604-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13608-\n13609-[Term]\n13610:id: PATO:0001962\n13611-name: involute\n13612-def: \"A curled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's edges of its surface being rolled inwards spirally on each side.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13613-subset: value_slim\n--\n13615-\n13616-[Term]\n13617:id: PATO:0001963\n13618-name: revolute\n13619-def: \"A curled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's edges of its surface being rolled backwards spirally on each side.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13620-subset: value_slim\n--\n13622-\n13623-[Term]\n13624:id: PATO:0001964\n13625-name: circinate\n13626-def: \"A curled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's edges of its surface being rolled spirally downwards.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13627-subset: value_slim\n--\n13629-\n13630-[Term]\n13631:id: PATO:0001965\n13632-name: reclinate\n13633-def: \"A curled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's edges of its surface being bent down upon their stalk.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13634-subset: value_slim\n--\n13636-\n13637-[Term]\n13638:id: PATO:0001966\n13639-name: convolute\n13640-def: \"A curled quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's one edge of its surface being wholly rolled up in another.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13641-subset: value_slim\n--\n13643-\n13644-[Term]\n13645:id: PATO:0001967\n13646-name: actinodromous\n13647-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having three or more primary branches diverging radially from a single point.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13648-subset: value_slim\n--\n13650-\n13651-[Term]\n13652:id: PATO:0001968\n13653-name: parallelodromous\n13654-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two or more parallel primary branches originate beside each other and converge apically.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13655-subset: value_slim\n--\n13657-\n13658-[Term]\n13659:id: PATO:0001969\n13660-name: craspedodromous\n13661-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having secondary branches terminating at the margin.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13662-subset: value_slim\n--\n13664-\n13665-[Term]\n13666:id: PATO:0001970\n13667-name: brochidodromous\n13668-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having secondary branches joined together in a series of prominent arches.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13669-subset: value_slim\n--\n13671-\n13672-[Term]\n13673:id: PATO:0001971\n13674-name: cladodromous\n13675-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having secondary branches freely branching toward the margin.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13676-subset: value_slim\n--\n13678-\n13679-[Term]\n13680:id: PATO:0001972\n13681-name: reticulodromous\n13682-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having secondary branches branching into a reticulum toward the margin.\" [Hickey:1988]\n13683-subset: value_slim\n--\n13685-\n13686-[Term]\n13687:id: PATO:0001973\n13688-name: cuspidate\n13689-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being tapering gradually into a rigid point.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13690-subset: value_slim\n--\n13692-\n13693-[Term]\n13694:id: PATO:0001974\n13695-name: retuse\n13696-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's terminating in a round end, the centre of which is depressed.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13697-subset: value_slim\n--\n13699-\n13700-[Term]\n13701:id: PATO:0001975\n13702-name: unserrated\n13703-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking sharp straight-edged teeth pointing to the apex.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13704-subset: value_slim\n--\n13708-\n13709-[Term]\n13710:id: PATO:0001976\n13711-name: serration\n13712-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or lacking sharp straight-edged teeth pointing to the apex.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13713-subset: value_slim\n--\n13715-\n13716-[Term]\n13717:id: PATO:0001977\n13718-name: angular\n13719-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having at least one salient angle on the margin.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13720-subset: value_slim\n--\n13723-\n13724-[Term]\n13725:id: PATO:0001978\n13726-name: cut\n13727-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being regularly divided by deep incisions.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13728-subset: value_slim\n--\n13731-\n13732-[Term]\n13733:id: PATO:0001979\n13734-name: lobed\n13735-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being partly divided into a determinate number of regions.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13736-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n13739-\n13740-[Term]\n13741:id: PATO:0001980\n13742-name: digitate\n13743-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having distinct parts arising from a common point or center.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n13744-subset: value_slim\n--\n13746-\n13747-[Term]\n13748:id: PATO:0001981\n13749-name: auriculate\n13750-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape resembling an ear.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/auriculate]\n13751-subset: value_slim\n--\n13753-\n13754-[Term]\n13755:id: PATO:0001982\n13756-name: attenuate\n13757-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gradually tapering to a slender point.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/attenuate]\n13758-subset: value_slim\n--\n13760-\n13761-[Term]\n13762:id: PATO:0001983\n13763-name: perfoliate\n13764-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's two basal lobes being united together.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13765-subset: value_slim\n--\n13767-\n13768-[Term]\n13769:id: PATO:0001984\n13770-name: decurrent\n13771-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being prolonged below the point of insertion.\" [ISBN:0881923214]\n13772-subset: value_slim\n--\n13774-\n13775-[Term]\n13776:id: PATO:0001985\n13777-name: frozen\n13778-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being kept below its freezing point.\" [OBI:OBI]\n13779-subset: value_slim\n--\n13781-\n13782-[Term]\n13783:id: PATO:0001986\n13784-name: dissolved\n13785-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's passing into solution.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13786-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13789-\n13790-[Term]\n13791:id: PATO:0001987\n13792-name: saccular\n13793-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a three dimensional cavity with a narrow or no opening, and often containing an anatomical substance.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13794-subset: value_slim\n--\n13797-\n13798-[Term]\n13799:id: PATO:0001988\n13800-name: quadrangular\n13801-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having four angles and four sides.\" [url:http\\://www.oed.com/]\n13802-subset: value_slim\n--\n13804-\n13805-[Term]\n13806:id: PATO:0001989\n13807-name: sinuous\n13808-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having many curves and turns.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13809-subset: value_slim\n--\n13812-\n13813-[Term]\n13814:id: PATO:0001990\n13815-name: duration of disease\n13816-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a disease by virtue of the bearer's duration of an impairment of health or of a condition of abnormal functioning.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13817-comment: MAH: I think this term should be obsoleted. Is it used?\n--\n13819-\n13820-[Term]\n13821:id: PATO:0001991\n13822-name: immortal\n13823-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being capable of indefinite growth or division.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n13824-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n13827-\n13828-[Term]\n13829:id: PATO:0001992\n13830-name: cellularity\n13831-def: \"An organismal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting cells.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13832-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13835-\n13836-[Term]\n13837:id: PATO:0001993\n13838-name: multicellular\n13839-def: \"A cellularity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of more than one cell.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13840-subset: value_slim\n--\n13843-\n13844-[Term]\n13845:id: PATO:0001994\n13846-name: unicellular\n13847-def: \"A cellularity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of exactly one cell.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13848-subset: value_slim\n--\n13850-\n13851-[Term]\n13852:id: PATO:0001995\n13853-name: organismal quality\n13854-def: \"A quality that inheres in an entire organism or part of an organism.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13855-is_a: PATO:0001241 ! physical object quality\n--\n13857-\n13858-[Term]\n13859:id: PATO:0001997\n13860-name: decreased amount\n13861-alt_id: PATO:0000419\n13862-alt_id: PATO:0000468\n--\n13873-\n13874-[Term]\n13875:id: PATO:0001998\n13876-name: conspicuousness\n13877-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its visibility.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13878-comment: This term was created as a grouping term for the 2 terms \"conspicuous\" and \"inconspicuous\". However, it is not clear if these terms should even remain in PATO.\n--\n13880-\n13881-[Term]\n13882:id: PATO:0001999\n13883-name: lacks parts or has fewer parts of type\n13884-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part < n of the indicated entity type, where n is the normal amount for a comparable organism. Note that the bearer of the quality is the whole, not the part. Formally: If a bearer entity e has fewer parts of type X at time t, then the number of instances x of X at t such that x part_of e is < n, where n is either the normal number for comparable entities, or n is stated explicitly. This case includes the limit case, where the bearer lacks all parts of the specified type.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13885-subset: relational_slim\n--\n13888-\n13889-[Term]\n13890:id: PATO:0002000\n13891-name: lacks all parts of type\n13892-alt_id: PATO:0001557\n13893-def: \"A quality of physical entities inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking a physical part as specified by the additional entity.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n--\n13900-\n13901-[Term]\n13902:id: PATO:0002001\n13903-name: has fewer parts of type\n13904-alt_id: PATO:0001569\n13905-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part < n AND has_part > 0 of the indicated entity type, where n is the normal amount for a comparable organism. Note that the bearer of the quality is the whole, not the part. Formally: If a bearer entity e has fewer parts of type X at time t, then the number of instances x of X at t such that x part_of e is < n, where n is either the normal number for comparable entities, or n is stated explicitly.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n--\n13915-\n13916-[Term]\n13917:id: PATO:0002002\n13918-name: has extra parts of type\n13919-alt_id: PATO:0001560\n13920-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part > n of the indicated entity type, where n is the normal amount for a comparable organism. Note that the bearer of the quality is the whole, not the part.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n--\n13932-\n13933-[Term]\n13934:id: PATO:0002003\n13935-name: population quality\n13936-def: \"A quality that inheres in an entire population or part of a population.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n13937-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13940-\n13941-[Term]\n13942:id: PATO:0002004\n13943-name: obsolete surface shape\n13944-def: \"A shape that inheres in a part of a surface. An object can have different surface shapes on different parts of its surface.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13945-comment: Consider PATO:0001925\n--\n13948-\n13949-[Term]\n13950:id: PATO:0002005\n13951-name: concavity\n13952-def: \"Surface shape that refers to the inward or outward curvature of the surface.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13953-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13955-\n13956-[Term]\n13957:id: PATO:0002006\n13958-name: 2-D shape\n13959-def: \"A shape that inheres in a 2 dimensional entity, such as a cross section or projection of a 3 dimensional entity.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13960-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13964-\n13965-[Term]\n13966:id: PATO:0002007\n13967-name: convex 3-D shape\n13968-def: \"A complete three dimensional shape in which for every line connecting pair of points on the object is within the object. Or: a shape lacking cavities. Contrast: concave.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13969-comment: Use this term or an is_a child of this term when the entire shape of the object is known.\n--\n13975-\n13976-[Term]\n13977:id: PATO:0002008\n13978-name: concave 3-D shape\n13979-def: \"A complete three dimensional shape in which there is a line connecting pair of points on the object that lies outside the object. Or: a shape with cavities. Contrast: concave.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n13980-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13985-\n13986-[Term]\n13987:id: PATO:0002009\n13988-name: branchiness\n13989-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the degree to which there are subdivisions or offshoots in a bearer entity.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n13990-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n13993-\n13994-[Term]\n13995:id: PATO:0002010\n13996-name: looseness\n13997-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bing full of small openings or gaps.\" [url:http\\://www.wordreference.com/definition/loose]\n13998-subset: value_slim\n--\n14000-\n14001-[Term]\n14002:id: PATO:0002011\n14003-name: neoplastic\n14004-def: \"A structural quality which is held by a bearer when the latter's disposition the presence of abnormally proliferating masses of cells.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n14005-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14010-\n14011-[Term]\n14012:id: PATO:0002012\n14013-name: coating\n14014-def: \"A texture quality that exists through a liquid cover on the surface of the bearer.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]\n14015-subset: value_slim\n--\n14017-\n14018-[Term]\n14019:id: PATO:0002013\n14020-name: fasciculation\n14021-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of whether the bearer forms a bundle of anatomical fibers, as of muscle or nerve.\" [answers.com:http\\://www.answers.com/]\n14022-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14024-\n14025-[Term]\n14026:id: PATO:0002014\n14027-name: structure, cavities\n14028-def: \"A structural quality that inheres in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing hollow areas.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14029-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14031-\n14032-[Term]\n14033:id: PATO:0002016\n14034-name: magnitude\n14035-is_a: PATO:0000068 ! qualitative\n14036-\n14037-[Term]\n14038:id: PATO:0002017\n14039-name: increased magnitude\n14040-synonym: \"high magnitude\" EXACT []\n14041-is_a: PATO:0002016 ! magnitude\n--\n14043-\n14044-[Term]\n14045:id: PATO:0002018\n14046-name: decreased magnitude\n14047-synonym: \"low magnitude\" EXACT []\n14048-is_a: PATO:0002016 ! magnitude\n--\n14050-\n14051-[Term]\n14052:id: PATO:0002019\n14053-name: aplastic growth\n14054-def: \"A growth quality of occurrent in which the growth of an organism, structure or group of organisms does not occur.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n14055-synonym: \"agenesis\" NARROW []\n--\n14057-\n14058-[Term]\n14059:id: PATO:0002020\n14060-name: pale pink\n14061-def: \"Pink color having high brightness and low saturation.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14062-is_a: PATO:0000954 ! pink\n14063-\n14064-[Term]\n14065:id: PATO:0002021\n14066-name: conical\n14067-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a cone (a 3-D shape with a round cross section that tapers).\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cone_(geometry)]\n14068-subset: value_slim\n--\n14072-\n14073-[Term]\n14074:id: PATO:0002022\n14075-name: villiform\n14076-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a minute projection (villus).\" [PATOC:PEM]\n14077-subset: value_slim\n--\n14079-\n14080-[Term]\n14081:id: PATO:0002023\n14082-name: apical-basal polarity\n14083-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location of features or characteristics along an apical-basal axis.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n14084-subset: value_slim\n--\n14086-\n14087-[Term]\n14088:id: PATO:0002024\n14089-name: anterior-posterior polarity\n14090-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location of features or characteristics along the anterior-posterior axis.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n14091-subset: value_slim\n--\n14095-\n14096-[Term]\n14097:id: PATO:0002025\n14098-name: external angle\n14099-def: \"A convex angle that is formed by one side of a polygon and a line extended from an adjacent side.\" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_angle]\n14100-subset: relational_slim\n--\n14103-\n14104-[Term]\n14105:id: PATO:0002026\n14106-name: non-progressive\n14107-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not increasing over time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14108-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n14115-\n14116-[Term]\n14117:id: PATO:0002027\n14118-name: osmolality\n14119-def: \"A concentration quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's amount of osmoles of solute per kilogram of solvent.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmolarity]\n14120-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14126-\n14127-[Term]\n14128:id: PATO:0002028\n14129-name: decreased osmolality\n14130-def: \"An osmolality which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14131-subset: relational_slim\n--\n14140-\n14141-[Term]\n14142:id: PATO:0002029\n14143-name: increased osmolality\n14144-def: \"An osmolality which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14145-subset: relational_slim\n--\n14154-\n14155-[Term]\n14156:id: PATO:0002030\n14157-name: specificity to\n14158-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits the ability of a probe to react precisely with a specific target molecule.\" [PATOC:mc]\n14159-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14165-\n14166-[Term]\n14167:id: PATO:0002031\n14168-name: upturned\n14169-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved or tilted such that the tip points upwards.\" [PATOC:cjm]\n14170-subset: value_slim\n--\n14174-\n14175-[Term]\n14176:id: PATO:0002032\n14177-name: forward scatter\n14178-def: \"A reflectivity quality inhering in light by virtue of the bearer's scattering occurring at small angle to the incident beam.\" [PATOC:mc]\n14179-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14183-\n14184-[Term]\n14185:id: PATO:0002033\n14186-name: side scatter\n14187-def: \"A reflective quality that is the light scattering occurring at wide angle (around 90 degrees) to the incident beam.\" [PATOC:mc]\n14188-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14192-\n14193-[Term]\n14194:id: PATO:0002034\n14195-name: undivided\n14196-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being unseparated into parts or divisions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14197-subset: value_slim\n--\n14202-\n14203-[Term]\n14204:id: PATO:0002035\n14205-name: ipsilateral to\n14206-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being on the same side in relation to another structure.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14207-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14214-\n14215-[Term]\n14216:id: PATO:0002036\n14217-name: axial to\n14218-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located towards the central axis of the organism or an extremity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14219-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14225-\n14226-[Term]\n14227:id: PATO:0002037\n14228-name: degeneration\n14229-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer exhibiting deterioration of its structure.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14230-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14235-\n14236-[Term]\n14237:id: PATO:0002038\n14238-name: non-degenerate\n14239-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer whose structure which does not deteriorate.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14240-subset: value_slim\n--\n14246-\n14247-[Term]\n14248:id: PATO:0002039\n14249-name: biconcave\n14250-def: \"A concave quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's curving inward on both sides or surfaces.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14251-subset: value_slim\n--\n14254-\n14255-[Term]\n14256:id: PATO:0002040\n14257-name: biconvex\n14258-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being convex on both sides or surface.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/biconvexity]\n14259-subset: value_slim\n--\n14263-\n14264-[Term]\n14265:id: PATO:0002041\n14266-name: anterior-posterior diameter\n14267-def: \"A diameter that is along the anterior-posterior axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14268-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14271-\n14272-[Term]\n14273:id: PATO:0002042\n14274-name: decreased anterior-posterior diameter\n14275-def: \"An anterior-posterior diameter quality which is relatively small.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14276-subset: value_slim\n--\n14281-\n14282-[Term]\n14283:id: PATO:0002043\n14284-name: increased anterior-posterior diameter\n14285-def: \"An anterior-posterior diameter quality which is relatively large.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14286-subset: value_slim\n--\n14291-\n14292-[Term]\n14293:id: PATO:0002044\n14294-name: trapezoid\n14295-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being a quadrilateral with two parallel sides.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14296-subset: value_slim\n--\n14299-\n14300-[Term]\n14301:id: PATO:0002045\n14302-name: dendritic\n14303-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having smaller branches arising from larger branches. Resembling a tree in branching structure.\" [PATOC:cvs]\n14304-subset: value_slim\n--\n14311-\n14312-[Term]\n14313:id: PATO:0002046\n14314-name: abaxial to\n14315-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being away from or on the opposite side of the central axis.\" [medical-dictionary:http\\://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/abaxial]\n14316-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14322-\n14323-[Term]\n14324:id: PATO:0002047\n14325-name: adaxial to\n14326-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located on the side nearest to the axis of an organ or organism.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/adaxial]\n14327-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14333-\n14334-[Term]\n14335:id: PATO:0002048\n14336-name: mosaicism\n14337-def: \"An organismal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two or more cell populations that differ in genetic makeup. This situation can affect any type of cell, including blood cells, gametes (egg and sperm cells), and skin.\" [Medline:http\\://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus]\n14338-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14343-\n14344-[Term]\n14345:id: PATO:0002049\n14346-name: lateral and rotional curvature\n14347-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved around an axis and towards the side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14348-subset: value_slim\n--\n14352-\n14353-[Term]\n14354:id: PATO:0002050\n14355-name: normal amount\n14356-def: \"An amount which normal.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14357-synonym: \"present in normal numbers in organism\" EXACT []\n--\n14362-\n14363-[Term]\n14364:id: PATO:0002051\n14365-name: increased occurrence\n14366-def: \"An occurrence which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14367-synonym: \"increased incidence\" EXACT []\n--\n14373-\n14374-[Term]\n14375:id: PATO:0002052\n14376-name: decreased occurrence\n14377-def: \"An occurrence which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14378-synonym: \"decreased incidence\" EXACT []\n--\n14384-\n14385-[Term]\n14386:id: PATO:0002053\n14387-name: dorso-ventrally flattened\n14388-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being flattened along dorso-ventral axis.\" [PATOC:MSP]\n14389-subset: value_slim\n--\n14393-\n14394-[Term]\n14395:id: PATO:0002054\n14396-name: laterally compressed\n14397-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being flattened along transverse axis.\" [PATOC:msp]\n14398-subset: value_slim\n--\n14404-\n14405-[Term]\n14406:id: PATO:0002055\n14407-name: increased fragility\n14408-def: \"A fragility which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14409-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14416-\n14417-[Term]\n14418:id: PATO:0002056\n14419-name: decreased fragility\n14420-def: \"A fragility which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14421-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14428-\n14429-[Term]\n14430:id: PATO:0002057\n14431-name: increased area\n14432-def: \"An area which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14433-subset: value_slim\n--\n14439-\n14440-[Term]\n14441:id: PATO:0002058\n14442-name: decreased area\n14443-def: \"An area which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14444-subset: value_slim\n--\n14450-\n14451-[Term]\n14452:id: PATO:0002059\n14453-name: emmision wavelength\n14454-def: \"The specific wavelength of light emitted by a fluorescent molecule, such as a labelled probe, upon absorption of light at the (higher) excitation wavelength.\" [web:http\\://www.expertglossary.com/]\n14455-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14459-\n14460-[Term]\n14461:id: PATO:0002060\n14462-name: absorption wavelength\n14463-def: \"The specific wavelength of radiation that can be retained by a bearer.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14464-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14468-\n14469-[Term]\n14470:id: PATO:0002062\n14471-name: physical quality of a process\n14472-subset: attribute_slim\n14473-is_a: PATO:0001236 ! process quality\n--\n14476-\n14477-[Term]\n14478:id: PATO:0002063\n14479-name: columnar\n14480-def: \"A shape inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being elongated and cylindrical.\" [PATOC:me]\n14481-subset: cell_quality\n--\n14487-\n14488-[Term]\n14489:id: PATO:0002064\n14490-name: fenestrated\n14491-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's delimited by a surface with holes.\" [PATOC:me]\n14492-subset: cell_quality\n--\n14498-\n14499-[Term]\n14500:id: PATO:0002065\n14501-name: star shaped\n14502-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being arranged like rays or radii; radiating from a common center.\" [PATOC:me]\n14503-subset: cell_quality\n--\n14510-\n14511-[Term]\n14512:id: PATO:0002066\n14513-name: crystal configuration\n14514-def: \"A solid configuration inhering in a material entity by virtue of its constituent atoms, molecules, or ions being arranged in an orderly repeating pattern extending in all three spatial dimensions.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal]\n14515-subset: value_slim\n--\n14519-\n14520-[Term]\n14521:id: PATO:0002067\n14522-name: stratification\n14523-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's layered configuration.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14524-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14528-\n14529-[Term]\n14530:id: PATO:0002068\n14531-name: stratified\n14532-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a layered configuration.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14533-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14539-\n14540-[Term]\n14541:id: PATO:0002069\n14542-name: unstratified\n14543-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking a layered configuration.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14544-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14550-\n14551-[Term]\n14552:id: PATO:0002070\n14553-name: affinity\n14554-def: \"A molecular quality that arises from the molecular attraction exerted between two atoms or compounds.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14555-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14562-\n14563-[Term]\n14564:id: PATO:0002071\n14565-name: increased affinity\n14566-def: \"An affinity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14567-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14575-\n14576-[Term]\n14577:id: PATO:0002072\n14578-name: decreased affinity\n14579-def: \"An affinity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14580-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14588-\n14589-[Term]\n14590:id: PATO:0002073\n14591-name: avidity\n14592-def: \"A molecular quality that arises from the synergistic strength of bond affinities between multiple bond interactions.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]\n14593-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14600-\n14601-[Term]\n14602:id: PATO:0002074\n14603-name: increased avidity\n14604-def: \"An avidity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14605-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14613-\n14614-[Term]\n14615:id: PATO:0002075\n14616-name: decreased avidity\n14617-def: \"An avidity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14618-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14626-\n14627-[Term]\n14628:id: PATO:0002076\n14629-name: movement behavioral quality\n14630-def: \"A behavioral quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's movement.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14631-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14636-\n14637-[Term]\n14638:id: PATO:0002077\n14639-name: stacked\n14640-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned with multiple entities of the same type above and below.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n14641-subset: value_slim\n--\n14645-\n14646-[Term]\n14647:id: PATO:0002078\n14648-name: hollow\n14649-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an empty space or cavity within.\" [url:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/hollow]\n14650-subset: value_slim\n--\n14654-\n14655-[Term]\n14656:id: PATO:0002080\n14657-name: broken into two pieces\n14658-def: \"A broken quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being separated into two contiguous wholes.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n14659-subset: value_slim\n--\n14663-\n14664-[Term]\n14665:id: PATO:0002081\n14666-name: shattered\n14667-def: \"A broken quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being broken into multiple contiguous wholes.\" [PATOC:GJM]\n14668-subset: value_slim\n--\n14672-\n14673-[Term]\n14674:id: PATO:0002082\n14675-name: partially broken\n14676-def: \"A broken quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being still one contiguous whole but structurally damaged such that in danger of become two or more.\" [PATOC:CJM]\n14677-subset: value_slim\n--\n14681-\n14682-[Term]\n14683:id: PATO:0002083\n14684-name: altered number of\n14685-def: \"Having extra or fewer parts.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14686-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14692-\n14693-[Term]\n14694:id: PATO:0002084\n14695-name: obsolete post-mortem\n14696-def: \"The period after death of the organism.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n14697-comment: Terms were requested by the OBI consortium but it was later decided that the term was not reflecting a quality rather what it might be refered to as a \"conferred quality\".\n--\n14702-\n14703-[Term]\n14704:id: PATO:0002085\n14705-name: obsolete pre-mortem\n14706-def: \"The period before death of the organism.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n14707-comment: Terms were requested by the OBI consortium but it was later decided that the term was not reflecting a quality rather what it might be refered to as a \"conferred quality\".\n--\n14712-\n14713-[Term]\n14714:id: PATO:0002087\n14715-name: bullet-shaped\n14716-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being short and wide and tapered distally.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14717-subset: value_slim\n--\n14721-\n14722-[Term]\n14723:id: PATO:0002088\n14724-name: monocystic\n14725-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's body containing one cyst - a formation of a sac-like closed membranous structure not associated with neoplasia.\" [mondofacto:mondofacto]\n14726-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14731-\n14732-[Term]\n14733:id: PATO:0002089\n14734-name: polycystic\n14735-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's body containing more than one cyst - formations of sac-like closed membranous structures not associated with neoplasia.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14736-subset: value_slim\n--\n14741-\n14742-[Term]\n14743:id: PATO:0002090\n14744-name: adenomatous\n14745-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting the morphological characteristics of a glandular epithelial cell.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14746-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14751-\n14752-[Term]\n14753:id: PATO:0002091\n14754-name: subacute\n14755-def: \"A quality of a single process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an onset and time course between acute and chronic.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14756-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n14762-\n14763-[Term]\n14764:id: PATO:0002092\n14765-name: anaplastic\n14766-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a neoplastic cell by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting breakdown of cell-cell interaction maintaining tissue architecture, proliferative dysregulation and bizarre modification to nucleus size and shape.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14767-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14772-\n14773-[Term]\n14774:id: PATO:0002093\n14775-name: ballooning\n14776-def: \"A volume quality inhering in a degenerating cell by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting an increase in volume associated with cytoplasmic abnormalities.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14777-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14782-\n14783-[Term]\n14784:id: PATO:0002094\n14785-name: basophilic\n14786-def: \"An affinity inhering in an anatomical structure by virtue of the bearer exhibiting a molecular interaction for basic dyes under specific pH conditions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14787-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14793-\n14794-[Term]\n14795:id: PATO:0002095\n14796-name: obsolete neoplasm disposition\n14797-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour to progress or fail to progress during it's life time.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14798-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n14802-\n14803-[Term]\n14804:id: PATO:0002096\n14805-name: neoplastic, non-malignant\n14806-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition not to progress, invade surrounding tissues or metastasize.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14807-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14817-\n14818-[Term]\n14819:id: PATO:0002097\n14820-name: neoplastic, malignant\n14821-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition to progress, invade surrounding tissues or metastasize.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14822-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14829-\n14830-[Term]\n14831:id: PATO:0002098\n14832-name: neoplastic, metastatic\n14833-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition to spread and invade distant tissues.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14834-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14841-\n14842-[Term]\n14843:id: PATO:0002099\n14844-name: differentiated\n14845-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its stable specialization to a particular cell type.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14846-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14852-\n14853-[Term]\n14854:id: PATO:0002100\n14855-name: undifferentiated\n14856-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of having not yet acquired a special structure of function.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14857-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14863-\n14864-[Term]\n14865:id: PATO:0002101\n14866-name: metaplastic\n14867-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of having changed from one fully differentiated state into another.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14868-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14874-\n14875-[Term]\n14876:id: PATO:0002102\n14877-name: proliferative\n14878-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a cell that arises by virtue of whether the bearer exhibits the ability to grow and proliferate in number through cell division.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14879-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n14885-\n14886-[Term]\n14887:id: PATO:0002103\n14888-name: infiltrative\n14889-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's penetrating or permeating another substance or area.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14890-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14896-\n14897-[Term]\n14898:id: PATO:0002104\n14899-name: inflamed\n14900-def: \"A compositional quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's infiltration by leukocytes, local edema and accumulation of plasma proteins.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14901-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14906-\n14907-[Term]\n14908:id: PATO:0002105\n14909-name: hemorrhagic\n14910-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting excessive discharge of blood from the blood vessels.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14911-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14916-\n14917-[Term]\n14918:id: PATO:0002106\n14919-name: poorly differentiated\n14920-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its lacking most of the cellular characteristics which would allow it to be fully differentiated.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14921-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14926-\n14927-[Term]\n14928:id: PATO:0002107\n14929-name: peripheral\n14930-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being at the edge or boundary of a related entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14931-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14937-\n14938-[Term]\n14939:id: PATO:0002108\n14940-name: papillary\n14941-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling small nipple like projection.\" [PATO:GVG]\n14942-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14947-\n14948-[Term]\n14949:id: PATO:0002109\n14950-name: caseous\n14951-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling cheese.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n14952-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14958-\n14959-[Term]\n14960:id: PATO:0002110\n14961-name: well differentiated\n14962-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its having most of the cellular characteristics of the tissue of origin.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14963-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n14968-\n14969-[Term]\n14970:id: PATO:0002111\n14971-name: moderately well differentiated\n14972-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its lacking few of the cellular characteristics which would allow it to be fully differentiated.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n14973-subset: cell_quality\n--\n14978-\n14979-[Term]\n14980:id: PATO:0002112\n14981-name: perforate\n14982-alt_id: PATO:0000649\n14983-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a hole or holes, especially a row or array of small holes.\" [answers.com:answers.com]\n--\n14992-\n14993-[Term]\n14994:id: PATO:0002113\n14995-name: cribriform\n14996-def: \"Perforated like a sieve.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n14997-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15002-\n15003-[Term]\n15004:id: PATO:0002114\n15005-name: fatty\n15006-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing excess lipid.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15007-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15012-\n15013-[Term]\n15014:id: PATO:0002115\n15015-name: fibrinoid\n15016-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing fibrin.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15017-subset: value_slim\n--\n15021-\n15022-[Term]\n15023:id: PATO:0002116\n15024-name: fibrinopurulent\n15025-def: \"A composition quality inhering in exudate by virtue of the bearer's containing fibrin.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15026-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15031-\n15032-[Term]\n15033:id: PATO:0002117\n15034-name: glandular\n15035-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhbiting the morphological characteristics of a gland.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15036-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15041-\n15042-[Term]\n15043:id: PATO:0002118\n15044-name: multiple\n15045-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being present in more than two copies.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15046-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15051-\n15052-[Term]\n15053:id: PATO:0002119\n15054-name: hydropic\n15055-def: \"A structural quality which is held by a bearer when the latter exhibits an excessive accumulation of intracellular fluid.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15056-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15061-\n15062-[Term]\n15063:id: PATO:0002120\n15064-name: suppurative\n15065-def: \"A quality inhering a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to generate pus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15066-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15072-\n15073-[Term]\n15074:id: PATO:0002121\n15075-name: trabecular\n15076-def: \"A spatial pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's structure resembling an irregular meshwork with cross-linking struts.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15077-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15082-\n15083-[Term]\n15084:id: PATO:0002122\n15085-name: mixed\n15086-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being composed of more than one identifiable entities.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15087-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15092-\n15093-[Term]\n15094:id: PATO:0002123\n15095-name: minimal\n15096-def: \"Being smallest in amount, extent or degree.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15097-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15102-\n15103-[Term]\n15104:id: PATO:0002124\n15105-name: laminar\n15106-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's processing the form of a thin plate sheet or layer.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15107-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15112-\n15113-[Term]\n15114:id: PATO:0002125\n15115-name: nodular\n15116-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting a knot-like mass.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15117-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15122-\n15123-[Term]\n15124:id: PATO:0002126\n15125-name: osseous\n15126-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing bone.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15127-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15133-\n15134-[Term]\n15135:id: PATO:0002127\n15136-name: scirrhous\n15137-def: \"A hardness quality of being rigid and resistant to pressure and fibrous.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15138-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15144-\n15145-[Term]\n15146:id: PATO:0002128\n15147-name: serous\n15148-def: \"A quality inhering a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing or resembling serum.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15149-subset: value_slim\n--\n15153-\n15154-[Term]\n15155:id: PATO:0002129\n15156-name: neoplastic, invasive\n15157-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition to invade surrounding tissues.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15158-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15165-\n15166-[Term]\n15167:id: PATO:0002130\n15168-name: neoplastic, deeply invasive\n15169-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition to invade surrounding tissues to a large extend.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15170-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15175-\n15176-[Term]\n15177:id: PATO:0002131\n15178-name: abduction\n15179-def: \"A displaced angular placement quality inhering in a body part by virtue of the bearer's movement away from the medial plane of the body.\" [wikipedia:wikipedia]\n15180-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15185-\n15186-[Term]\n15187:id: PATO:0002132\n15188-name: neoplastic, non-invasive\n15189-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition not to invade surrounding tissues.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15190-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15196-\n15197-[Term]\n15198:id: PATO:0002133\n15199-name: adduction\n15200-def: \"A displaced angular placement quality inhering in a body part by virtue of the bearer's movement closer the medial plane of the body.\" [wikipedia:wikipedia]\n15201-comment: This term is also used in reference to the operation of the muscle in anatomy or musculature.\n--\n15207-\n15208-[Term]\n15209:id: PATO:0002134\n15210-name: fibrillary\n15211-def: \"A composition quaity inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's containing of or pertaining to fibrils, or nanoscale fibers.\" [wikipedia:wikipedia]\n15212-subset: value_slim\n--\n15217-\n15218-[Term]\n15219:id: PATO:0002135\n15220-name: delayed closure\n15221-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's delay to complete the closure of the opening of an anatomical entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15222-is_a: PATO:0000502 ! delayed\n--\n15225-\n15226-[Term]\n15227:id: PATO:0002136\n15228-name: radiopacity\n15229-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's relative inability of electromagnetism to pass through a particular material, particularly X-rays.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]\n15230-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15236-\n15237-[Term]\n15238:id: PATO:0002137\n15239-name: radiopaque\n15240-def: \"A radiopacity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's prevention of the passage of electromagnetic radiation.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]\n15241-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15246-\n15247-[Term]\n15248:id: PATO:0002138\n15249-name: edibility\n15250-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being fit to be eaten.\" [PATOC:VO]\n15251-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15258-\n15259-[Term]\n15260:id: PATO:0002139\n15261-name: edible\n15262-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being suitable for use as food.\" [PATOC:VO]\n15263-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15271-\n15272-[Term]\n15273:id: PATO:0002140\n15274-name: inedible\n15275-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer not being suitable for use as food.\" [PATOC:VO]\n15276-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15283-\n15284-[Term]\n15285:id: PATO:0002141\n15286-name: irregular density\n15287-def: \"A density quality which lacks pattern.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15288-subset: value_slim\n--\n15292-\n15293-[Term]\n15294:id: PATO:0002142\n15295-name: bracket\n15296-subset: value_slim\n15297-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n--\n15300-\n15301-[Term]\n15302:id: PATO:0002143\n15303-name: sloped downward\n15304-subset: value_slim\n15305-is_a: PATO:0001481 ! sloped\n--\n15308-\n15309-[Term]\n15310:id: PATO:0002144\n15311-name: increased radiopacity\n15312-def: \"A radiopacity that is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15313-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15320-\n15321-[Term]\n15322:id: PATO:0002145\n15323-name: decreased radiopacity\n15324-def: \"A radiopacity that is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15325-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15332-\n15333-[Term]\n15334:id: PATO:0002146\n15335-name: virulence\n15336-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the severity of infectious disease caused by the bearer in a target organism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8941-3984]\n15337-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15342-\n15343-[Term]\n15344:id: PATO:0002147\n15345-name: reduced virulence\n15346-def: \"A virulence that is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15347-subset: value_slim\n--\n15354-\n15355-[Term]\n15356:id: PATO:0002148\n15357-name: increased virulence\n15358-def: \"A virulence that is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15359-subset: value_slim\n--\n15365-\n15366-[Term]\n15367:id: PATO:0002149\n15368-name: ivory\n15369-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer exhibiting increased density resulting in exhibiting increased degree of radiopacity (in X-rays).\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15370-subset: value_slim\n--\n15374-\n15375-[Term]\n15376:id: PATO:0002150\n15377-name: splayed caudal\n15378-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outwards from the part of the body from which the tail arises.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15379-subset: value_slim\n--\n15385-\n15386-[Term]\n15387:id: PATO:0002151\n15388-name: splayed dorsal\n15389-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outwards from the back or upper surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15390-subset: value_slim\n--\n15395-\n15396-[Term]\n15397:id: PATO:0002152\n15398-name: splayed lateral\n15399-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outwards from the side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15400-subset: value_slim\n--\n15404-\n15405-[Term]\n15406:id: PATO:0002153\n15407-name: splayed rostral\n15408-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outwards the front of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15409-subset: value_slim\n--\n15415-\n15416-[Term]\n15417:id: PATO:0002154\n15418-name: splayed ventral\n15419-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outwards the abdomen of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15420-subset: value_slim\n--\n15426-\n15427-[Term]\n15428:id: PATO:0002155\n15429-name: medially rotated\n15430-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the middle of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15431-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15437-\n15438-[Term]\n15439:id: PATO:0002156\n15440-name: laterally rotated\n15441-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the side of an organism.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15442-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15448-\n15449-[Term]\n15450:id: PATO:0002157\n15451-name: partially dislocated\n15452-alt_id: PATO:0002160\n15453-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being slightly out of its usual or proper place, or position.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n15462-\n15463-[Term]\n15464:id: PATO:0002161\n15465-name: bicornuate\n15466-def: \"Having two horns or horn-shaped branches.\" [mondofacto:mondofacto]\n15467-subset: value_slim\n--\n15471-\n15472-[Term]\n15473:id: PATO:0002162\n15474-name: high-arched\n15475-def: \"A concave quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's forming or resembling an arch of an increased apical height.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15476-subset: value_slim\n--\n15481-\n15482-[Term]\n15483:id: PATO:0002163\n15484-name: herniated into\n15485-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bodily structure that has protruded through an abnormal opening in the wall that contains it into the surface or boundary of another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15486-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15492-\n15493-[Term]\n15494:id: PATO:0002164\n15495-name: curved medial\n15496-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the middle.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15497-subset: value_slim\n--\n15501-\n15502-[Term]\n15503:id: PATO:0002165\n15504-name: drooping\n15505-def: \"To bent or hang downwards.\" [thefreedictionary.:thefreedictionary.]\n15506-subset: value_slim\n--\n15511-\n15512-[Term]\n15513:id: PATO:0002166\n15514-name: premature closure\n15515-def: \"A duration quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's premature completion of the closure of the opening of an anatomical entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15516-subset: value_slim\n--\n15520-\n15521-[Term]\n15522:id: PATO:0002167\n15523-name: herniated out of\n15524-def: \"A protruding quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bodily structure that has protruded out of the surface or boundary of another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15525-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15531-\n15532-[Term]\n15533:id: PATO:0002168\n15534-name: displaced to\n15535-def: \"An angular placement quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being changed in position in relation to another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15536-subset: relational_slim\n--\n15541-\n15542-[Term]\n15543:id: PATO:0002169\n15544-name: split medially\n15545-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being split along the median axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15546-subset: value_slim\n--\n15550-\n15551-[Term]\n15552:id: PATO:0002170\n15553-name: split laterally\n15554-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being split asymmetrically on one side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15555-subset: value_slim\n--\n15559-\n15560-[Term]\n15561:id: PATO:0002171\n15562-name: split bilaterally\n15563-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being split on two side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15564-subset: value_slim\n--\n15568-\n15569-[Term]\n15570:id: PATO:0002172\n15571-name: split radially\n15572-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being split along the radial axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15573-subset: value_slim\n--\n15577-\n15578-[Term]\n15579:id: PATO:0002173\n15580-name: misaligned towards\n15581-def: \"An alignment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in a improper spatial positioning towards an additional entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15582-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15587-\n15588-[Term]\n15589:id: PATO:0002174\n15590-name: misaligned away from\n15591-def: \"An alignment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being in a improper spatial positioning away from an additional entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15592-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15597-\n15598-[Term]\n15599:id: PATO:0002175\n15600-name: spatial deviation\n15601-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's changed direction of position towards another entity.\" [PATO:GVG]\n15602-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15606-\n15607-[Term]\n15608:id: PATO:0002176\n15609-name: deviation towards the lateral side\n15610-def: \"A deviation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's changed direction of position towards the side.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15611-subset: value_slim\n--\n15615-\n15616-[Term]\n15617:id: PATO:0002177\n15618-name: deviation towards the medial side\n15619-def: \"A deviation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's changed direction of position towards the middle.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15620-subset: value_slim\n--\n15624-\n15625-[Term]\n15626:id: PATO:0002178\n15627-name: mislocalised radially\n15628-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being out of its usual or proper place, or position around a central point or axis.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15629-subset: value_slim\n--\n15633-\n15634-[Term]\n15635:id: PATO:0002179\n15636-name: mislocalised proximally\n15637-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards to point of attachment or origin.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15638-subset: value_slim\n--\n15642-\n15643-[Term]\n15644:id: PATO:0002180\n15645-name: straight\n15646-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being free of curves, bends, or angles.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n15647-subset: value_slim\n--\n15651-\n15652-[Term]\n15653:id: PATO:0002181\n15654-name: displaced\n15655-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's being changed in position.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15656-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15660-\n15661-[Term]\n15662:id: PATO:0002182\n15663-name: molecular quality\n15664-alt_id: PATO:0002061\n15665-def: \"A quality which inheres in a molecular entity, a single molecule, atom, ion, radical etc.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n15670-\n15671-[Term]\n15672:id: PATO:0002183\n15673-name: cyclicity\n15674-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of whether that there is a presence of cycles in the connection of the atoms within the molecular entity.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15675-subset: value_slim\n--\n15679-\n15680-[Term]\n15681:id: PATO:0002184\n15682-name: cyclic cyclicity\n15683-def: \"Cyclic cyclicity inheres in a molecule when the atoms of the molecule do contain at least one cycle in the atom-atom connection paths (through bonds).\" [PATOC:JH]\n15684-subset: value_slim\n--\n15688-\n15689-[Term]\n15690:id: PATO:0002185\n15691-name: acyclic cyclicity\n15692-def: \"Acyclic cyclicity inheres in a molecule when the atoms within the molecule do not contain at least one cycle in the atom-atom connection paths (through the bonds).\" [PATOC:JH]\n15693-subset: value_slim\n--\n15697-\n15698-[Term]\n15699:id: PATO:0002186\n15700-name: polarity\n15701-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of whether or not the molecular entity has a separation of electric charge which leads to the molecule having an electric dipole.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15702-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15707-\n15708-[Term]\n15709:id: PATO:0002187\n15710-name: polar polarity\n15711-def: \"Polar polarity is a quality that inheres in a molecular entity when the molecular entity is polar, i.e. does possess an electric dipole.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15712-subset: value_slim\n--\n15717-\n15718-[Term]\n15719:id: PATO:0002188\n15720-name: nonpolar polarity\n15721-def: \"A molecular quality which inheres in a molecular entity when the molecular entity does not possess an electrical dipole.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15722-subset: value_slim\n--\n15726-\n15727-[Term]\n15728:id: PATO:0002189\n15729-name: electric polarizability\n15730-def: \"The ease of distortion of the electron cloud of a molecular entity by an electric field.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15731-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15736-\n15737-[Term]\n15738:id: PATO:0002190\n15739-name: aromaticity\n15740-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the presence of a conjugated ring of unsaturated bonds, lone pairs, or empty orbitals that exhibit a stabilization stronger than would be expected by the stabilization of conjugation alone.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15741-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15746-\n15747-[Term]\n15748:id: PATO:0002191\n15749-name: aromatic\n15750-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity when it possesses at least one ring that is aromatic, i.e. A conjugated ring of unsaturated bonds, lone pairs, or empty orbitals that exhibit a stabilization stronger than would be expected by the stabilization of conjugation alone.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15751-subset: value_slim\n--\n15757-\n15758-[Term]\n15759:id: PATO:0002192\n15760-name: non-aromatic\n15761-def: \"A quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the molecule possessing no rings that are aromatic.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15762-subset: value_slim\n--\n15767-\n15768-[Term]\n15769:id: PATO:0002193\n15770-name: electric charge\n15771-def: \"A molecular quality that inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the overall electric charge of the molecule, which is due to a comparison between the total number of electrons and the total number of protons.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15772-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15777-\n15778-[Term]\n15779:id: PATO:0002194\n15780-name: neutral charge\n15781-def: \"A quality which inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the molecular entity possessing the same amount of electrons overall as protons, thus having an overall neutral charge.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15782-subset: value_slim\n--\n15788-\n15789-[Term]\n15790:id: PATO:0002195\n15791-name: positive charge\n15792-def: \"A quality which inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the molecular entity possessing more protons overall than electrons, thus having an overall positive charge.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15793-subset: value_slim\n--\n15799-\n15800-[Term]\n15801:id: PATO:0002196\n15802-name: negative charge\n15803-def: \"A quality which inheres in a molecular entity by virtue of the molecular entity possessing more electrons overall than protons, thus having an overall negative charge.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15804-subset: value_slim\n--\n15809-\n15810-[Term]\n15811:id: PATO:0002197\n15812-name: electronegativity\n15813-def: \"A quality that describes the power of an atom to attract electrons to itself .\" [PATOC:JH]\n15814-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15820-\n15821-[Term]\n15822:id: PATO:0002198\n15823-name: quality of a substance\n15824-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of its constitution.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15825-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15829-\n15830-[Term]\n15831:id: PATO:0002199\n15832-name: meltability\n15833-def: \"A quality which inheres in a substance by virtue of the ease with which the substance can be changed from a solid to a liquid state especially by the application of heat.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15834-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15838-\n15839-[Term]\n15840:id: PATO:0002200\n15841-name: vaporizability\n15842-def: \"A quality which inheres in a substance by virtue of the ease with which the substance can be changed into a gaseous state.\" [PATOC:JH]\n15843-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15847-\n15848-[Term]\n15849:id: PATO:0002201\n15850-name: handedness\n15851-def: \"A behavioral quality inhering ina bearer by virtue of the bearer's unequal distribution of fine motor skill between its left and right hands or feet.\" [birnlex:2178]\n15852-comment: Adapted from Wikipedia and the birnlex term that is dbxref'd. Added on behalf of OBI at March 2010 workshop.\n--\n15858-\n15859-[Term]\n15860:id: PATO:0002202\n15861-name: left handedness\n15862-def: \"Handedness where the organism preferentially uses the left hand or foot for tasks requiring the use of a single hand or foot or a dominant hand or foot.\" [birnlex:2038]\n15863-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15868-\n15869-[Term]\n15870:id: PATO:0002203\n15871-name: right handedness\n15872-def: \"Handedness where the organism preferentially uses the right hand or foot for tasks requiring the use of a single hand or foot or a dominant hand or foot.\" [birnlex:2184]\n15873-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15878-\n15879-[Term]\n15880:id: PATO:0002204\n15881-name: ambidextrous handedness\n15882-def: \"Handedness where the organism exhibits no overall dominance in the use of right or left hand or foot in the performance of tasks that require one hand or foot or a dominant hand or foot.\" [birnlex:2042]\n15883-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n15888-\n15889-[Term]\n15890:id: PATO:0002205\n15891-name: capacitance\n15892-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ability to hold an electrical charge.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]\n15893-comment: Capacitance is also a measure of the amount of electrical energy stored (or separated) for a given electric potential.\n--\n15900-\n15901-[Term]\n15902:id: PATO:0002206\n15903-name: neonatal\n15904-def: \"A maturity quality inhering to a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being at the point or short after birth.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15905-subset: value_slim\n--\n15909-\n15910-[Term]\n15911:id: PATO:0002207\n15912-name: insertion depth\n15913-def: \"A quality that is the distance between the end of the inserted object and the surface of the object into which it penetrates.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15914-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n15920-\n15921-[Term]\n15922:id: PATO:0002208\n15923-name: spoon-shaped\n15924-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of a spoon.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/spoon-shaped]\n15925-subset: value_slim\n--\n15929-\n15930-[Term]\n15931:id: PATO:0002209\n15932-name: incisiform\n15933-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having the shape of an incisor tooth.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/incisiform]\n15934-subset: value_slim\n--\n15938-\n15939-[Term]\n15940:id: PATO:0002210\n15941-name: bulbous\n15942-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a teardrop.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15943-subset: value_slim\n--\n15950-\n15951-[Term]\n15952:id: PATO:0002211\n15953-name: recurved\n15954-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved backward or inward.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/recurved]\n15955-subset: value_slim\n--\n15959-\n15960-[Term]\n15961:id: PATO:0002212\n15962-name: slender\n15963-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being small or narrow in circumference or width in proportion to length or height.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/slender]\n15964-subset: value_slim\n--\n15969-\n15970-[Term]\n15971:id: PATO:0002213\n15972-name: obclavate\n15973-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape being inversely clavate.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n15974-subset: cell_quality\n--\n15979-\n15980-[Term]\n15981:id: PATO:0002214\n15982-name: bilobed\n15983-def: \"A lobed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided into or having two lobes.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/bilobed]\n15984-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n15989-\n15990-[Term]\n15991:id: PATO:0002215\n15992-name: falciform\n15993-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having the shape of a scythe or sickle.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/falciform]\n15994-subset: value_slim\n--\n16004-\n16005-[Term]\n16006:id: PATO:0002216\n16007-name: ubiquinated\n16008-def: \"A molecular quality that pertains to the post-translational modification of a protein by the covalent attachment of one or more ubiquitin monomer.\" [neurolex:http\\://neurolex.org/]\n16009-subset: value_slim\n--\n16014-\n16015-[Term]\n16016:id: PATO:0002217\n16017-name: nitrated\n16018-def: \"A molecular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being combined, or impregnated, with nitric acid, or some of its compounds.\" [neurolex:http\\://neurolex.org/wiki/Category\\:Nitrated_Molecular_Quality]\n16019-subset: value_slim\n--\n16023-\n16024-[Term]\n16025:id: PATO:0002218\n16026-name: demyelinated\n16027-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's loss of myelin sheath.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/demyelinated]\n16028-comment: For example loss of myelin sheath from a normally myelinated axon or dendrite.\n--\n16034-\n16035-[Term]\n16036:id: PATO:0002219\n16037-name: fan-shaped\n16038-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer that is shaped in the form of a fan.\" [thefreedictionary:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/fan-shaped]\n16039-subset: value_slim\n--\n16044-\n16045-[Term]\n16046:id: PATO:0002220\n16047-name: phosphorylated\n16048-def: \"A quality inhering in a protein or a molecule by virtue of the bearer's having a phosphate (PO4) group.\" [wikipedia:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorylated]\n16049-subset: value_slim\n--\n16055-\n16056-[Term]\n16057:id: PATO:0002221\n16058-name: increased phosphorylation\n16059-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being phosphorylated to a more than normal extent, or fully saturated with phosphate groups.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hyperphosphorylated]\n16060-subset: value_slim\n--\n16067-\n16068-[Term]\n16069:id: PATO:0002222\n16070-name: decreased phosphorylation\n16071-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being phosphorylated to a lesser than normal extent, or less than fully.\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hypophosphorylated]\n16072-subset: value_slim\n--\n16079-\n16080-[Term]\n16081:id: PATO:0002223\n16082-name: oxidized\n16083-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having reacted with oxygen, or been modified by oxidation (the reaction in which the atoms of an element lose electrons and the valence of the element increases).\" [Wikipedia:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxidized]\n16084-subset: value_slim\n--\n16088-\n16089-[Term]\n16090:id: PATO:0002224\n16091-name: V-shaped\n16092-def: \"An angular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a single angle in its length giving the bearer the form of the letter V.\" [PATOC:JE]\n16093-subset: value_slim\n--\n16097-\n16098-[Term]\n16099:id: PATO:0002225\n16100-name: L-shaped\n16101-def: \"An angular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a single angle in its length giving the bearer the form of the letter L.\" [PATOC:JE]\n16102-subset: value_slim\n--\n16106-\n16107-[Term]\n16108:id: PATO:0002226\n16109-name: subcylindrical\n16110-def: \"A cylindrical shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being imperfectly cylindrical or approximately cylindrical.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/Subcylindrical]\n16111-subset: value_slim\n--\n16115-\n16116-[Term]\n16117:id: PATO:0002227\n16118-name: cup-shaped\n16119-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape form resembling the shape of a cup.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/cup-shaped]\n16120-subset: value_slim\n--\n16125-\n16126-[Term]\n16127:id: PATO:0002228\n16128-name: acuminate\n16129-def: \"A tapered shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's tapering gradually to a sharp point.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/acuminate]\n16130-subset: value_slim\n--\n16134-\n16135-[Term]\n16136:id: PATO:0002229\n16137-name: subrectangular\n16138-def: \"A quadrangular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being approximately rectangular.\" [url:http\\://dictionary.reference.com/browse/subrectangular?qsrc=2446&o=100074]\n16139-subset: value_slim\n--\n16143-\n16144-[Term]\n16145:id: PATO:0002230\n16146-name: subtriangular\n16147-def: \"A triangular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being nearly, but not perfectly, triangular.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/Subtriangular]\n16148-subset: value_slim\n--\n16152-\n16153-[Term]\n16154:id: PATO:0002231\n16155-name: multifid\n16156-def: \"A split shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or being divided into many lobes or similar segments.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/multifid]\n16157-subset: value_slim\n--\n16161-\n16162-[Term]\n16163:id: PATO:0002232\n16164-name: semicircular\n16165-def: \"A 2-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having shape or form of half a circle.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/semicircle]\n16166-subset: value_slim\n--\n16172-\n16173-[Term]\n16174:id: PATO:0002233\n16175-name: far from\n16176-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located far (not close to) in space in relation to another entity.\" [PATOC:PM]\n16177-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16184-\n16185-[Term]\n16186:id: PATO:0002234\n16187-name: emarginate\n16188-def: \"A notched shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a notched tip or edge.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/emarginate]\n16189-subset: value_slim\n--\n16193-\n16194-[Term]\n16195:id: PATO:0002235\n16196-name: blade-like\n16197-def: \"A tapered shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being flat, slender, and tapering to a point.\" [PATOC:JE]\n16198-subset: value_slim\n--\n16206-\n16207-[Term]\n16208:id: PATO:0002236\n16209-name: aliform\n16210-def: \"Shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a wing.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/aliform]\n16211-subset: value_slim\n--\n16216-\n16217-[Term]\n16218:id: PATO:0002237\n16219-name: retrorse\n16220-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved backward or downward.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/retrorse]\n16221-subset: value_slim\n--\n16225-\n16226-[Term]\n16227:id: PATO:0002238\n16228-name: antrorse\n16229-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved forward or upward.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/antrorse]\n16230-subset: value_slim\n--\n16234-\n16235-[Term]\n16236:id: PATO:0002239\n16237-name: hourglass-shaped\n16238-def: \"A concave 3-D shape that inheres in the bearer by virtue of the bearer's nearly) symmetric shape wide at its ends and narrow in the middle, resembling the figure of number 8.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hourglass-shaped]\n16239-subset: value_slim\n--\n16244-\n16245-[Term]\n16246:id: PATO:0002240\n16247-name: teardrop-shaped\n16248-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape resembling falling drop.\" [url:wordnetweb.princeton.edu/perl/webwn]\n16249-subset: value_slim\n--\n16254-\n16255-[Term]\n16256:id: PATO:0002241\n16257-name: trilobed\n16258-def: \"A lobed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided into or having three lobes.\" [url:http\\://www.thefreedictionary.com/trilobed]\n16259-subset: value_slim\n--\n16263-\n16264-[Term]\n16265:id: PATO:0002242\n16266-name: velocity\n16267-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's rate of change of the position.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velocity]\n16268-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16273-\n16274-[Term]\n16275:id: PATO:0002243\n16276-name: fluid flow rate\n16277-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a fluid (liquid or gas) by virtue of the amount of fluid which passes through a given surface per unit time.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volumetric_flow_rate]\n16278-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16285-\n16286-[Term]\n16287:id: PATO:0002244\n16288-name: mass flow rate\n16289-def: \"A flow rate quality inhering in a substance by virtue of the mass of substance which passes through a given surface per unit time.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_flow_rate]\n16290-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16294-\n16295-[Term]\n16296:id: PATO:0002245\n16297-name: increased force\n16298-def: \"A force which relative high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16299-subset: value_slim\n--\n16306-\n16307-[Term]\n16308:id: PATO:0002246\n16309-name: decreased force\n16310-def: \"A force which is relative low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16311-subset: value_slim\n--\n16318-\n16319-[Term]\n16320:id: PATO:0002247\n16321-name: degree of pigmentation\n16322-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having or lacking of substances produced by living organisms that have a color resulting from selective color absorption.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biological_pigment]\n16323-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16329-\n16330-[Term]\n16331:id: PATO:0002248\n16332-name: pigmented\n16333-def: \"A degree of pigmentation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having substances produced by living organisms that have a color resulting from selective color absorption.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16334-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n16341-\n16342-[Term]\n16343:id: PATO:0002249\n16344-name: unpigmented\n16345-def: \"A degree of pigmentation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking substances produced by living organisms that have a color resulting from selective color absorption.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16346-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n16353-\n16354-[Term]\n16355:id: PATO:0002250\n16356-name: increased pigmentation\n16357-def: \"A degree of pigmentation quality that is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16358-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n16366-\n16367-[Term]\n16368:id: PATO:0002251\n16369-name: decreased pigmentation\n16370-def: \"A degree of pigmentation quality that is relative low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16371-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n16379-\n16380-[Term]\n16381:id: PATO:0002252\n16382-name: antero-posteriorly flattened\n16383-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being flattened along the antero-posterior axis.\" [PATOC:JC]\n16384-subset: value_slim\n--\n16389-\n16390-[Term]\n16391:id: PATO:0002253\n16392-name: platelike\n16393-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being roundish, flattish shape, possibly with a slightly angled edge.\" [PATOC:CVC]\n16394-subset: value_slim\n--\n16399-\n16400-[Term]\n16401:id: PATO:0002254\n16402:name: flattened\n16403-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's surface becoming more extended in a plane.\" [PATOC:CVS]\n16404-comment: Becoming flat but not necessarily completely flat.\n16405-subset: value_slim\n--\n16410-\n16411-[Term]\n16412:id: PATO:0002255\n16413-name: grooved\n16414-def: \"Texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked with one or more channels.\" [PATOC:JE]\n16415-subset: value_slim\n--\n16421-\n16422-[Term]\n16423:id: PATO:0002256\n16424-name: tricuspidate\n16425-def: \"A cuscpidate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer possessing three cusps.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16426-subset: value_slim\n--\n16431-\n16432-[Term]\n16433:id: PATO:0002257\n16434-name: multicuspidate\n16435-def: \"A cuscpidate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer possessing more than one cusp.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16436-subset: value_slim\n--\n16440-\n16441-[Term]\n16442:id: PATO:0002258\n16443-name: pointed\n16444-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a point.\" [PATOC:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/pointed]\n16445-subset: value_slim\n--\n16449-\n16450-[Term]\n16451:id: PATO:0002259\n16452-name: adjacent to\n16453-alt_id: PATO:0001771\n16454-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located near in space in relation to another entity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n--\n16464-\n16465-[Term]\n16466:id: PATO:0002260\n16467-name: semi erect\n16468-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being partially upright in position or posture.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16469-synonym: \"semi upright\" EXACT []\n--\n16473-\n16474-[Term]\n16475:id: PATO:0002261\n16476-name: located in\n16477-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location within another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16478-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16483-\n16484-[Term]\n16485:id: PATO:0002262\n16486-name: phosphorylation\n16487-def: \"A quality inhering in a protein or a molecule by virtue of the addition of a phosphate (PO4) group to the bearer.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorylation]\n16488-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16493-\n16494-[Term]\n16495:id: PATO:0002263\n16496-name: dephosphorylated\n16497-def: \"A quality inhering in a protein or a molecule by virtue of the bearer's lacking a phosphate (PO4) group.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dephosphorylation]\n16498-subset: value_slim\n--\n16503-\n16504-[Term]\n16505:id: PATO:0002264\n16506-name: organization quality\n16507-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being arranged in a systematic fashion.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16508-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16512-\n16513-[Term]\n16514:id: PATO:0002265\n16515-name: behavioural activity\n16516-def: \"A behavioral quality of a process inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to exhibit marked activity.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16517-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16523-\n16524-[Term]\n16525:id: PATO:0002266\n16526-name: 3-D shape\n16527-def: \"A shape that inheres in a 3 dimensional entity.\" [PATOC:OREGON]\n16528-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n--\n16531-\n16532-[Term]\n16533:id: PATO:0002267\n16534-name: edge shape\n16535-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n16536-property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2061-091X\n--\n16538-\n16539-[Term]\n16540:id: PATO:0002268\n16541-name: centered\n16542-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located in a position equidistant from edges.\" [PATOC:OREGON]\n16543-subset: value_slim\n--\n16547-\n16548-[Term]\n16549:id: PATO:0002269\n16550-name: accumulation\n16551-def: \"A structural quality of the collection or massing of one physical object within another physical object.\" [PATOC:CVC]\n16552-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16559-\n16560-[Term]\n16561:id: PATO:0002270\n16562-name: increased accumulation\n16563-def: \"An increased number of physical objects that are accumulated within another physical object usually as a result of a failure to break down or remove objects in a timely manner.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16564-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16571-\n16572-[Term]\n16573:id: PATO:0002271\n16574-name: decreased accumulation\n16575-def: \"An accumulation which is relative low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16576-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16582-\n16583-[Term]\n16584:id: PATO:0002272\n16585-name: parallel to\n16586-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located at the same continuous distance relative to another object.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16587-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16592-\n16593-[Term]\n16594:id: PATO:0002273\n16595-name: marbled\n16596-def: \"Multicolored quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being colored with a variegated pattern resembling marble,.\" [url:http\\://www.oed.com/]\n16597-subset: value_slim\n--\n16601-\n16602-[Term]\n16603:id: PATO:0002274\n16604-name: mottled\n16605-def: \"Multicolored quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being dappled with spots, patches, or blotches of different colors.\" [url:http\\://www.oed.com/]\n16606-subset: value_slim\n--\n16610-\n16611-[Term]\n16612:id: PATO:0002275\n16613-name: high contrast color pattern\n16614-def: \"A color pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's color pattern in which light and dark colors (for example white and black) are codistributed to create a visual impression.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16615-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n16619-\n16620-[Term]\n16621:id: PATO:0002276\n16622-name: barred\n16623-def: \"A color pattern inhering in a bearer by virtue of bearer's exhibiting vertical bars of one hue or degree of saturation crossing another.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16624-subset: value_slim\n--\n16628-\n16629-[Term]\n16630:id: PATO:0002277\n16631-name: iridescent\n16632-def: \"A quality of certain surfaces which appear to change colour as the angle of view changes.\" [url:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iridescence]\n16633-is_a: PATO:0001615 ! variant color\n--\n16636-\n16637-[Term]\n16638:id: PATO:0002278\n16639-name: articulated with\n16640-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's participating in a joint with another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16641-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16645-\n16646-[Term]\n16647:id: PATO:0002279\n16648-name: tightly articulated with\n16649-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being strongly articulated with another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16650-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16654-\n16655-[Term]\n16656:id: PATO:0002280\n16657-name: broadly articulated with\n16658-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing a broad surface in articulation with another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16659-subset: relational_slim\n--\n16663-\n16664-[Term]\n16665:id: PATO:0002281\n16666-name: biscupidate\n16667-def: \"A cuscpidate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer possessing two cusps.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16668-synonym: \"bicuspid\" EXACT []\n--\n16672-\n16673-[Term]\n16674:id: PATO:0002282\n16675-name: increased mobility\n16676-def: \"A mobility which is relative high.\" [PATO:GVG]\n16677-subset: value_slim\n--\n16683-\n16684-[Term]\n16685:id: PATO:0002283\n16686-name: decreased mobility\n16687-def: \"A mobility which is relative low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16688-subset: value_slim\n--\n16694-\n16695-[Term]\n16696:id: PATO:0002284\n16697-name: tension\n16698-def: \"A physical quality that pertains by virtue of a pulling force that is directed away from the bearer and attempts to stretch or elongate the bearer.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16699-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n16704-\n16705-[Term]\n16706:id: PATO:0002285\n16707-name: increased branchiness\n16708-def: \"Branchiness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of increasing the degree to which there are subdivisions or offshoots in a bearer entity.\" [PATOC:CVS]\n16709-subset: value_slim\n--\n16714-\n16715-[Term]\n16716:id: PATO:0002286\n16717-name: decreased branchiness\n16718-def: \"Branchiness quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of decreasing the degree to which there are subdivisions or offshoots in a bearer entity.\" [PATOC:CVS]\n16719-subset: value_slim\n--\n16724-\n16725-[Term]\n16726:id: PATO:0002287\n16727-name: increased elasticity\n16728-def: \"An elasticity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16729-subset: value_slim\n--\n16735-\n16736-[Term]\n16737:id: PATO:0002288\n16738-name: decreased elasticity\n16739-def: \"An elasticity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16740-subset: value_slim\n--\n16746-\n16747-[Term]\n16748:id: PATO:0002289\n16749-name: setose\n16750-def: \"A hairy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being covered with setae.\" [ISBN:0913424137]\n16751-comment: Setose as a label is used extensively to describe insect phenotypes that have hairy-like appearances (i.e., they are covered in setae, not the hairs of mammals). A bristle is a type of seta.\n--\n16756-\n16757-[Term]\n16758:id: PATO:0002290\n16759-name: aplastic/hypoplastic\n16760-def: \"Decreased size or absence of organ, tissue or cell due to a reduction in cell numbers.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n16761-synonym: \"aplasia/hypoplasia\" EXACT []\n--\n16765-\n16766-[Term]\n16767:id: PATO:0002291\n16768-name: agenesis\n16769-def: \"Absence of a tissue or organ due to failure to develop.\" [PATO:GVG]\n16770-is_a: PATO:0040060 ! absence of anatomical entity\n--\n16773-\n16774-[Term]\n16775:id: PATO:0002292\n16776-name: transient\n16777-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's underlying structure being capable of change.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16778-comment: For example, structures undergoing endochondral ossification change in composition from cartilaginous to ossified.\n--\n16784-\n16785-[Term]\n16786:id: PATO:0002293\n16787-name: permanent\n16788-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's underlying structure not changing over time.\" [PATOC:WD]\n16789-synonym: \"permanent structure\" EXACT []\n--\n16793-\n16794-[Term]\n16795:id: PATO:0002294\n16796-name: scrobiculate\n16797-def: \"A texture that is uniformly covered in short, oblong, or trench-like depressions.\" [Book:Book]\n16798-is_a: PATO:0000150 ! texture\n--\n16801-\n16802-[Term]\n16803:id: PATO:0002295\n16804-name: areolate\n16805-def: \"A surface feature shape inhering in a surface by virtue of the bearer's being divided by ridge-like structures into a number of small, irregular spaces.\" [Book:Book]\n16806-subset: value_slim\n--\n16810-\n16811-[Term]\n16812:id: PATO:0002296\n16813-name: foveate\n16814-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a surface by virtue of the bearer's being marked by the presence of small, shallow, regular depressions called fovae.\" [Book:Book]\n16815-subset: value_slim\n--\n16821-\n16822-[Term]\n16823:id: PATO:0002297\n16824-name: decreased cellular motility\n16825-def: \"A cellular motility which is lower relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16826-subset: value_slim\n--\n16830-\n16831-[Term]\n16832:id: PATO:0002298\n16833-name: increased cellular motility\n16834-def: \"A cellular motility which is higher relative to the normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16835-subset: value_slim\n--\n16839-\n16840-[Term]\n16841:id: PATO:0002299\n16842-name: tubular\n16843-def: \"A cylindrical shape that is hollow.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16844-synonym: \"tube like\" EXACT []\n--\n16851-\n16852-[Term]\n16853:id: PATO:0002300\n16854-name: increased quality\n16855-def: \"A quality that has a value that is increased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16856-is_a: PATO:0000069 ! deviation (from_normal)\n--\n16861-\n16862-[Term]\n16863:id: PATO:0002301\n16864-name: decreased quality\n16865-def: \"A quality that has a value that is decreased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16866-is_a: PATO:0000069 ! deviation (from_normal)\n--\n16871-\n16872-[Term]\n16873:id: PATO:0002302\n16874-name: decreased process quality\n16875-def: \"A quality of a process that has a value that is decreased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16876-is_a: PATO:0001236 ! process quality\n--\n16881-\n16882-[Term]\n16883:id: PATO:0002303\n16884-name: decreased object quality\n16885-def: \"A quality of an object that has a value that is decreased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16886-is_a: PATO:0001241 ! physical object quality\n--\n16891-\n16892-[Term]\n16893:id: PATO:0002304\n16894-name: increased process quality\n16895-def: \"A quality of a process that has a value that is increased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16896-is_a: PATO:0001236 ! process quality\n--\n16901-\n16902-[Term]\n16903:id: PATO:0002305\n16904-name: increased object quality\n16905-def: \"A quality of an object that has a value that is increased compared to normal or average.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n16906-is_a: PATO:0001241 ! physical object quality\n--\n16911-\n16912-[Term]\n16913:id: PATO:0002306\n16914-name: equilateral triangular\n16915-def: \"A triangular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having all sides of the same length.\" [PATOC:JB]\n16916-subset: value_slim\n--\n16922-\n16923-[Term]\n16924:id: PATO:0002307\n16925-name: isosceles triangular\n16926-def: \"A triangular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two sides have the same length.\" [PATOC:JB]\n16927-subset: scalar_slim\n--\n16932-\n16933-[Term]\n16934:id: PATO:0002308\n16935-name: scalene triangular\n16936-def: \"A triangular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having all sides of unequal length.\" [PATOC:JB]\n16937-subset: value_slim\n--\n16941-\n16942-[Term]\n16943:id: PATO:0002309\n16944-name: fiber shaped\n16945-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a consistently sized and approximately round cross-section along its length, which is many times larger than its diameter.\" [PATOC:DC]\n16946-comment: Note that a fiber shaped object may take any circuitous or straight path through space (think of a length of string or rope).\n--\n16951-\n16952-[Term]\n16953:id: PATO:0002310\n16954-name: robust\n16955-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being strong, thick or sturdy.\" [PATOC:BF]\n16956-subset: value_slim\n--\n16960-\n16961-[Term]\n16962:id: PATO:0002311\n16963-name: fimbriated\n16964-def: \"Having a fringe or border of hairlike or fingerlike projections.\" [PATO:WS]\n16965-subset: value_slim\n--\n16969-\n16970-[Term]\n16971:id: PATO:0002312\n16972-name: segmented\n16973-def: \"Consisting of segments or similar parts arranged in a longitudinal series.\" [OED:]\n16974-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n16979-\n16980-[Term]\n16981:id: PATO:0002313\n16982-name: telescopic\n16983-def: \"Having or resembling the shape of a telescope.\" [PATOC:BF]\n16984-subset: value_slim\n--\n16988-\n16989-[Term]\n16990:id: PATO:0002314\n16991-name: ligamentous\n16992-def: \"Having the nature or characteristic of, a ligament; composed of the tissue proper to ligaments.\" [PATOC:BF]\n16993-subset: value_slim\n--\n16997-\n16998-[Term]\n16999:id: PATO:0002315\n17000-name: brush-like shape\n17001-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling the end of a brush with a multitude of bristles.\" [PATOC:BF]\n17002-subset: value_slim\n--\n17006-\n17007-[Term]\n17008:id: PATO:0002316\n17009-name: autogenous\n17010-def: \"Being separate or discrete from other skeletal elements.\" [PATOC:WD]\n17011-subset: value_slim\n--\n17016-\n17017-[Term]\n17018:id: PATO:0002317\n17019-name: parallelogram\n17020-def: \"A convex quadrilateral is a parallelogram if and only if any one of the following statements are true:\\n1. Each diagonal divides the quadrilateral into two congruent triangles with the same orientation.\\n2. The opposite sides are congruent in pairs.\\n3. The diagonals bisect each other.\\n4. The opposite angles are congruent in pairs.\\n5. The sum of the squares of the sides equals the sum of the squares of the diagonals. (This is the parallelogram law)\\n6.It possesses rotational symmetry.\\n7.One pair of opposite sides are parallel and congruent.\\n8.Two pairs of adjacent angles are supplementary.\" [wikipedia:Parallelogram]\n17021-subset: value_slim\n--\n17025-\n17026-[Term]\n17027:id: PATO:0002318\n17028-name: superelliptic\n17029-def: \"A shape constituting a transition between a rectangle and a circle; a closed curve, of which the circle and ellipse are special cases, whose parametric equation is x = a.cos2/rt, y = b.cos2/rt\" [wiktionary:superellipse]\n17030-synonym: \"Lamé curve\" EXACT []\n--\n17034-\n17035-[Term]\n17036:id: PATO:0002319\n17037-name: squircle\n17038-def: \"A shape with properties between those of a square and those of a circle.\" [wikipedia:Squircle]\n17039-subset: value_slim\n--\n17043-\n17044-[Term]\n17045:id: PATO:0002320\n17046-name: diamond shaped\n17047-def: \"A superelliptic shape inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape resembling a diamond.\" [PATO:WC]\n17048-subset: value_slim\n--\n17052-\n17053-[Term]\n17054:id: PATO:0002321\n17055-name: hypoelliptic\n17056-is_a: PATO:0002318 ! superelliptic\n17057-relationship: is_opposite_of PATO:0002322 ! hyperelliptic\n--\n17060-\n17061-[Term]\n17062:id: PATO:0002322\n17063-name: hyperelliptic\n17064-is_a: PATO:0002318 ! superelliptic\n17065-relationship: is_opposite_of PATO:0002321 ! hypoelliptic\n--\n17068-\n17069-[Term]\n17070:id: PATO:0002323\n17071-name: temporal distribution quality\n17072-def: \"A temporal distribution pattern of process occurrences within a regulation/reference process.\" [PATOC:LC]\n17073-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17077-\n17078-[Term]\n17079:id: PATO:0002324\n17080-name: offset quality\n17081-def: \"The temporal relation between the end of the process with respect to a reference process.\" [PATOC:LC]\n17082-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17088-\n17089-[Term]\n17090:id: PATO:0002325\n17091-name: onset quality\n17092-def: \"The temporal relation between the start of the process with respect to a reference process.\" [PATOC:LC]\n17093-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17098-\n17099-[Term]\n17100:id: PATO:0002326\n17101-name: angle\n17102-def: \"An orientation inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's placement at an angle.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17103-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17108-\n17109-[Term]\n17110:id: PATO:0002327\n17111-name: increased angle to\n17112-def: \"An angle which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17113-subset: relational_slim\n--\n17120-\n17121-[Term]\n17122:id: PATO:0002328\n17123-name: decreased angle to\n17124-def: \"An angle which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17125-subset: relational_slim\n--\n17132-\n17133-[Term]\n17134:id: PATO:0002329\n17135-name: hyponastic\n17136-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a upward bending of its leaves or other plant parts.\" [PATOC:DS]\n17137-subset: value_slim\n--\n17141-\n17142-[Term]\n17143:id: PATO:0002330\n17144-name: oblanceolate\n17145-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being extended along a straight line, and is shaped like a reversed lance-point, with the tapering point attached to the leafstalk.\" [PATOC:PG]\n17146-subset: value_slim\n--\n17150-\n17151-[Term]\n17152:id: PATO:0002331\n17153-name: adhesive\n17154-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer exhibiting molecular attraction to another entity in contact.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17155-subset: value_slim\n--\n17161-\n17162-[Term]\n17163:id: PATO:0002332\n17164-name: non-adhesive\n17165-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer not exhibiting molecular attraction to another entity in contact.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17166-subset: value_slim\n--\n17172-\n17173-[Term]\n17174:id: PATO:0002333\n17175-name: increased adhesivity\n17176-def: \"A adhesivity which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17177-subset: value_slim\n--\n17183-\n17184-[Term]\n17185:id: PATO:0002334\n17186-name: decreased adhesivity\n17187-def: \"A adhesivity which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17188-is_a: PATO:0002303 ! decreased object quality\n--\n17193-\n17194-[Term]\n17195:id: PATO:0002335\n17196-name: tholiform\n17197-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being dome-shaped.\" [PATOC:dd]\n17198-subset: value_slim\n--\n17202-\n17203-[Term]\n17204:id: PATO:0002336\n17205-name: pyramidal\n17206-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having triangular faces that meet at a common point and containing a polygonal shaped base.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17207-subset: value_slim\n--\n17211-\n17212-[Term]\n17213:id: PATO:0002337\n17214-name: lance-ovate\n17215-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a continuous convex surface with an axis of symmetry and one axis longer than the other; characterized with an egg-shaped form crossed with a lance-head shaped form.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17216-subset: value_slim\n--\n17220-\n17221-[Term]\n17222:id: PATO:0002338\n17223-name: lanceolate-triangular\n17224-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a lance-head, considerably longer than wide, tapering towards the tip from below the middle together forming three angles; attached at the broad end.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17225-subset: value_slim\n--\n17229-\n17230-[Term]\n17231:id: PATO:0002339\n17232-name: hispid\n17233-def: \"A quality of being covered with stiff or rough hairs.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17234-subset: value_slim\n--\n17238-\n17239-[Term]\n17240:id: PATO:0002340\n17241-name: hispidulous\n17242-def: \"A quality of being minutely hispid.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17243-subset: value_slim\n--\n17247-\n17248-[Term]\n17249:id: PATO:0002341\n17250-name: tomentose\n17251-def: \"A quality of being covered with short, dense, matted hairs.\" [thefreedictionary:www.thefreedictionary.com]\n17252-subset: value_slim\n--\n17256-\n17257-[Term]\n17258:id: PATO:0002342\n17259-name: cupulate\n17260-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being a cupule, with a structure similar to a cup that also encloses the ovule in partiality.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17261-subset: value_slim\n--\n17265-\n17266-[Term]\n17267:id: PATO:0002343\n17268-name: decumbent\n17269-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lying or growing on the ground but with erect or rising tips.\" [thefreedictionary:www.thefreedictionary.com]\n17270-subset: value_slim\n--\n17274-\n17275-[Term]\n17276:id: PATO:0002344\n17277-name: arachnose\n17278-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being characterized by fine, entangled hairs giving the appearance of cobweb.\" [PATOC:DD]\n17279-subset: value_slim\n--\n17283-\n17284-[Term]\n17285:id: PATO:0002345\n17286-name: lemon-shaped\n17287-def: \"A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a quadric surface in three dimensions obtained by rotating less than half of a circular arc about an axis passing through the endpoints of the arc\" [PATOC:MH]\n17288-subset: value_slim\n--\n17292-\n17293-[Term]\n17294:id: PATO:0002346\n17295-name: snowman-shaped\n17296-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two connected parts, roughly spherical, of different sizes.\" [PATOC:MH]\n17297-subset: value_slim\n--\n17301-\n17302-[Term]\n17303:id: PATO:0002347\n17304-name: obconical\n17305-def: \"A conical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a cone, with the pointed end attached to an organism.\" [wiktionary:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obconical]\n17306-subset: value_slim\n--\n17310-\n17311-[Term]\n17312:id: PATO:0002348\n17313-name: ligneous\n17314-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer resembling wood.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/ligneous]\n17315-subset: value_slim\n--\n17319-\n17320-[Term]\n17321:id: PATO:0002349\n17322-name: basal to\n17323-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the base of an organism relative to another entity.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/basal]\n17324-subset: value_slim\n--\n17328-\n17329-[Term]\n17330:id: PATO:0002350\n17331-name: cauline to\n17332-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the stalk of an organism relative to another entity.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/cauline]\n17333-subset: value_slim\n--\n17337-\n17338-[Term]\n17339:id: PATO:0002351\n17340-name: fleshy\n17341-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer resembling or containing flesh.\" [wiktionary:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fleshy]\n17342-subset: value_slim\n--\n17346-\n17347-[Term]\n17348:id: PATO:0002352\n17349-name: herbaceous\n17350-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's upper parts die back to the rootstock at the end of the growing season.\" [PATOC:PG]\n17351-subset: scalar_slim\n--\n17355-\n17356-[Term]\n17357:id: PATO:0002353\n17358-name: activation quality\n17359-def: \"A quality that inheres in a bearer in virtue of its realizing one of its functions.\" [PATOC:RH]\n17360-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17364-\n17365-[Term]\n17366:id: PATO:0002354\n17367-name: active\n17368-def: \"A quality of an physical object that is currently realizing one of its functions.\" [PATOC:RH]\n17369-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17374-\n17375-[Term]\n17376:id: PATO:0002355\n17377-name: inactive\n17378-def: \"A quality of a physical object that is currently realizing none of its functions.\" [PATOC:RH]\n17379-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17384-\n17385-[Term]\n17386:id: PATO:0002356\n17387-name: constitutively active\n17388-def: \"A quality of a physical object that has been constantly realizing some of its functions.\" [PATOC:RH]\n17389-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17393-\n17394-[Term]\n17395:id: PATO:0002357\n17396-name: D-shaped\n17397-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a strait side and an arched side giving the bearer the form of the letter D.\" [PATOC:AE]\n17398-subset: value_slim\n--\n17402-\n17403-[Term]\n17404:id: PATO:0002358\n17405-name: ridged\n17406-def: \"An elongated raised margin or border.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17407-subset: value_slim\n--\n17412-\n17413-[Term]\n17414:id: PATO:0002359\n17415-name: broad\n17416-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's width being notably higher than its length.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17417-subset: value_slim\n--\n17421-\n17422-[Term]\n17423:id: PATO:0002360\n17424-name: tendency\n17425-def: \"A disposition that can be compared on a linear scale - that is that it can be increased or decreased.\" [PATOC:RH]\n17426-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17432-\n17433-[Term]\n17434:id: PATO:0002361\n17435-name: increased tendency\n17436-def: \"A tendency which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17437-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n17445-\n17446-[Term]\n17447:id: PATO:0002362\n17448-name: decreased tendency\n17449-def: \"A tendency which is relatively low.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17450-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n17458-\n17459-[Term]\n17460:id: PATO:0002363\n17461-name: bronze\n17462-def: \"A medium brown color with a metallic sheen, resembles the actual alloy bronze.\" [PATO:LC]\n17463-subset: value_slim\n--\n17467-\n17468-[Term]\n17469:id: PATO:0002364\n17470-name: shortened\n17471-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's length being notably lower than its width.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17472-subset: value_slim\n--\n17477-\n17478-[Term]\n17479:id: PATO:0002365\n17480-name: intact female\n17481-def: \"Female quality of having complete, unaltered reproductive organs\" [PATOC:MF]\n17482-subset: value_slim\n--\n17486-\n17487-[Term]\n17488:id: PATO:0002366\n17489-name: intact male\n17490-def: \"Male quality of having complete, unaltered reproductive organs.\" [PATOC:MF]\n17491-subset: value_slim\n--\n17495-\n17496-[Term]\n17497:id: PATO:0002367\n17498-name: castrated male\n17499-def: \"Male quality of being incapable to reproduce because of functional loss of the testicles from surgical removal or chemical means.\" [PATOC:MF]\n17500-subset: value_slim\n--\n17504-\n17505-[Term]\n17506:id: PATO:0002368\n17507-name: nulliparous\n17508-def: \"A viviparous organism having never given birth.\" [PATOC:mf]\n17509-subset: value_slim\n--\n17513-\n17514-[Term]\n17515:id: PATO:0002369\n17516-name: multiparous\n17517-def: \"A viviparous organism that has given birth two or more times.\" [wiki:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_(biology)]\n17518-subset: value_slim\n--\n17523-\n17524-[Term]\n17525:id: PATO:0002370\n17526-name: parity\n17527-def: \"The number of time that a viviparous organism has given birth.\" [wiki:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_(biology)]\n17528-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17532-\n17533-[Term]\n17534:id: PATO:0002371\n17535-name: primiparous\n17536-def: \"A viviparous organism having given birth one time.\" [wiki:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_(biology)]\n17537-subset: value_slim\n--\n17542-\n17543-[Term]\n17544:id: PATO:0002372\n17545-name: grand multiparous\n17546-def: \"A viviparous organism that has given birth five or more times.\" [wiki:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_(biology)]\n17547-subset: value_slim\n--\n17551-\n17552-[Term]\n17553:id: PATO:0002373\n17554-name: mediolateral polarity\n17555-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's location of features or characteristics along the mediolateral axis.\" [PATOC:DS]\n17556-subset: value_slim\n--\n17560-\n17561-[Term]\n17562:id: PATO:0002374\n17563-name: fluctuating\n17564-def: \"Recurrent and often more or less cyclic alteration.\" [PATOC:DS]\n17565-subset: value_slim\n--\n17569-\n17570-[Term]\n17571:id: PATO:0002375\n17572-name: trumpet-shaped\n17573-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape form resembling the shape of a trumpet.\" [PATOC:DS]\n17574-subset: value_slim\n--\n17578-\n17579-[Term]\n17580:id: PATO:0002376\n17581-name: inflated\n17582-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being filled with air.\" [PATOC:CVS]\n17583-subset: value_slim\n--\n17589-\n17590-[Term]\n17591:id: PATO:0002377\n17592-name: uninflated\n17593-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being not filed with air.\" [PATOC:CVS]\n17594-subset: value_slim\n--\n17599-\n17600-[Term]\n17601:id: PATO:0002378\n17602-name: acinus\n17603-def: \"Having a shape that resembles a many-lobed \\\"berry,\\\" such as a raspberry.\" [wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acinus]\n17604-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17609-\n17610-[Term]\n17611:id: PATO:0002379\n17612-name: ovariohysterectomized female\n17613-def: \"A female fertility quality inhering in a female by virtue of the bearer's not being capable of reproducing because of surgical removal of ovaries and uterus.\" [PATOC:MF]\n17614-subset: value_slim\n--\n17618-\n17619-[Term]\n17620:id: PATO:0002380\n17621-name: ovariectomized female\n17622-def: \"A female fertility quality inhering in a female by virtue of the bearer's not being capable of reproducing because of surgical removal of ovaries.\" [PATOC:MF]\n17623-subset: value_slim\n--\n17627-\n17628-[Term]\n17629:id: PATO:0002381\n17630-name: waxiness\n17631-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the presence of long chain aliphatic lipids on the surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:lm]\n17632-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n17636-\n17637-[Term]\n17638:id: PATO:0002382\n17639-name: increased waxiness\n17640-def: \"A waxiness which is relatively high.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17641-subset: value_slim\n--\n17647-\n17648-[Term]\n17649:id: PATO:0002383\n17650-name: decreased waxiness\n17651-def: \"A waxiness which is relatively low.\" []\n17652-is_a: PATO:0002303 ! decreased object quality\n--\n17657-\n17658-[Term]\n17659:id: PATO:0002384\n17660-name: waxy\n17661-def: \"Presence of long chain aliphatic lipids on the surface of an organism.\" [PATOC:lm]\n17662-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17667-\n17668-[Term]\n17669:id: PATO:0002385\n17670-name: striate-angular\n17671-def: \"A shape 