ng in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's increased ability to endure a stimulus.\" [PATOC:LC]\n17749-subset: relational_slim\n--\n17756-\n17757-[Term]\n17758:id: PATO:0002394\n17759-name: decreased tolerance to\n17760-def: \"A tolerance quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's decreased ability to endure a stimulus.\" [PATOC:LC]\n17761-subset: relational_slim\n--\n17768-\n17769-[Term]\n17770:id: PATO:0002395\n17771-name: mislocalized abaxially\n17772-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned away from the axis of an organism.\" [PATOC:EH]\n17773-subset: value_slim\n--\n17777-\n17778-[Term]\n17779:id: PATO:0002396\n17780-name: mislocalized adaxially\n17781-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned towards the axis of an organism.\" [PATOC:EH]\n17782-subset: value_slim\n--\n17786-\n17787-[Term]\n17788:id: PATO:0002397\n17789-name: subcircular\n17790-def: \"A circular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being nearly, but not perfectly, circular.\" [PATOC:AD]\n17791-subset: value_slim\n--\n17797-\n17798-[Term]\n17799:id: PATO:0002398\n17800-name: obsolete <new term>\n17801-property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2061-091X\n17802-is_obsolete: true\n--\n17804-\n17805-[Term]\n17806:id: PATO:0002399\n17807-name: anteromedially rotated\n17808-def: \"A rotation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of being rotated towards the front and the middle of an organism.\" [PATOC:JI]\n17809-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17814-\n17815-[Term]\n17816:id: PATO:0002400\n17817-name: fusiform\n17818-def: \"Having a spindle-like shape that is wide in the middle and tapers at both ends.\" [wikipedia:wikipedia]\n17819-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17824-\n17825-[Term]\n17826:id: PATO:0002401\n17827-name: random pattern\n17828-def: \"characterised by an unidentifiable pattern.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17829-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17834-\n17835-[Term]\n17836:id: PATO:0002402\n17837-name: multifocal to coalescing\n17838-def: \"Multiple lesions some interconnecting with each other.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17839-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17844-\n17845-[Term]\n17846:id: PATO:0002403\n17847-name: generalized\n17848-def: \"Affecting all regions without specificity of distribution.\" [PATOC:MPTH]\n17849-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n17856-\n17857-[Term]\n17858:id: PATO:0002404\n17859-name: segmental\n17860-def: \"Affecting a segment or segments.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17861-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17866-\n17867-[Term]\n17868:id: PATO:0002405\n17869-name: friability\n17870-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to be reduced to smaller pieces with little effort.\" [Wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friability]\n17871-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17876-\n17877-[Term]\n17878:id: PATO:0002406\n17879-name: friable\n17880-def: \"Easily reduced to powder or easily fragmentable or crumbly.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17881-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17886-\n17887-[Term]\n17888:id: PATO:0002407\n17889-name: indurated\n17890-def: \"Having become firm or hard especially by increase of fibrous elements.\" [mw:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/indurated]\n17891-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17896-\n17897-[Term]\n17898:id: PATO:0002408\n17899-name: watery\n17900-def: \"Having the consistency of water.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17901-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17906-\n17907-[Term]\n17908:id: PATO:0002409\n17909-name: fluid-filled\n17910-def: \"Bounded structure filled with fluid.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17911-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17916-\n17917-[Term]\n17918:id: PATO:0002410\n17919-name: beige\n17920-def: \"A colour that is very pale yellowish brown.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17921-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17926-\n17927-[Term]\n17928:id: PATO:0002411\n17929-name: yellow brown\n17930-def: \"A color consisting of yellow and brown hue.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17931-subset: value_slim\n--\n17935-\n17936-[Term]\n17937:id: PATO:0002412\n17938-name: dark yellow brown\n17939-def: \"A color consisting of yellow and brown hue and low brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17940-subset: value_slim\n--\n17944-\n17945-[Term]\n17946:id: PATO:0002413\n17947-name: light yellow brown\n17948-def: \"A color consisting of yellow and brown hue and high brightness.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17949-is_a: PATO:0002411 ! yellow brown\n--\n17952-\n17953-[Term]\n17954:id: PATO:0002414\n17955-name: chronic-active\n17956-def: \"A quality of duration having progressive course of indefinite duration with active, acute-like elements.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17957-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17962-\n17963-[Term]\n17964:id: PATO:0002415\n17965-name: focally extensive\n17966-def: \"Single lesion with expansion into surrounding tissue.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17967-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17972-\n17973-[Term]\n17974:id: PATO:0002416\n17975-name: sunken\n17976-def: \"Flattened from above downward; below the normal level or the level of the surrounding parts.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17977-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17982-\n17983-[Term]\n17984:id: PATO:0002417\n17985-name: transmural\n17986-def: \"Extending through or affecting the entire thickness of the wall of an organ or cavity or boundary.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n17987-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n17992-\n17993-[Term]\n17994:id: PATO:0002418\n17995-name: acidophilic\n17996-def: \"An affinity inhering in an anatomical structure by virtue of the bearer exhibiting a molecular interaction for acidic dyes under specific pH conditions.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n17997-comment: Eosin stains acidophilic structures, hence eosinophilic is the same as acidophilic.\n--\n18004-\n18005-[Term]\n18006:id: PATO:0002419\n18007-name: obsolete eosinophilic\n18008-def: \"OBSOLETE. An affinity inhering in an anatomical structure by virtue of the bearer exhibiting a molecular interaction for eosin dye.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n18009-comment: Eosin stains acidophilic structures, hence eosinophilic is the same as acidophilic. See https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/471\n--\n18016-\n18017-[Term]\n18018:id: PATO:0002420\n18019-name: amphiphilic\n18020-def: \"Having both hydrophilic and hydrophobic (or lipophilic) groups.\" [wikipedia:http\\://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amphiphilic]\n18021-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n18026-\n18027-[Term]\n18028:id: PATO:0002421\n18029-name: cicatricial\n18030-def: \"Having or resembling the characteristic of a cicatrix - a scar resulting from formation and contraction of fibrous tissue.\" [mw:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/cicatricial]\n18031-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n18036-\n18037-[Term]\n18038:id: PATO:0002422\n18039-name: acinar\n18040-def: \"Pertaining to the individual parts making up an aggregate fruit like a many-lobed \\\"berry,\\\" such as a raspberry.\" [wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acinus]\n18041-comment: Acinus is Latin for berry.\n--\n18047-\n18048-[Term]\n18049:id: PATO:0002423\n18050-name: papillomatous\n18051-def: \"A round or lobulated protruding form resembling a nipple.\" [PATOC:MPATH]\n18052-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n18057-\n18058-[Term]\n18059:id: PATO:0002424\n18060-name: divergent from\n18061-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two or more entities that extend from a common point in different directions.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18062-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n18067-\n18068-[Term]\n18069:id: PATO:0002425\n18070-name: exposed\n18071-def: \"Open to view or not covered by another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18072-subset: value_slim\n--\n18076-\n18077-[Term]\n18078:id: PATO:0002426\n18079-name: scaphoid\n18080-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a boat.\" [wordnetweb:wordnetweb]\n18081-subset: value_slim\n--\n18085-\n18086-[Term]\n18087:id: PATO:0002427\n18088-name: knobbled\n18089-def: \"A surface feature shape having numerous very small circular rounded projections or protuberances.\" [thefreedictionary.com:thefreedictionary.com]\n18090-subset: value_slim\n--\n18094-\n18095-[Term]\n18096:id: PATO:0002428\n18097-name: tripodal\n18098-def: \"A 3-D shape with three supports or legs.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18099-subset: value_slim\n--\n18103-\n18104-[Term]\n18105:id: PATO:0002429\n18106-name: x-shaped\n18107-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of the letter X.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18108-subset: value_slim\n--\n18112-\n18113-[Term]\n18114:id: PATO:0002430\n18115-name: strap-shaped\n18116-def: \"A shape quality in which the bearer is shaped like a narrow band; ligulate.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n18117-subset: value_slim\n--\n18121-\n18122-[Term]\n18123:id: PATO:0002431\n18124-name: waisted\n18125-def: \"A shape quality in which the bearer possesses a gradual, yet distinct, thinning from a wide starting point.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18126-subset: value_slim\n--\n18130-\n18131-[Term]\n18132:id: PATO:0002432\n18133-name: spade-shaped\n18134-def: \"A shape that is in the form of a spade.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18135-subset: value_slim\n--\n18139-\n18140-[Term]\n18141:id: PATO:0002433\n18142-name: sculpted surface\n18143-def: \"A surface feature shape marked by large amounts of relief, often with multiple ridges and grooves in close association. Topographically complex.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18144-subset: value_slim\n--\n18148-\n18149-[Term]\n18150:id: PATO:0002434\n18151-name: perpendicular to\n18152-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located at a right angle relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18153-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18158-\n18159-[Term]\n18160:id: PATO:0002435\n18161-name: abutting\n18162-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer touching another entity along a border or with a projecting part.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n18163-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18170-\n18171-[Term]\n18172:id: PATO:0002436\n18173-name: offset\n18174-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's position being displaced from a reference point.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18175-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18180-\n18181-[Term]\n18182:id: PATO:0002437\n18183-name: interlocked with\n18184-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being locked together or interconnected to another entity.\" [merriam-webster:merriam-webster]\n18185-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18190-\n18191-[Term]\n18192:id: PATO:0002438\n18193-name: subdermal\n18194-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located or placed beneath the skin.\" [thefreedictionary:thefreedictionary]\n18195-subset: value_slim\n--\n18200-\n18201-[Term]\n18202:id: PATO:0002439\n18203-name: w-shaped\n18204-def: \"An angular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having two angles in its length giving the bearer the form of the letter W.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18205-subset: value_slim\n--\n18209-\n18210-[Term]\n18211:id: PATO:0002440\n18212-name: ornamentation\n18213-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the degree of the bearer's highly topographical with ridges, pits, rugosity or other surface structures.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n18214-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n18218-\n18219-[Term]\n18220:id: PATO:0002441\n18221-name: ornamented\n18222-def: \"A surface feature shape in which the bearer's surface is highly topographical with ridges, pits, rugosity or other surface structures.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18223-subset: value_slim\n--\n18228-\n18229-[Term]\n18230:id: PATO:0002442\n18231-name: unornamented\n18232-def: \"A surface feature shape in which the bearer's surface is lacking ridges, pits, rugosity or other surface structures.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18233-subset: value_slim\n--\n18238-\n18239-[Term]\n18240:id: PATO:0002443\n18241-name: level with\n18242-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located at the same level as another entity.\" [PATOC:NI]\n18243-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18248-\n18249-[Term]\n18250:id: PATO:0002444\n18251-name: mineralized\n18252-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being composed of or possessing inorganic material.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18253-subset: value_slim\n--\n18257-\n18258-[Term]\n18259:id: PATO:0002445\n18260-name: torsioned\n18261-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being twisted or turned.\" [freedictionary:freedictionary]\n18262-comment: The word \"torsion\" has multiple different meanings in different context (e.g. the act of twisting or the morphology of the digestive tract in gastropods). This term refers purely to the resulting shape and is not to be used in the engineering and mechanics sense of torsion. \\nNote: kinked PATO:0001798(synonym twisted) is similar to 'torsioned', but it is different in that something that is kinked has sharp twists or turns.\n--\n18267-\n18268-[Term]\n18269:id: PATO:0002446\n18270-name: anchor-shaped\n18271-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape resembling an anchor.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18272-subset: value_slim\n--\n18276-\n18277-[Term]\n18278:id: PATO:0002447\n18279-name: quadripartite\n18280-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being divided into four parts.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18281-subset: value_slim\n--\n18285-\n18286-[Term]\n18287:id: PATO:0002448\n18288-name: oriented towards\n18289-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being aligned or positioned towards another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18290-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18295-\n18296-[Term]\n18297:id: PATO:0002449\n18298-name: posteromedial to\n18299-def: \"A spatial quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located toward the rear and mid-line surface of an organism relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18300-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18305-\n18306-[Term]\n18307:id: PATO:0002450\n18308-name: firm\n18309-def: \"A hardness quality of giving significant resistance to pressure.\" [PATOC:CM]\n18310-subset: value_slim\n--\n18314-\n18315-[Term]\n18316:id: PATO:0002451\n18317-name: sexually dimorphic\n18318-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a phenotypic difference between males and females of the same species.\" [PATOC:WC]\n18319-subset: value_slim\n--\n18323-\n18324-[Term]\n18325:id: PATO:0002452\n18326-name: decondensed\n18327-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being thinner or more loosely packed.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18328-subset: value_slim\n--\n18333-\n18334-[Term]\n18335:id: PATO:0002453\n18336-name: eroding\n18337-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer bring gradually worn away.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18338-subset: value_slim\n--\n18342-\n18343-[Term]\n18344:id: PATO:0002454\n18345-name: carpel-like\n18346-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a carpel.\" [PATO:JL]\n18347-subset: value_slim\n--\n18351-\n18352-[Term]\n18353:id: PATO:0002455\n18354-name: corymb-like\n18355-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's architecture bearing resemblence to a corymb type of inflorescence.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18356-subset: value_slim\n--\n18360-\n18361-[Term]\n18362:id: PATO:0002456\n18363-name: inflorescence-like\n18364-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of an inflorescence.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18365-subset: value_slim\n--\n18369-\n18370-[Term]\n18371:id: PATO:0002457\n18372-name: leaf-like\n18373-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a leaf.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18374-subset: value_slim\n--\n18378-\n18379-[Term]\n18380:id: PATO:0002458\n18381-name: pin-like\n18382-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being thin and lacking outgrowths.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18383-subset: value_slim\n--\n18387-\n18388-[Term]\n18389:id: PATO:0002459\n18390-name: sepal-like\n18391-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a sepal,\" [PATOC:JL]\n18392-subset: value_slim\n--\n18396-\n18397-[Term]\n18398:id: PATO:0002460\n18399-name: shriveled\n18400-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being smaller and contracted, especially due to loss of moisture.\" [PATOC:JL]\n18401-subset: value_slim\n--\n18405-\n18406-[Term]\n18407:id: PATO:0002461\n18408-name: wilty\n18409-def: \"To bend or hang downwards due to loss of water\" []\n18410-subset: value_slim\n--\n18414-\n18415-[Term]\n18416:id: PATO:0002462\n18417-name: collagenous\n18418-def: \"A composition quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of collagen.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18419-subset: value_slim\n--\n18423-\n18424-[Term]\n18425:id: PATO:0002463\n18426-name: extends to\n18427-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of some aspect of the bearer extending to the position of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18428-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18432-\n18433-[Term]\n18434:id: PATO:0002464\n18435-name: extends beyond\n18436-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of some aspect of the bearer extending past the position of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18437-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18441-\n18442-[Term]\n18443:id: PATO:0002465\n18444-name: prism shaped\n18445-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a prism.\" []\n18446-subset: value_slim\n--\n18451-\n18452-[Term]\n18453:id: PATO:0002466\n18454-name: keyhole shaped\n18455-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer resembling a keyhole.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18456-subset: value_slim\n--\n18460-\n18461-[Term]\n18462:id: PATO:0002467\n18463-name: lathlike\n18464-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer resembling a thin narrow strip.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18465-subset: value_slim\n--\n18469-\n18470-[Term]\n18471:id: PATO:0002468\n18472-name: distensible\n18473-def: \"A structure quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being capable of swelling or stretching.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18474-subset: value_slim\n--\n18478-\n18479-[Term]\n18480:id: PATO:0002469\n18481-name: sutured to\n18482-def: \"Structural quality inhering in a bearer in which a joint has apposed bony surfaces united by fibrous tissue, permitting no movement; found only between bones.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18483-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18488-\n18489-[Term]\n18490:id: PATO:0002470\n18491-name: transformed to\n18492-def: \"A morphological quality between two bearers inhering that one bearer is subject to change the nature, function, or condition of itself to become the other.\" [PATOC:LC]\n18493-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18498-\n18499-[Term]\n18500:id: PATO:0002471\n18501-name: increased velocity\n18502-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's increased rate of change of the position.\" [PATOC:NV]\n18503-subset: value_slim\n--\n18509-\n18510-[Term]\n18511:id: PATO:0002472\n18512-name: decreased velocity\n18513-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's decreased rate of change of the position.\" [PATOC:NV]\n18514-subset: value_slim\n--\n18520-\n18521-[Term]\n18522:id: PATO:0002473\n18523-name: neoplastic, spontaneous\n18524-def: \"A disposition inhering in a tumour by virtue of the bearer's disposition to spontaneously arise.\" [PATOC:NV]\n18525-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n18530-\n18531-[Term]\n18532:id: PATO:0002474\n18533-name: bitter\n18534-def: \"A flavor quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an acrid, sharp, or disagreeable flavor.\" [PATOC:LC]\n18535-subset: value_slim\n--\n18539-\n18540-[Term]\n18541:id: PATO:0002475\n18542-name: subterminal\n18543-def: \"A position quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's existing near the end of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18544-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18549-\n18550-[Term]\n18551:id: PATO:0002476\n18552-name: terminal\n18553-def: \"A position quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's forming the end of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18554-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18559-\n18560-[Term]\n18561:id: PATO:0002477\n18562-name: brittle\n18563-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to breaks without significant deformation (strain) when subjected to stress.\" [wikipedia:http\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brittleness]\n18564-subset: value_slim\n--\n18568-\n18569-[Term]\n18570:id: PATO:0002478\n18571-name: transversely striated\n18572-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by narrow lines or grooves, usually parallel, that are oriented transversely relative to the long axis of the bearer.\" [PATOC:DS]\n18573-subset: cell_quality\n--\n18579-\n18580-[Term]\n18581:id: PATO:0002479\n18582-name: obliquely striated\n18583-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by narrow lines or grooves, usually parallel, that are oriented obliquely relative to the long axis of the bearer.\" [PATOC:DS]\n18584-subset: cell_quality\n--\n18590-\n18591-[Term]\n18592:id: PATO:0002480\n18593-name: poorly ossified\n18594-def: \"A quality inhering in an bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing only minor levels of ossification.\" [PATOC:AD]\n18595-subset: value_slim\n--\n18599-\n18600-[Term]\n18601:id: PATO:0002481\n18602-name: oblique orientation\n18603-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a slanting direction or position : neither perpendicular nor parallel.\" [merriam-wester:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/oblique]\n18604-subset: value_slim\n--\n18608-\n18609-[Term]\n18610:id: PATO:0002482\n18611-name: slit-like\n18612-def: \"Shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer exhibiting a narrow and elongate opening.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18613-subset: value_slim\n--\n18617-\n18618-[Term]\n18619:id: PATO:0002483\n18620-name: external to\n18621-def: \"Positional quality in which an entity is located outside of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18622-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18627-\n18628-[Term]\n18629:id: PATO:0002484\n18630-name: inverted-V shaped\n18631-def: \"An angular shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a single angle in its length giving the bearer the form of an inverted letter V.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18632-subset: value_slim\n--\n18637-\n18638-[Term]\n18639:id: PATO:0002485\n18640-name: parallel-sided\n18641-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing two sides that are at the same continuous distance relative to each other.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18642-subset: value_slim\n--\n18646-\n18647-[Term]\n18648:id: PATO:0002486\n18649-name: multi-organismal process quality\n18650-def: \"A quality inhering in a process by virtue of that process having two or more organisms as participants.\" [PATOC:DS]\n18651-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n18655-\n18656-[Term]\n18657:id: PATO:0002487\n18658-name: single organismal process quality\n18659-def: \"A quality inhering in a process by virtue of that process having exactly one organism as a participant.\" [PATOC:DS]\n18660-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n18665-\n18666-[Term]\n18667:id: PATO:0002488\n18668-name: overlapping\n18669-def: \"Overlap with quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned over another entity so as to cover some portion of it.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18670-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18675-\n18676-[Term]\n18677:id: PATO:0002489\n18678-name: overlapped by\n18679-def: \"Overlap with quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being positioned under another entity so as to be covered by some portion of it.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18680-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18685-\n18686-[Term]\n18687:id: PATO:0002490\n18688-name: anterior orientation\n18689-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anteriorly.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18690-subset: value_slim\n--\n18695-\n18696-[Term]\n18697:id: PATO:0002491\n18698-name: anterodorsal orientation\n18699-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anterodorsally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18700-subset: value_slim\n--\n18706-\n18707-[Term]\n18708:id: PATO:0002492\n18709-name: anterolateral orientation\n18710-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anterolaterally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18711-subset: value_slim\n--\n18716-\n18717-[Term]\n18718:id: PATO:0002493\n18719-name: anteroventral orientation\n18720-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anteroventrally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18721-subset: value_slim\n--\n18726-\n18727-[Term]\n18728:id: PATO:0002494\n18729-name: distal orientation\n18730-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed distally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18731-subset: value_slim\n--\n18737-\n18738-[Term]\n18739:id: PATO:0002495\n18740-name: dorsal orientation\n18741-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed dorsally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18742-subset: value_slim\n--\n18748-\n18749-[Term]\n18750:id: PATO:0002496\n18751-name: dorsolateral orientation\n18752-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed dorsolaterally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18753-subset: value_slim\n--\n18758-\n18759-[Term]\n18760:id: PATO:0002497\n18761-name: lateral orientation\n18762-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed laterally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18763-subset: value_slim\n--\n18768-\n18769-[Term]\n18770:id: PATO:0002498\n18771-name: medial orientation\n18772-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed medially.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18773-subset: value_slim\n--\n18778-\n18779-[Term]\n18780:id: PATO:0002499\n18781-name: posterior orientation\n18782-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed posteriorly.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18783-subset: value_slim\n--\n18788-\n18789-[Term]\n18790:id: PATO:0002500\n18791-name: ventrolaterally orientation\n18792-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed ventrolaterally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18793-subset: value_slim\n--\n18798-\n18799-[Term]\n18800:id: PATO:0002501\n18801-name: ventral orientation\n18802-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed ventrally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18803-subset: value_slim\n--\n18808-\n18809-[Term]\n18810:id: PATO:0002502\n18811-name: transverse orientation\n18812-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed transversely.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18813-subset: value_slim\n--\n18818-\n18819-[Term]\n18820:id: PATO:0002503\n18821-name: posterolateral orientation\n18822-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed posterolaterally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18823-subset: value_slim\n--\n18828-\n18829-[Term]\n18830:id: PATO:0002504\n18831-name: posterodorsal orientation\n18832-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed posterodorsally.\" [PATOC:WD]\n18833-subset: value_slim\n--\n18839-\n18840-[Term]\n18841:id: PATO:0002505\n18842-name: nucleated\n18843-def: \"A nucleate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having one or more nucleus.\" [PATOC:GVG]\n18844-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n18849-\n18850-[Term]\n18851:id: PATO:0002506\n18852-name: alobate\n18853-def: \"A surface feature shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's not having undulating edges forming lobes.\" [PATOC:DOS]\n18854-subset: value_slim\n--\n18858-\n18859-[Term]\n18860:id: PATO:0002507\n18861-name: keratinous\n18862-def: \"A composition quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's consisting of keratin.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18863-subset: value_slim\n--\n18867-\n18868-[Term]\n18869:id: PATO:0002508\n18870-name: concealed\n18871-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being hidden from view.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18872-subset: value_slim\n--\n18876-\n18877-[Term]\n18878:id: PATO:0002509\n18879-name: hexagonal\n18880-def: \"A 2-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having six angles and six sides.\" [Merriam-Webster:hexagonal]\n18881-subset: value_slim\n--\n18885-\n18886-[Term]\n18887:id: PATO:0002510\n18888-name: multipartite\n18889-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being divided into multiple parts.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18890-subset: value_slim\n--\n18894-\n18895-[Term]\n18896:id: PATO:0002511\n18897-name: cane-like\n18898-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a cane.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18899-subset: value_slim\n--\n18904-\n18905-[Term]\n18906:id: PATO:0002512\n18907-name: confluent with\n18908-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer flowing or coming together with another entity.\" [Merriam-Webster:confluent]\n18909-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18914-\n18915-[Term]\n18916:id: PATO:0002513\n18917-name: oblique to\n18918-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a slanting direction (neither perpendicular nor parallel) relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18919-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18924-\n18925-[Term]\n18926:id: PATO:0002514\n18927-name: anteromedial orientation\n18928-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anteromedially.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18929-subset: value_slim\n--\n18934-\n18935-[Term]\n18936:id: PATO:0002515\n18937-name: increased elevation relative to\n18938-def: \"An elevation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue the bearer's being in a high position relative to another entity.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18939-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18944-\n18945-[Term]\n18946:id: PATO:0002516\n18947-name: concealed by\n18948-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being hidden from view or covered by another entity.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18949-subset: relational_slim\n--\n18954-\n18955-[Term]\n18956:id: PATO:0002517\n18957-name: saddle-shaped\n18958-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a saddle.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18959-subset: value_slim\n--\n18963-\n18964-[Term]\n18965:id: PATO:0002518\n18966-name: flush\n18967-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being level or even with another surface.\" [WordReference:flush]\n18968-subset: value_slim\n--\n18972-\n18973-[Term]\n18974:id: PATO:0002519\n18975-name: cancellous\n18976-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an open, latticed, or porous structure; used especially of bone.\" [TheFreeDictionary:cancellous]\n18977-subset: value_slim\n--\n18981-\n18982-[Term]\n18983:id: PATO:0002520\n18984-name: scute-like\n18985-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being shaped like a scute or an osteoderm.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18986-subset: value_slim\n--\n18990-\n18991-[Term]\n18992:id: PATO:0002521\n18993-name: funnel-shaped\n18994-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a funnel.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n18995-subset: value_slim\n--\n18999-\n19000-[Term]\n19001:id: PATO:0002522\n19002-name: keel-shaped\n19003-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having an elongate structure, similar to a ridge, that extends longitudinally along an anatomical entity.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19004-subset: value_slim\n--\n19008-\n19009-[Term]\n19010:id: PATO:0002523\n19011-name: vertical to\n19012-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located at a right angle relative to another entity and to the horizon.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19013-subset: relational_slim\n--\n19018-\n19019-[Term]\n19020:id: PATO:0002524\n19021-name: mesiolateral orientation\n19022-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed mesiolaterally.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19023-subset: value_slim\n--\n19027-\n19028-[Term]\n19029:id: PATO:0002525\n19030-name: separating\n19031-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being in a position that produces a separation in, or acting to separate, another entity.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19032-subset: relational_slim\n--\n19037-\n19038-[Term]\n19039:id: PATO:0002526\n19040-name: anterodistal orientation\n19041-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed anterodistally.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19042-synonym: \"antero-distal orientation\" EXACT []\n--\n19047-\n19048-[Term]\n19049:id: PATO:0002527\n19050-name: posterodistal orientation\n19051-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed posterodistally.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19052-synonym: \"postero-distal orientation\" EXACT []\n--\n19057-\n19058-[Term]\n19059:id: PATO:0002528\n19060-name: obsolete borderline intensity\n19061-comment: obsoleted because the ID was accidentally reused\n19062-is_obsolete: true\n--\n19064-\n19065-[Term]\n19066:id: PATO:0002529\n19067-name: obsolete profound intensity\n19068-comment: obsoleted because the ID was accidentally reused\n19069-is_obsolete: true\n--\n19071-\n19072-[Term]\n19073:id: PATO:0002530\n19074-name: obsolete episodic\n19075-comment: obsoleted because the ID was accidentally reused\n19076-is_obsolete: true\n--\n19078-\n19079-[Term]\n19080:id: PATO:0002531\n19081-name: obsolete refractory\n19082-comment: obsoleted because the ID was accidentally reused\n19083-is_obsolete: true\n--\n19085-\n19086-[Term]\n19087:id: PATO:0002532\n19088-name: obsolete secondary\n19089-comment: obsoleted because the ID was accidentally reused\n19090-is_obsolete: true\n--\n19092-\n19093-[Term]\n19094:id: PATO:0002533\n19095-name: bipartite\n19096-def: \"A multipartite quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being divided into two parts.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19097-subset: value_slim\n--\n19101-\n19102-[Term]\n19103:id: PATO:0002534\n19104-name: plowshare shaped\n19105-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a plowshare.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19106-subset: value_slim\n--\n19112-\n19113-[Term]\n19114:id: PATO:0002535\n19115-name: peg-like\n19116-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a short and stout cylindrical shape.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19117-subset: value_slim\n--\n19121-\n19122-[Term]\n19123:id: PATO:0002536\n19124-name: boomerang shaped\n19125-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape like a boomerang, with two arms connected at an angle.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19126-subset: value_slim\n--\n19130-\n19131-[Term]\n19132:id: PATO:0002537\n19133-name: subovoid\n19134-def: \"A spheroid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting a shape not quite ovoid. approximately ovoid.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/subovoid]\n19135-subset: value_slim\n--\n19139-\n19140-[Term]\n19141:id: PATO:0002538\n19142-name: concavo-convex\n19143-def: \"A shape quality that obtains by virtue of the bearer being concave on one side and convex on the other.\" [merriam-webster:http\\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/concavo-convex]\n19144-subset: value_slim\n--\n19149-\n19150-[Term]\n19151:id: PATO:0002539\n19152-name: ring shaped\n19153-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape like a ring (a circular shape enclosing a space).\" [PATOC:WD]\n19154-subset: value_slim\n--\n19160-\n19161-[Term]\n19162:id: PATO:0002540\n19163-name: spur shaped\n19164-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing a small, spike-like shape.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19165-subset: value_slim\n--\n19169-\n19170-[Term]\n19171:id: PATO:0002541\n19172-name: homeostatic\n19173-def: \"Pertaining to the ability or tendency of an organism or cell to maintain internal equilibrium by adjusting its physiological processes.\" [GO:0042592]\n19174-is_a: PATO:0001995 ! organismal quality\n--\n19177-\n19178-[Term]\n19179:id: PATO:0002628\n19180-name: borderline intensity\n19181-def: \"An intensity which is borderline in it its effect or force as compared to baseline or normal.\" []\n19182-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n19186-\n19187-[Term]\n19188:id: PATO:0002629\n19189-name: profound intensity\n19190-def: \"An intensity which is characterized by being very severe.\" [PATO:MAH]\n19191-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n19195-\n19196-[Term]\n19197:id: PATO:0002630\n19198-name: episodic\n19199-def: \"An occurrence quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a course that occurs occasionally.\" [PATO:MAH]\n19200-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n19204-\n19205-[Term]\n19206:id: PATO:0002631\n19207-name: refractory\n19208-def: \"An occurrence of a process during which time there is an inability to change the course, extent, or repetition of the process.\" [PATO:MAH]\n19209-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n19213-\n19214-[Term]\n19215:id: PATO:0002632\n19216-name: secondary\n19217-def: \"A quality in which the effect or outcome is not primary or the focus of the observation.\" [PATO:MAH]\n19218-subset: hpo_slim\n--\n19222-\n19223-[Term]\n19224:id: PATO:0005000\n19225-name: hemispheroid\n19226-def: \"A 3-D shape that is half of a sphere.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19227-subset: value_slim\n--\n19231-\n19232-[Term]\n19233:id: PATO:0005001\n19234-name: variability of count\n19235-def: \"A variability quality inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer having a variable number or count of an entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19236-subset: value_slim\n--\n19242-\n19243-[Term]\n19244:id: PATO:0005002\n19245-name: pear shaped\n19246-def: \"Having the shape of a pear; tapering near the top and bulging toward the base or bottom. From thefreedictionary.com\" [PATOC:WD]\n19247-subset: value_slim\n--\n19251-\n19252-[Term]\n19253:id: PATO:0005003\n19254-name: paddle shaped\n19255-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling the form of a paddle.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19256-subset: value_slim\n--\n19260-\n19261-[Term]\n19262:id: PATO:0005004\n19263-name: subelliptical\n19264-def: \"A shape that is almost an ellipse.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19265-subset: value_slim\n--\n19269-\n19270-[Term]\n19271:id: PATO:0005005\n19272-name: radiating\n19273-def: \"Shape quality inhering in a bearer expanding outward, or having parts expanding outward, from a center point.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19274-subset: value_slim\n--\n19278-\n19279-[Term]\n19280:id: PATO:0005006\n19281-name: differentiated from\n19282-def: \"A morphology quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being morphologically distinguishable from another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19283-subset: relational_slim\n--\n19289-\n19290-[Term]\n19291:id: PATO:0005007\n19292-name: hypsodont\n19293-def: \"A 3-D shape inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having dentition characterized by high-crowned teeth and enamel which extends far past the gum line, which provides extra material for wear and tear.\" [DOI:10.1111/j.1469-185X.2011.00176.x]\n19294-comment: Need to include axiom: hypsodont inheres_in some ('tooth crown' and bearer_of 'increased \\nheight').\n--\n19299-\n19300-[Term]\n19301:id: PATO:0005008\n19302-name: brachydont\n19303-def: \"A 3-D shape inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having dentition characterized by low-crowned teeth. Human teeth are brachydont.\" [DOI:10.1111/j.1469-185X.2011.00176.x]\n19304-comment: Need to include axiom: brachydont inheres_in some ('tooth crown' and bearer_of 'decreased \\nheight').\n--\n19309-\n19310-[Term]\n19311:id: PATO:0005009\n19312-name: molariform\n19313-def: \"A 3-D shape inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an entity in the form of a molar tooth.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19314-subset: value_slim\n--\n19318-\n19319-[Term]\n19320:id: PATO:0005010\n19321-name: plumose\n19322-def: \"A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having many fine filaments or branches that give a feathery appearance: for example, resembling a feather.\" [www.oxforddictionaries.com:http\\://www.oxforddictionaries.com/us/definition/american_english/plumose]\n19323-subset: value_slim\n--\n19327-\n19328-[Term]\n19329:id: PATO:0005011\n19330-name: continuous with\n19331-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer possessing an uninterrupted or unbroken connection or spatial distribution relative to the position of another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19332-subset: relational_slim\n--\n19337-\n19338-[Term]\n19339:id: PATO:0005012\n19340-name: complete structure\n19341-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being fully formed compared to entities lacking parts.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19342-subset: value_slim\n--\n19347-\n19348-[Term]\n19349:id: PATO:0005013\n19350-name: incomplete structure\n19351-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lacking parts or having a reduced form compared to fully formed entities.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19352-subset: value_slim\n--\n19357-\n19358-[Term]\n19359:id: PATO:0005014\n19360-name: subspherical\n19361-def: \"A spheroid shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being nearly, but not perfectly, spherical.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19362-subset: value_slim\n--\n19366-\n19367-[Term]\n19368:id: PATO:0005015\n19369-name: tapered size\n19370-def: \"A size quality inhering in an entity or set of entities in which size increases or decreases along the extent of the entity or set.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19371-subset: value_slim\n--\n19376-\n19377-[Term]\n19378:id: PATO:0005016\n19379-name: surrounded by\n19380-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being enclosed on all sides by another entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19381-subset: relational_slim\n--\n19387-\n19388-[Term]\n19389:id: PATO:0005017\n19390-name: labiolingually compressed\n19391-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being compressed from the side facing the lips to the side facing the tongue.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19392-subset: value_slim\n--\n19396-\n19397-[Term]\n19398:id: PATO:0005018\n19399-name: mesiodistally compressed\n19400-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being compressed from the side facing the midline of the jaw to the side opposite the midline.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19401-subset: value_slim\n--\n19405-\n19406-[Term]\n19407:id: PATO:0005019\n19408-name: curved lingually\n19409-def: \"A curvature quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved towards the tongue.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19410-subset: value_slim\n--\n19414-\n19415-[Term]\n19416:id: PATO:0005020\n19417-name: irregularly shaped\n19418-def: \"A shape quality inhering on a bearer by virtue of a bearer's shape lacking in pattern or uniformity; for example, it may have sides of different lengths, different curvatures, or unequal angles.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19419-subset: value_slim\n--\n19423-\n19424-[Term]\n19425:id: PATO:0005021\n19426-name: unicuspidate\n19427-def: \"Cuspidate quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's possessing a single cusp.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19428-subset: value_slim\n--\n19432-\n19433-[Term]\n19434:id: PATO:0005022\n19435-name: uniform diameter\n19436-def: \"A diameter that remains constant throughout the extent of an entity.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19437-subset: value_slim\n--\n19441-\n19442-[Term]\n19443:id: PATO:0005023\n19444-name: parasagittal orientation\n19445-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is in the parasagittal plane.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19446-subset: value_slim\n--\n19450-\n19451-[Term]\n19452:id: PATO:0005024\n19453-name: longitudinal orientation\n19454-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed along the longitudinal or anterior-posterior axis.\" [PATOC:WD]\n19455-subset: value_slim\n--\n19459-\n19460-[Term]\n19461:id: PATO:0010000\n19462-name: maximally connected\n19463-def: \"A structural quality inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer consisting of a single, maximally connected structure.\" [GOC:dos]\n19464-comment: What counts as maximally connected may be relative to some specification of granularity.\n--\n19468-\n19469-[Term]\n19470:id: PATO:0010001\n19471-name: disconnected\n19472-def: \"A structural quality inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer consisting of multiple structures lacking any physical connection to each other.\" [GOC:dos]\n19473-is_a: PATO:0000141 ! structure\n--\n19476-\n19477-[Term]\n19478:id: PATO:0010002\n19479-name: propagation velocity\n19480-def: \"The velocity of spatial propagation of a process. Examples include the velocity of propagation of an action potential along an axon.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]\n19481-is_a: PATO:0002062 ! physical quality of a process\n--\n19484-\n19485-[Term]\n19486:id: PATO:0010003\n19487-name: increased propagation velocity\n19488-def: \"A propagation velocity that is higher than normal.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]\n19489-is_a: PATO:0002304 ! increased process quality\n--\n19493-\n19494-[Term]\n19495:id: PATO:0010004\n19496-name: decreased propagation velocity\n19497-def: \"A propagation velocity that is lower than normal.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]\n19498-is_a: PATO:0002302 ! decreased process quality\n--\n19502-\n19503-[Term]\n19504:id: PATO:0010005\n19505-name: spatial distribution of a process\n19506-def: \"A physical quality of a process that is its spatial distribution. For example, bone mineralization follows stereotypical spatial distribution patterns during development, which may be altered in some phenotypes.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]\n19507-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19511-\n19512-[Term]\n19513:id: PATO:0010006\n19514-name: cell morphology\n19515-def: \"A quality of a single cell inhering in the bearer by virtue of the bearer's size or shape or structure.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]\n19516-comment: Use this term for morphologies that can *only* inhere in a cell, e.g. morphological qualities inhering in a cell by virtue of the presence, location or shape of one or more cell parts.\n--\n19520-\n19521-[Term]\n19522:id: PATO:0010007\n19523-name: multiciliated\n19524-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having multiple cilia.\" [PMID:36924208]\n19525-is_a: PATO:0001408 ! ciliated\n--\n19528-\n19529-[Term]\n19530:id: PATO:0010008\n19531-name: monociliated\n19532-def: \"A cellular quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having only one cilium.\" [PMID:36924208]\n19533-is_a: PATO:0001408 ! ciliated\n--\n19536-\n19537-[Term]\n19538:id: PATO:0015001\n19539-name: absence due to degeneration\n19540-def: \"Absence due to a degenerative process.\" [PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n19541-subset: absent_slim\n--\n19546-\n19547-[Term]\n19548:id: PATO:0015002\n19549-name: process efficacy\n19550-def: \"The ability of a process to produce its output.\" [PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n19551-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19554-\n19555-[Term]\n19556:id: PATO:0015003\n19557-name: decreased efficacy\n19558-def: \"A decrease in the ability of a process to produce its output.\" [PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n19559-subset: value_slim\n--\n19564-\n19565-[Term]\n19566:id: PATO:0015004\n19567-name: increased efficacy\n19568-def: \"A increase in the ability of a process to produce its output.\" [PATOC:PortlandMeetingFeb2015]\n19569-subset: value_slim\n--\n19574-\n19575-[Term]\n19576:id: PATO:0015005\n19577-name: tendrilous\n19578-def: \"Slender and spirally coiled.\" [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tendril]\n19579-subset: value_slim\n--\n19586-\n19587-[Term]\n19588:id: PATO:0015006\n19589-name: polymeric\n19590-def: \"A quality inhering in a structure by virtue of it consisting of many of repeated, similar or identical subunits, arranged in some orderly array.\" [GOC:DOS, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/78]\n19591-comment: A complete coverage of this domain would subclasses homopolymeric, copolymeric, crystalline.\n--\n19594-\n19595-[Term]\n19596:id: PATO:0015007\n19597-name: prominence\n19598-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the degree to which the bearers stands out or projects beyond a surface or line.\" [GOC:CJM]\n19599-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19601-\n19602-[Term]\n19603:id: PATO:0015008\n19604-name: distensibility\n19605-def: \"A quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the extent to which the bearer is capable of being stretched or swollen.\" [GOC:CJM]\n19606-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19608-\n19609-[Term]\n19610:id: PATO:0015009\n19611-name: humidity\n19612-def: \"A quality inhering in air by virtue of the partial pressure exerted by the bearer's water vapour content.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/90]\n19613-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19615-\n19616-[Term]\n19617:id: PATO:0015010\n19618-name: increased humidity\n19619-def: \"An increase in humidity.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/90]\n19620-subset: value_slim\n--\n19625-\n19626-[Term]\n19627:id: PATO:0015011\n19628-name: decreased humidity\n19629-def: \"An decrease in humidity.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/90]\n19630-subset: value_slim\n--\n19634-\n19635-[Term]\n19636:id: PATO:0015012\n19637-name: quality of a plasma\n19638-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's exhibiting the physical characteristics of an entity consisting of roughly equal proportions of positively and negatively charged particles, having neither a defined volume nor defined shape, having internal magnetic fields, and being electrically conductive.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/88]\n19639-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19641-\n19642-[Term]\n19643:id: PATO:0015013\n19644-name: degree of illumination\n19645-def: \"The degree to which the bearer is exposed to visible light.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/89]\n19646-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19648-\n19649-[Term]\n19650:id: PATO:0015014\n19651-name: increased degree of illumination\n19652-def: \"An increase in illumination.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/89]\n19653-subset: value_slim\n--\n19658-\n19659-[Term]\n19660:id: PATO:0015015\n19661-name: decreased degree of illumination\n19662-def: \"An decrease in illumination.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/89]\n19663-subset: value_slim\n--\n19667-\n19668-[Term]\n19669:id: PATO:0015016\n19670-name: stepped\n19671-def: \"Having a shape or form that resembles a step of a stairway (e.g., a ledge or offset margin).\" [http://www.thefreedictionary.com/stepped, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/82]\n19672-subset: value_slim\n--\n19674-\n19675-[Term]\n19676:id: PATO:0015017\n19677-name: quality of a colloid\n19678-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an entity by virtue of a portion of the bearer's molecular or polymolecular constituents present in one phase being dispersed in a portion of the bearer's constituents present in another phase.\" [ENVO:pb, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/91, https://goldbook.iupac.org/html/C/C01172.html]\n19679-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19681-\n19682-[Term]\n19683:id: PATO:0015018\n19684-name: quality of an aerosol\n19685-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an entity by virtue of the bearer's solid or liquid constituents being suspended in a gas.\" [ENVO:pb, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/91]\n19686-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19688-\n19689-[Term]\n19690:id: PATO:0015019\n19691-name: C-shaped\n19692-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of the letter C.\" [github:mah11, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/96]\n19693-subset: value_slim\n--\n19695-\n19696-[Term]\n19697:id: PATO:0015020\n19698-name: J-shaped\n19699-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of the letter J.\" [github:mah11, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/96]\n19700-subset: value_slim\n--\n19702-\n19703-[Term]\n19704:id: PATO:0015021\n19705-name: combustibility\n19706-def: \"The propensity of a material to undergo combustion. Combustion encompasses smouldering and flaming combustion. Combustibility is usually applied to solids.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combustibility, https://github.com/EnvironmentOntology/envo/issues/384]\n19707-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19709-\n19710-[Term]\n19711:id: PATO:0015022\n19712-name: increased combustibility\n19713-def: \"An increase in combustibility.\" []\n19714-subset: value_slim\n--\n19719-\n19720-[Term]\n19721:id: PATO:0015023\n19722-name: decreased combustibility\n19723-def: \"An decrease in combustibility.\" []\n19724-subset: value_slim\n--\n19729-\n19730-[Term]\n19731:id: PATO:0015024\n19732-name: increased porosity\n19733-def: \"An increase in porosity.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/110]\n19734-subset: value_slim\n--\n19737-\n19738-[Term]\n19739:id: PATO:0015025\n19740-name: decreased porosity\n19741-def: \"An decrease in porosity.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/110]\n19742-subset: value_slim\n--\n19746-\n19747-[Term]\n19748:id: PATO:0015026\n19749-name: stability\n19750-def: \"quality, state, or degree of being stable.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/113]\n19751-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19754-\n19755-[Term]\n19756:id: PATO:0015027\n19757-name: increased stability\n19758-def: \"An increase in stability.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/113]\n19759-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n19763-\n19764-[Term]\n19765:id: PATO:0015028\n19766-name: decreased stability\n19767-def: \"A decrease in stability.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/113]\n19768-subset: disposition_slim\n--\n19773-\n19774-[Term]\n19775:id: PATO:0015029\n19776-name: quality of a suspension\n19777-def: \"A physical quality inhering in an entity by virtue of the bearer's solid or liquid constituents being transiently dispersed in a solid, liquid, or gas before settling due to gravity or centrifugal forces.\" [ENVO:pb, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/91]\n19778-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19780-\n19781-[Term]\n19782:id: PATO:0015030\n19783-name: plume-shaped\n19784-def: \"A shape that ineres in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's mass being distributed in a feather-like fashion.\" [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/122]\n19785-subset: value_slim\n--\n19789-\n19790-[Term]\n19791:id: PATO:0015031\n19792-name: contamination\n19793-def: \"The presence of a constituent, impurity, or some other undesirable element that spoils, corrupts, infects, makes unfit, or makes inferior a material, physical body, natural environment, place of human occupancy, or other material entity.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contamination, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/420]\n19794-subset: attribute_slim\n--\n19797-\n19798-[Term]\n19799:id: PATO:0015032\n19800-name: increased contamination\n19801-def: \"An increase in contamination.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contamination, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/420]\n19802-subset: value_slim\n--\n19806-\n19807-[Term]\n19808:id: PATO:0015033\n19809-name: decreased contamination\n19810-def: \"A decrease in contamination.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contamination, https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/420]\n19811-subset: value_slim\n--\n19816-\n19817-[Term]\n19818:id: PATO:0020000\n19819-name: genotypic sex\n19820-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual based upon genotypic composition of sex chromosomes.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n19821-comment: Note that the chromosomal constitution of genotypic sex varies in different organisms. In human, we have XY, XX, though abnormal XXY, X0, XYY, and other combinations are possible.\n--\n19824-\n19825-[Term]\n19826:id: PATO:0020001\n19827-name: male genotypic sex\n19828-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual based upon genotypic composition that confers the capability for an organism to differentiate male gonads.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n19829-comment: Note that the chromosomal constitution of genotypic sex varies in different organisms. In human, this would be XY, though abnormal XXY and XYY would also result in a male phenotypic outcome.\n--\n19832-\n19833-[Term]\n19834:id: PATO:0020002\n19835-name: female genotypic sex\n19836-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population based upon genotypic composition that confers the capability for an organism to differentiate female gonads.\" [PATOC:MAH]\n19837-comment: Note that the chromosomal constitution of genotypic sex varies in different organisms. In human, this would be XX, though abnormal X0 and XXX would also result in a female phenotypic outcome.\n--\n19840-\n19841-[Term]\n19842:id: PATO:0025000\n19843-name: potability\n19844-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to being fit to be used as a safe means of hydration.\" [Wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drinking_water]\n19845-synonym: \"drinkability\" EXACT []\n--\n19849-\n19850-[Term]\n19851:id: PATO:0025001\n19852-name: non-potable\n19853-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer not being suitable for use as a safe means of hydration.\" [Wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drinking_water]\n19854-synonym: \"undrinkable\" EXACT []\n--\n19860-\n19861-[Term]\n19862:id: PATO:0025002\n19863-name: potable\n19864-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being suitable for use as a safe means of hydration.\" [Wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drinking_water]\n19865-synonym: \"drinkable\" EXACT []\n--\n19870-\n19871-[Term]\n19872:id: PATO:0030000\n19873-name: anteriorized\n19874-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally anterior structures and missing some or all of what are normally posterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19875-synonym: \"anterioralized\" EXACT []\n--\n19878-\n19879-[Term]\n19880:id: PATO:0030001\n19881-name: dorsalized\n19882-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally dorsal structures and missing some or all of what are normally ventral structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19883-is_a: PATO:0000646 ! malformed\n--\n19885-\n19886-[Term]\n19887:id: PATO:0030002\n19888-name: posteriorized\n19889-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally posterior structures and missing some or all of what are normally anterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19890-synonym: \"posterioralized\" EXACT []\n--\n19893-\n19894-[Term]\n19895:id: PATO:0030003\n19896-name: ventralized\n19897-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally ventral structures and missing some or all of what are normally dorsal structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19898-is_a: PATO:0000646 ! malformed\n--\n19900-\n19901-[Term]\n19902:id: PATO:0030004\n19903-name: partially anteriorized\n19904-def: \"An anteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally anterior structures and missing some but not all of what are normally posterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19905-synonym: \"partially anterioralized\" EXACT []\n--\n19908-\n19909-[Term]\n19910:id: PATO:0030005\n19911-name: partially dorsalized\n19912-def: \"A dorsalized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally dorsal structures and missing some but not all of what are normally ventral structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19913-is_a: PATO:0030001 ! dorsalized\n--\n19915-\n19916-[Term]\n19917:id: PATO:0030006\n19918-name: partially posteriorized\n19919-def: \"A posteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally posterior structures and missing some but not all of what are normally anterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19920-synonym: \"partially posterioralized\" EXACT []\n--\n19923-\n19924-[Term]\n19925:id: PATO:0030007\n19926-name: partially ventralized\n19927-def: \"A ventralized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally ventral structures and missing some but not all of what are normally dorsal structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19928-is_a: PATO:0030003 ! ventralized\n--\n19930-\n19931-[Term]\n19932:id: PATO:0030008\n19933-name: dorso-anteriorized\n19934-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally dorso-anterior structures and missing some or all of what are normally ventro-posterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19935-is_a: PATO:0000646 ! malformed\n--\n19937-\n19938-[Term]\n19939:id: PATO:0030009\n19940-name: partially dorso-anteriorized\n19941-def: \"A dorso-anteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally dorso-anterior structures and missing some but not all of what are normally ventro-posterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19942-is_a: PATO:0030008 ! dorso-anteriorized\n--\n19944-\n19945-[Term]\n19946:id: PATO:0030010\n19947-name: wholly dorso-anteriorized\n19948-def: \"A dorso-anteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally dorso-anterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19949-is_a: PATO:0030008 ! dorso-anteriorized\n--\n19951-\n19952-[Term]\n19953:id: PATO:0030011\n19954-name: ventro-posteriorized\n19955-def: \"A malformed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally ventro-posterior structures and missing some or all of what are normally dorso-anterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19956-is_a: PATO:0000646 ! malformed\n--\n19958-\n19959-[Term]\n19960:id: PATO:0030012\n19961-name: partially ventro-posteriorized\n19962-def: \"A ventro-posteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing what are normally ventro-posterior structures and missing some but not all of what are normally dorso-anterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19963-is_a: PATO:0030011 ! ventro-posteriorized\n--\n19965-\n19966-[Term]\n19967:id: PATO:0030013\n19968-name: wholly ventro-posteriorized\n19969-def: \"A ventro-posteriorized quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's gross morphology containing only what are normally ventro-posterior structures.\" [PATOC:EJS]\n19970-is_a: PATO:0030011 ! ventro-posteriorized\n--\n19972-\n19973-[Term]\n19974:id: PATO:0040000\n19975-name: heterotaxic\n19976-def: \"An oriented quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being abnormally placed or arranged.\" [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/heterotaxic]\n19977-is_a: PATO:0000625 ! inverted\n--\n19980-\n19981-[Term]\n19982:id: PATO:0040001\n19983-name: obsolete ring-shaped\n19984-is_obsolete: true\n19985-replaced_by: PATO:0002539\n19986-\n19987-[Term]\n19988:id: PATO:0040002\n19989-name: position originates from\n19990-def: \"A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of some aspect of that bearer beginning from a position on another entity.\" []\n19991-comment: Original label \"originates from\" changed to current label to differentiate that this term is a positional quality rather than one that connects between an entity and another entity it originates from.\n--\n19996-\n19997-[Term]\n19998:id: PATO:0040003\n19999-name: pathogenicity\n20000-def: \"The ability of a pathogen to produce an infectious disease or disorder in an another organism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8941-3984]\n20001-is_a: PATO:0001995 ! organismal quality\n--\n20004-\n20005-[Term]\n20006:id: PATO:0040004\n20007-name: plush\n20008-def: \"A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being covered or partially covered with hair that has increased thickness and softness.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n20009-is_a: PATO:0000150 ! texture\n--\n20012-\n20013-[Term]\n20014:id: PATO:0040005\n20015-name: posteroventral orientation\n20016-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed posteroventrally.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20017-synonym: \"posteroventrally oriented\" EXACT []\n--\n20021-\n20022-[Term]\n20023:id: PATO:0040006\n20024-name: crown like\n20025-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape like a crown.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20026-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n--\n20029-\n20030-[Term]\n20031:id: PATO:0040007\n20032-name: shell shaped\n20033-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a shape like a shell.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20034-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n--\n20037-\n20038-[Term]\n20039:id: PATO:0040008\n20040-name: fringed\n20041-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having an ornamental border consisting of short straight or twisted threads or strips hanging from cut or raveled edges or from a separate band.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/fringe]\n20042-is_a: PATO:0002267 ! edge shape\n--\n20045-\n20046-[Term]\n20047:id: PATO:0040009\n20048-name: bowl shaped\n20049-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped in the form of a bowl.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20050-is_a: PATO:0002008 ! concave 3-D shape\n--\n20053-\n20054-[Term]\n20055:id: PATO:0040010\n20056-name: mobile relative to\n20057-def: \"Mobility relative to a second entity.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20058-comment: For example, distinct anteroposterior mobility of palatine relative to mesethmoid.\n--\n20062-\n20063-[Term]\n20064:id: PATO:0040011\n20065-name: immobile relative to\n20066-def: \"Immobility relative to a second entity.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20067-comment: For example: distinct anteroposterior immobility of palatine relative to mesethmoid.\n--\n20071-\n20072-[Term]\n20073:id: PATO:0040012\n20074-name: plug shaped\n20075-def: \"A shape that is in the form of a plug, being tube-like and expanded on one end.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20076-synonym: \"plug like\" EXACT []\n--\n20080-\n20081-[Term]\n20082:id: PATO:0040013\n20083-name: dorsomedial orientation\n20084-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed dorsomedially.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20085-synonym: \"dorsomedially directed\" EXACT []\n--\n20089-\n20090-[Term]\n20091:id: PATO:0040014\n20092-name: band shaped\n20093-def: \"A shape that is in the form of a narrow strip encircling an object.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/band]\n20094-synonym: \"band like\" EXACT []\n--\n20101-\n20102-[Term]\n20103:id: PATO:0040015\n20104-name: trough shaped\n20105-def: \"A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's shape resembling that of a trough, being narrow, long, and boxlike in shape.\" [http://www.dictionary.com/browse/trough, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20106-synonym: \"trough like\" EXACT []\n--\n20112-\n20113-[Term]\n20114:id: PATO:0040016\n20115-name: pentagonal\n20116-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having five angles and five sides.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/pentagonal]\n20117-is_a: PATO:0002006 ! 2-D shape\n--\n20120-\n20121-[Term]\n20122:id: PATO:0040017\n20123-name: dysplastic growth\n20124-def: \"A growth quality of occurrent in which the growth of an organism, structure or group of organisms is abnormal.\" [https://www.cancer.gov/publications/dictionaries/cancer-terms/def/dysplasia]\n20125-synonym: \"dysgenesis\" NARROW []\n--\n20129-\n20130-[Term]\n20131:id: PATO:0040019\n20132-name: fibrotic\n20133-def: \"Fibrosis is the formation of excess fibrous connective tissue in an organ or tissue in a reparative or reactive process.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrosis]\n20134-is_a: PATO:0000025 ! composition\n--\n20137-\n20138-[Term]\n20139:id: PATO:0040020\n20140-name: spayed female\n20141-def: \"Female quality of being incapable to reproduce because of functional loss of the ovaries and/or uterus from surgical removal.\" []\n20142-is_a: PATO:0000383 ! female\n--\n20145-\n20146-[Term]\n20147:id: PATO:0040021\n20148-name: unpaired\n20149-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part n=1 of the indicated entity type, where n is bilaterally paired for a comparable organism..\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20150-is_a: PATO:0000467 ! present\n--\n20152-\n20153-[Term]\n20154:id: PATO:0040022\n20155-name: flared\n20156-def: \"A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being expanded laterally and or opened outward in shape.\" []\n20157-is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape\n--\n20160-\n20161-[Term]\n20162:id: PATO:0040023\n20163-name: distomedial orientation\n20164-def: \"An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having a position that is directed distomedially, ie, pertaining to an inside aspect, but also farther away from the center of the body.\" [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distomedial]\n20165-synonym: \"disto-medial orientation\" EXACT []\n--\n20170-\n20171-[Term]\n20172:id: PATO:0040024\n20173-name: bilaterally paired\n20174-def: \"The bearer of this quality has_part n=2 of the indicated entity type, where n is unpaired for a comparable organism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3162-7490]\n20175-synonym: \"paired\" BROAD []\n--\n20178-\n20179-[Term]\n20180:id: PATO:0040025\n20181-name: lesioned\n20182-def: \"A structural quality which is held by a bearer where a localized pathological or traumatic structural change, damage, deformity, or discontinuity of tissue, organ, or body part is present.\" [NCIT:C3824]\n20183-is_a: PATO:0000141 ! structure\n--\n20185-\n20186-[Term]\n20187:id: PATO:0040026\n20188-name: structurally discontinuous\n20189-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked by interruptions or gaps.\" []\n20190-comment: This term is intended for use for terms such as MP:0010461 discontinuous pulmonary artery and MP:0004157 interrupted aortic arch.\n--\n20194-\n20195-[Term]\n20196:id: PATO:0040027\n20197-name: doubled haploid\n20198-def: \"A ploidy quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's haploid cells undergo chromosome doubling.\" [Wikipedia:https\\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doubled_haploidy]\n20199-synonym: \"double haploid\" EXACT []\n--\n20203-\n20204-[Term]\n20205:id: PATO:0040028\n20206-name: parous\n20207-def: \"An organismal quality of having successfully reproduced.\" [EFO:0002947]\n20208-is_a: PATO:0001434 ! reproductive quality\n--\n20210-\n20211-[Term]\n20212:id: PATO:0040029\n20213-name: shaded\n20214-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of that bearer being shielded from visible light.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4366-3088]\n20215-comment: Shaded does not refer to radiation more generally, as this would be more shielded than shaded.\n--\n20218-\n20219-[Term]\n20220:id: PATO:0040030\n20221-name: decreased width and length\n20222-def: \"A width and length quality which is relatively small, where both width and length are decreased.\" []\n20223-subset: value_slim\n--\n20228-\n20229-[Term]\n20230:id: PATO:0040031\n20231-name: increased width and length\n20232-def: \"A width and length quality that is relatively large, where both width and length are increased.\" []\n20233-subset: value_slim\n--\n20238-\n20239-[Term]\n20240:id: PATO:0040032\n20241-name: increased linear velocity\n20242-def: \"A distance traveled in a specific time that is relatively high.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2244-7917]\n20243-is_a: PATO:0002304 ! increased process quality\n--\n20245-\n20246-[Term]\n20247:id: PATO:0040033\n20248-name: decreased linear velocity\n20249-def: \"A distance traveled in a specific time that is relatively low.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2244-7917]\n20250-is_a: PATO:0002302 ! decreased process quality\n--\n20252-\n20253-[Term]\n20254:id: PATO:0040034\n20255-name: fractured\n20256-def: \"A broken quality where an entity is cracked or broken, usually a bone.\" [https://medlineplus.gov/fractures.html]\n20257-is_a: PATO:0001444 ! broken\n--\n20259-\n20260-[Term]\n20261:id: PATO:0040035\n20262-name: transversely fractured\n20263-def: \"A fractured quality where the fracture traverses the bone perpendicular to the axis of the bone.\" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/transverse-fracture?lang=us]\n20264-synonym: \"fractured, transverse\" EXACT []\n--\n20267-\n20268-[Term]\n20269:id: PATO:0040036\n20270-name: impact-fractured\n20271-def: \"A fractured quality in which one of the fragments is driven into another fragment.\" [https://www.dictionary.com/browse/impacted-fracture]\n20272-synonym: \"fractured, impacted\" EXACT []\n--\n20276-\n20277-[Term]\n20278:id: PATO:0040037\n20279-name: linearly fractured\n20280-def: \"A fractured quality where the fracture runs parallel to the long axis of a bone.\" [https://www.dictionary.com/browse/linear-fracture]\n20281-synonym: \"fractured, linear\" EXACT []\n--\n20284-\n20285-[Term]\n20286:id: PATO:0040038\n20287-name: obliquely fractured\n20288-def: \"A fractured quality where the fracture occurs at a plane oblique to the long axis of the bone.\" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/oblique-fracture?lang=us]\n20289-synonym: \"fractured, oblique\" EXACT []\n--\n20292-\n20293-[Term]\n20294:id: PATO:0040039\n20295-name: spirally fractured\n20296-def: \"A fractured quality that occurs when torque (a rotating force) is applied along the axis of a bone.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spiral_fracture]\n20297-synonym: \"fractured, spiral\" EXACT []\n--\n20301-\n20302-[Term]\n20303:id: PATO:0040040\n20304-name: compression-fractured\n20305-def: \"A fractured quality that is caused by a loss of bone mass (osteoporosis) that occurs as part of aging.\" [https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/osteoporosis/multimedia/compression-fractures/img-20008995]\n20306-synonym: \"compression fractured\" EXACT []\n--\n20312-\n20313-[Term]\n20314:id: PATO:0040041\n20315-name: avulsion fractured\n20316-def: \"A fractured quality in which the fragment of bone tears away from the main mass of bone as a result of physical trauma.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avulsion_fracture]\n20317-synonym: \"fractured, avulsion\" EXACT []\n--\n20320-\n20321-[Term]\n20322:id: PATO:0040042\n20323-name: decreased ratio\n20324-def: \"A decreased quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's decreased magnitude in proportion to the magnitude of another entity.\" [] {terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140\", terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"}\n20325-comment: Example: decreased proportion of CD4 T cells relative to total T cells.\n--\n20334-\n20335-[Term]\n20336:id: PATO:0040043\n20337-name: increased ratio\n20338-def: \"An increased quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's increased magnitude in proportion to the magnitude of another entity.\" [] {terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140\", terms:contributor=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"}\n20339-comment: Example: increased proportion of CD4 T cells relative to total T cells.\n--\n20348-\n20349-[Term]\n20350:id: PATO:0040044\n20351-name: ruptured\n20352-def: \"A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's components being torn, typically used for soft tissues or membranes.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n20353-synonym: \"burst\" EXACT []\n--\n20356-\n20357-[Term]\n20358:id: PATO:0040045\n20359-name: population growth rate\n20360-def: \"The rate or speed of the change in in number of a population.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9900-7880, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n20361-is_a: PATO:0001492 ! growth rate\n--\n20364-\n20365-[Term]\n20366:id: PATO:0040046\n20367-name: single organismal growth rate\n20368-def: \"The rate or speed of the change in size of an individual entity.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9900-7880, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597]\n20369-is_a: PATO:0002487 ! single organismal process quality\n--\n20371-\n20372-[Term]\n20373:id: PATO:0040047\n20374-name: fragmented\n20375-def: \"Existing or functioning as though broken into separate parts; disorganized; disunified.\" [https://www.dictionary.com/browse/unfragmented]\n20376-comment: Moved to a child of wholeness because broken implies a trauma and fragmented could be caused by a developmental process. See HP:0100168 Fragmented epiphyses as an example.\n--\n20379-\n20380-[Term]\n20381:id: PATO:0040048\n20382-name: erythematous\n20383-def: \"Red due to increase blood circulation in a defined area.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]\n20384-synonym: \"erythema\" EXACT []\n--\n20388-\n20389-[Term]\n20390:id: PATO:0040049\n20391-name: male with DSD\n20392-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population who are otherwise male of a non-hermaphroditic species who has ambiguous or atypical congenital development of the reproductive system.\" []\n20393-comment: The term intersex is popular in use, but may be considered offensive when applied to humans. DSD can be expanded multiple ways to 'disorders/differences of sexual development/differentiation'.\n--\n20401-\n20402-[Term]\n20403:id: PATO:0040050\n20404-name: diandrous\n20405-def: \"A phenotypic sex quality inhering in a  plant organism or a population of plants in which the flowers have two stamens.\" [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2908-3327] {comment=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8815-0078\"}\n20406-is_a: PATO:0001894 ! phenotypic sex\n--\n20408-\n20409-[Term]\n20410:id: PATO:0040051\n20411-name: monandrous\n20412-def: \"A phenotypic sex quality inhering in a  plant organism or a population of plants in which the flowers have only one stamen.\" [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2908-3327, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8815-0078]\n20413-is_a: PATO:0001894 ! phenotypic sex\n--\n20415-\n20416-[Term]\n20417:id: PATO:0040052\n20418-name: protogynous\n20419-def: \"A sequential hermaphroditic quality whereby organisms start out as female and change to male at a later life stage.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism] {comment=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2908-3327\"}\n20420-synonym: \"protogyny\" EXACT []\n--\n20423-\n20424-[Term]\n20425:id: PATO:0040053\n20426-name: protandrous\n20427-def: \"A sequential hermaphroditic quality whereby organisms start out as male and change to female at a later life stage.\" [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2908-3327, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism]\n20428-synonym: \"protandry\" EXACT []\n--\n20431-\n20432-[Term]\n20433:id: PATO:0040054\n20434-name: protogynous hermaphroditism\n20435-def: \"A protogynous quality whereby organisms start out as female and change to hermaphrodite at a later life stage.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism]\n20436-synonym: \"protogynous hermaphrodite\" EXACT []\n--\n20440-\n20441-[Term]\n20442:id: PATO:0040055\n20443-name: protandrous hermaphroditism\n20444-def: \"A protandrous quality whereby organisms start out as male and change to hermaphrodite at a later life stage.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism]\n20445-synonym: \"protandrous hermaphrodite\" EXACT []\n--\n20449-\n20450-[Term]\n20451:id: PATO:0040056\n20452-name: female with DSD\n20453-def: \"A biological sex quality inhering in an individual or a population who are otherwise female of a non-hermaphroditic species who has ambiguous or atypical congenital development of the reproductive system.\" []\n20454-comment: The term intersex is popular in use, but may be considered offensive when applied to humans. DSD can be expanded multiple ways to 'disorders/differences of sexual development/differentiation'.\n--\n20462-\n20463-[Term]\n20464:id: PATO:0040057\n20465-name: population process quality\n20466-def: \"A quality inhering in a process by virtue of that process having a population or part of a population, where population is defined as a collection of individuals from the same taxonomic class distinguished by one or more characteristics, as participants.\" [https://www.alliancegenome.org/glossary]\n20467-is_a: PATO:0001236 ! process quality\n--\n20469-\n20470-[Term]\n20471:id: PATO:0040058\n20472-name: absence of physical object\n20473-def: \"A quality denoting the lack of a physical entity or object, such as a chemical.\" [thefreedictionary.:thefreedictionary.]\n20474-subset: absent_slim\n--\n20478-\n20479-[Term]\n20480:id: PATO:0040059\n20481-name: absent process\n20482-def: \"A quality denoting the lack of a process or function.\" []\n20483-subset: absent_slim\n--\n20488-\n20489-[Term]\n20490:id: PATO:0040060\n20491-name: absence of anatomical entity\n20492-def: \"A quality denoting the lack of an anatomical entity or cellular component.\" [thefreedictionary.:thefreedictionary.]\n20493-comment: Absence of anatomical entity should only be used when all of the entity is absent. For example, absent teeth would mean all teeth are absent not some teeth are absent.\n--\n20499-\n20500-[Term]\n20501:id: PATO:0040070\n20502-name: thermoplastic\n20503-def: \"A physical quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to deform by heating.\" [http://www.gesamp.org/publications/guidelines-for-the-monitoring-and-assessment-of-plastic-litter-in-the-ocean, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8166-0486]\n20504-is_a: PATO:0001018 ! physical quality\n--\n20509-\n20510-[Term]\n20511:id: PATO:0040071\n20512-name: nuclear/cytoplasmic ratio\n20513-def: \"A quality inhering in a cell by virtue of the ratio between the volume of its nucleus and the volume of its cytoplasm.\" [Wikipedia:NC_ratio&oldid=931936284]\n20514-synonym: \"N:C ratio\" EXACT []\n--\n20517-\n20518-[Term]\n20519:id: PATO:0040072\n20520-name: high nuclear/cytoplasmic ratio\n20521-def: \"A quality inhering in a cell by virtue of the cell having a high nuclear/cytoplasmic ratio.\" [http://lymerick.net/blood-cells.pdf, Wikipedia:NC_ratio&oldid=931936284]\n20522-comment: A high nuclear/cytolasmic ratio is 70% or higher.\n--\n20526-\n20527-[Term]\n20528:id: PATO:0045000\n20529-name: normal rate\n20530-def: \"A rate which is relatively normal.\" []\n20531-subset: mpath_slim\n--\n20535-\n20536-[Term]\n20537:id: PATO:0045001\n20538-name: normal object quality\n20539-def: \"A quality of an object that has a value that is normal or average.\" []\n20540-is_a: PATO:0001241 ! physical object quality\n--\n20544-\n20545-[Term]\n20546:id: PATO:0045002\n20547-name: normal acidity\n20548-