nt.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005006 \"ionocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005006 obo:CL_0000066)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005007 (Kolmer-Agduhr neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18680739\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005007 \"Kolmer-Agduhr neurons are ciliated GABAergic neurons that contact the central canal of the spinal cord and have ipsilateral ascending axons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005007 \"KA cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15539490\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005007 \"KA interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9634146\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005007 \"KA neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005007 \"Kolmer-Agduhr cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005007 \"Kolmer-Agduhr neuron\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005007 obo:CL_0000617)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005007 obo:CL_0005000)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005008 (macular hair cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:cvs\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005008 \"An auditory hair cell located in the macula that is sensitive to auditory stimuli.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005008 \"macular hair cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0005008 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000202 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000054)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005008 obo:CL_0000202)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005009 (renal principal cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005009 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney which regulates sodium and potassium balance. The activity of sodium and potassium channels on the apical membrane of the cell is regulated by aldosterone and vasopressin. In mammals this cell type is located in the renal collecting duct system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005009 \"renal principal cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005009 obo:CL_0000075)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005009 obo:CL_0002518)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005010 (renal intercalated cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005010 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney that regulates acid/base balance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0005010 \"FMA:86560\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005010 \"intercalated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25632105\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0005010 \"Intercalated cells are also called “mitochondria-rich cells”, reflecting the high levels of round mitochondria at their apical pole, or in their cytoplasm, a distribution that is quite different from that of other kidney tubule cells, which accumulated mitochondria around the basolateral membrane. These cells also have numerous irregular apical microvilli compared with the surrounding segment-specific cells. Intercalated cells lack a central cilium, at least in the cortex, which also differentiates them from the adjacent principal cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005010 \"renal intercalated cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005010 obo:CL_0000075)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005010 obo:CL_0002078)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005010 obo:CL_0002518)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001285))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005011 (renal alpha-intercalated cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005011 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney which secretes acid and reabsorbs base to regulate acid/base balance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25632105\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005011 \"type A intercalated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25632105\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005011 \"type A-IC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25632105\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0005011 \"Type A intercalated cells are the more abundant type of intercalated cell in the outer stripe of the outer medulla in most mammalian species.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005011 \"renal alpha-intercalated cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005011 obo:CL_0005010)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005011 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046717))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005012 (multiciliated epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28400610\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38032388\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005012 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell with multiple motile cilia on its apical surface. These cells facilitate the movement of liquids such as mucus or cerebrospinal fluid across the epithelial surface.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0005012 \"multi-ciliated cell\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0005012 \"multiciliated cell\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005012 \"multi-ciliated epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005012 \"multiciliated epithelial cell\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0005012 \"MCC\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22118931\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23959957\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25729351\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26378583\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0005012 \"While the term 'multi-ciliated epithelial cell' refers to cells with multiple motile cilia, there are exceptions where epithelial cells may have multiple non-motile cilia. Examples include olfactory sensory neurons, which have non-motile cilia for sensory detection, and choroid plexus epithelial cells, which possess multiple non-motile cilia with transient motility during development. Multiciliated cells are essential for human health, and their dysfunction can lead to various diseases known as ciliopathies, such as primary ciliary dyskinesia. This condition affects the respiratory system, brain ventricles, and reproductive system, leading to chronic respiratory infections, hydrocephalus, and infertility\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005012 \"multiciliated epithelial cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0005012 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0031514) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0010007)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005013 (single ciliated epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005013 \"A ciliated epithelial cell with a single cilium.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005013 \"single ciliated epithelial cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005013 obo:CL_0000066)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005929))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005014 (auditory epithelial supporting cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005014 \"A non-sensory cell that extends from the basement membrane to the apical surface of the auditory epithelium and provides support for auditory hair cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005014 \"auditory epithelial support cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005014 \"auditory epithelial supporting cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005014 obo:CL_0000630)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005014 obo:CL_0000710)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005014 obo:CL_0002491)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005015 (inner phalangeal cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005015 \"An auditory epithelial support cell that surrounds the nerve fibers and synapses of the auditory inner hair cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0005015 \"FMA:79801\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005015 \"inner phalangeal cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0005015 obo:CL_0002165)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0005016 (obsolete apical cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"TAIR:TB\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005016 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0030007 from Plant Ontology instead. The apical cell is the upper cell formed after the first division of a plant zygote.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
